Eighth Canto\line }{\cf7\insrsid4605116 Withdrawal of the Cosmic Creations
\par }\pard\plain \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat7 \f43\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\fs28\cf13\insrsid4605116  \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam Canto 8: "Withdrawal of the Cosmic Creations"}{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain 
\s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat7 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.1.1 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it said: O my lord, my spiritual master, now I have fully heard from Your Grace about the dynasty of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu. But there are also other Manus, and I want to hear about their dynasties. Kindly describe them to us.

\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.2 - O learned br\'e4hma\'eba, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, the great learned persons who are completely intelligent describe the activities and appearance of 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead during the various manvantaras. We are very eager to hear about these narrations. Kindly describe them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.3 - O learned br\'e4hma\'eba, kindly describe to us whatever activities the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who cre
ated this cosmic manifestation, has performed in the past manvantaras, is performing at present, and will perform in the future manvantaras.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.4 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: In the present kalpa there have already been six Manus. I have described to you Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu and the appearance of many demigods. In this kalpa of Brahm\'e4, Sv\'e4
yambhuva is the first Manu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.5 - Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu had two daughters, named \'c4k\'fcti and Devah\'fcti. From their wombs, the Supreme Personality of Godhead appeared as two sons named Yaj\'efam\'fc
rti and Kapila respectively. These sons were entrusted with preaching about religion and knowledge.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.6 - O best of the Kurus, I have already described [in the Third Canto] the activities of Kapila, the son of Devah\'fcti. Now I shall describe the activities of Yaj\'efapati, the son of \'c4k\'fcti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.7 - Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, the husband of \'c7atar\'fcp\'e4, was by nature not at all attached to enjoyment of the senses. Thus he gave up his kingdom of sense enjoyment and entered the forest with his wife to
 practice austerities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.8 - O scion of Bharata, after Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu had thus entered the forest with his wife, he stood on one leg on the bank of the River Sunand\'e4
, and in this way, with only one leg touching the earth, he performed great austerities for one hundred years. While performing these austerities, he spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.9 - Lord Manu said: The supreme living being has created this material world of animation; it is not that He was created by this material world. When everything is
 silent, the Supreme Being stays awake as a witness. The living entity does not know Him, but He knows everything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.10 - Within this universe, the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His Supersoul feature is present everywhere, wherever there are anim
ate or inanimate beings. Therefore, one should accept only that which is allotted to him; one should not desire to infringe upon the property of others.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.11 - Although the Supreme Personality of Godhead constantly watches the activities of the world
, no one sees Him. However, one should not think that because no one sees Him, He does not see, for His power to see is never diminished. Therefore, everyone should worship the Supersoul, who always stays with the individual soul as a friend.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.12 - 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead has no beginning, no end and no middle. Nor does He belong to a particular person or nation. He has no inside or outside. The dualities found within this material world, such as beginning and end, mine and theirs, are al
l absent from the personality of the Supreme Lord. The universe, which emanates from Him, is another feature of the Lord. Therefore the Supreme Lord is the ultimate truth, and He is complete in greatness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.13 - The entire cosmic manifestation is the 
body of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Absolute Truth, who has millions of names and unlimited potencies. He is self-effulgent, unborn and changeless. He is the beginning of everything, but He has no beginning. Because He has created this cosmic 
manifestation by His external energy, the universe appears to be created, maintained and annihilated by Him. Nonetheless, He remains inactive in His spiritual energy and is untouched by the activities of the material energy.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.14 - Therefore, to enabl
e people to reach the stage of activities that are not tinged by fruitive results, great saints first engage people in fruitive activities, for unless one begins by performing activities as recommended in the \'e7\'e4
stras, one cannot reach the stage of liberation, or activities that produce no reactions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.15 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is full in opulence by His own gain, yet He acts as the creator, maintainer and annihilator of this material world. In spite of acting in that way, He is never ent
angled. Hence devotees who follow in His footsteps are also never entangled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.16 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, works just like an ordinary human being, yet He does not desire to enjoy the fruits of work. He is full in knowledge, free 
from material desires and diversions, and completely independent. As the supreme teacher of human society, He teaches His own way of activities, and thus He inaugurates the real path of religion. I request everyone to follow Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.17 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu was thus in a trance, chanting the mantras of Vedic instruction known as the Upani\'f1ads. Upon seeing him, the R\'e4k\'f1
asas and asuras, being very hungry, wanted to devour him. Therefore they ran after him with great speed.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.18 - The Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu, who sits in everyone's heart, appearing as Yaj\'efapati, observed that the R\'e4k\'f1asas and demons were going to devour Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu. Thus the Lord, accompanied by His sons named the Y\'e4mas and by all the other demigods, killed the demons and R\'e4k\'f1asas. He then took the post of Indra and began to rule the heavenly kingdom.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.19 - The son of Agni named Sv\'e4roci\'f1a became the second Manu. His several sons were headed by Dyumat, Su\'f1e\'eba and Roci\'f1mat.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.20 - During the reign of Sv\'e4roci\'f1a, the post of Indra was assumed by Rocana, the son of Yaj\'efa. Tu\'f1ita and others became the principal demigods, and \'dc
rja, Stambha and others became the seven saints. All of them were faithful devotees of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.21 - Veda\'e7ir\'e4 was a very celebrated \'e5\'f1i. From the womb of his wife, whose name was Tu\'f1it\'e4, came the avat\'e4ra named Vibhu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.22 - Vibhu remained a brahmac\'e4ri and never married throughout his life. From him, eighty-eight thousand other saintly persons took lessons on self-control, austerity and similar behavior.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.23 - O King, the third Manu, Uttama, was the son of King Priyavrata. Among the sons of this Manu were Pavana, S\'e5\'efjaya and Yaj\'efahotra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.24 - During the reign of the third Manu, Pramada and other sons of Vasi\'f1\'f6ha became the seven sages. The Satyas, Veda\'e7rutas and Bhadras became demigods, and Satyajit was selected to be Indra, the King of heaven.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.25 - In this manvantara, the Supreme Personality of Godhead appeared from the womb of S\'fcn\'e5t\'e4, who was the 
wife of Dharma, the demigod in charge of religion. The Lord was celebrated as Satyasena, and He appeared with other demigods, known as the Satyavratas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.26 - Satyasena, along with His friend Satyajit, who was the King of heaven, Indra, killed all the untruthful, impious and misbehaved Yak\'f1as, R\'e4k\'f1
asas and ghostly living entities, who gave pains to other living beings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.27 - The brother of the third Manu, Uttama, was celebrated by the name T\'e4masa, and he became the fourth Manu. T\'e4masa had ten sons, headed by P\'e5thu, Khy\'e4ti, Nara and Ketu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.28 - During the reign of T\'e4masa Manu, among the demigods were the Satyakas, Haris and V\'e9ras. The heavenly King, Indra, was Tri\'e7ikha. The sages in saptar\'f1i-dh\'e4ma were headed by Jyotirdh\'e4ma.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.29 - O King, in the T\'e4masa manvantara the sons of Vidh\'e5ti, who were known as the Vaidh\'e5
tis, also became demigods. Since in course of time the Vedic authority was lost, these demigods, by their own powers, protected the Vedic authority.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.30 - Also in this manvantara, the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu, took birth from the womb of Hari\'eb\'e9, the wife of Harimedh\'e4
, and He was known as Hari. Hari saved His devotee Gajendra, the King of the elephants, from the mouth of a crocodile.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.31 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it said: My lord, B\'e4dar\'e4ya\'ebi, we wish to hear from you in detail how the King of the elephants, when attacked by a crocodile, was delivered by Hari.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.32 - Any literature or narration in which the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Uttama\'e7loka, is described and glorified is certainly great, pure, glorious, auspicious and all good.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.1.33 - \'c7r\'e9 S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O br\'e4hma\'ebas, when Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who was awaiting impending death, thus requested \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 to speak, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, encouraged by the King's words, offered respect to the King and spoke with great pleasure in the assembly of sages, who desired to hear him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\fs28\cf13\insrsid4605116 
