{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When the Lord delivered Gajendra, King of the elephants, all the demigods, sages and Gandharvas, headed by Brahm\'e4 and \'c7
iva, praised this activity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and showered flowers upon both the Lord and Gajendra.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.2 - There was a beating of kettledrums in the heavenly planets, the inhabitants of Gandharvaloka began to dance and sing, while great sages and the inhabitants of C\'e4ra\'eb
aloka and Siddhaloka offered prayers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Puru\'f1ottama.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.3-4 - The best of the Gandharvas, King H\'fch\'fc, having been cursed by Devala Muni, 
had become a crocodile. Now, having been delivered by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he assumed a very beautiful form as a Gandharva. Understanding by whose mercy this had happened, he immediately offered his respectful obeisances with his head and b
egan chanting prayers just suitable for the transcendental Lord, the supreme eternal, who is worshiped by the choicest verses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.5 - Having been favored by the causeless mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and having regained his original form, King H\'fch\'fc
 circumambulated the Lord and offered his obeisances. Then, in the presence of all the demigods, headed by Brahm\'e4, he returned to Gandharvaloka. He had been freed of all sinful reactions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.6 - Because Gajendra, King of the elephants, had been touched directly by the hands of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he was immediately freed of all material ignorance and bondage. Thus he received the salvation of s
\'e4r\'fcpya-mukti, in which he achieved the same bodily features as the Lord, being dressed in yellow garments and possessing four hands.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.7 - This Gajendra had formerly been a Vai\'f1\'ebava and the king of the country known as P\'e4\'eb\'f2ya, which is in the province of Dravi\'f2a [South India]. In his previous life, he was known as Indradyumna Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.8 - Indradyumna Mah\'e4r\'e4ja retired from family life and went to the Malaya Hills, where he had a small cottage for his \'e4\'e7
rama. He wore matted locks on his head and always engaged in austerities. Once, while observing a vow of silence, he was fully engaged in the worship of the Lord and absorbed in the ecstasy of love of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.9 - While Indradyumna Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was engaged in ecstatic meditation, worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the great sage Agastya Muni arrived there, surrounded by his disciples. When the Muni saw that Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja Indradyumna, who was sitting in a secluded place, remained silent and did not follow the etiquette of offering him a reception, he was very angry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.10 - Agastya Muni then spoke this curse against the King: This King Indradyumna is not at all gentle. Being low and uneducated, he has insulted a br\'e4hma\'eb
a. May he therefore enter the region of darkness and receive the dull, dumb body of an elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.11-12 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear
 King, after Agastya Muni had thus cursed King Indradyumna, the Muni left that place along with his disciples. Since the King was a devotee, he accepted Agastya Muni's curse as welcome because it was the desire of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. There
fore, although in his next life he got the body of an elephant, because of devotional service he remembered how to worship and offer prayers to the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.13 - Upon delivering the King of the elephants from the clutches of the crocodile, and from material existence, which resembles a crocodile, the Lord awarded him the status of s\'e4r\'fc
pya-mukti. In the presence of the Gandharvas, the Siddhas and the other demigods, who were praising the Lord for His wonderful transcendental activities, the Lord, sitting on the back of His carrier, Garu\'f2
a, returned to His all-wonderful abode and took Gajendra with Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.14 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, I have now described the wonderful power of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, as displayed when the Lord delivered the King of the elephants. O be
st of the Kuru dynasty, those who hear this narration become fit to be promoted to the higher planetary systems. Simply because of hearing this narration, they gain a reputation as devotees, they are unaffected by the contamination of Kali-yuga, and they 
never see bad dreams.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.15 - Therefore, after getting up from bed in the morning, those who desire their own welfare-especially the br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas and in particular the br\'e4hma\'eba Vai\'f1\'eb
avas-should chant this narration as it is, without deviation, to counteract the troubles of bad dreams.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.16 - O best of the Kuru dynasty, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Supersoul of everyone, being thus pleased, addressed Gajendra in the presence of everyone there. He spoke the following blessings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.4.17-24 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: Freed from all sinful reactions are those who rise from bed at the end of night, early in the morning, and fully concentrate their minds with great attention upon My form; your form; this lake
; this mountain; the caves; the gardens; the cane plants; the bamboo plants; the celestial trees; the residential quarters of Me, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva; the three peaks of Trik\'fc\'f6
a Mountain, made of gold, silver and iron; My very pleasing abode [the ocean of milk]; the white island, \'c7vetadv\'e9pa, which is always brilliant with spiritual rays; My mark of \'c7r\'e9vatsa; the Kaustubha gem; My Vaijayant\'e9
 garland; My club, Kaumodak\'e9; My Sudar\'e7ana disc and P\'e4\'efcajanya conchshell; My bearer, Garu\'f2a, the king of the birds; My bed, \'c7e\'f1a N\'e4ga; My expansion of energy the goddess of fortune; Lord Brahm\'e4; N\'e4rada Muni; Lord \'c7
iva; Prahl\'e4da; My incarnations like Matsya, K\'fcrma and Var\'e4ha; My unlimited all-auspicious activities, which yield piety to he who hears them; the sun; the moon; fire; the mantra o\'e0k\'e4
ra; the Absolute Truth; the total material energy; the cows and br\'e4hma\'ebas; devotional service; the wives of Soma and Ka\'e7yapa, who are all daughters of King Dak\'f1a; the Rivers Ganges, Sarasvat\'e9, Nand\'e4 and Yamun\'e4 [K\'e4lind\'e9]; the ele
phant Air\'e4vata; Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja; the seven \'e5\'f1is; and the pious human beings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.25 - My dear devotee, unto those who rise from bed at the end of night and offer Me the prayers offered by you, I give an eternal residence in the spiritual world at the end of their lives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.4.26 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After giving this instruction, the Lord, who is known as H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a, bugled with His P\'e4\'ef
cajanya conchshell, in this way pleasing all the demigods, headed by Lord Brahm\'e4. Then He mounted the back of His carrier, Garu\'f2a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
