\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.31 - The proposals submitted by King Indra were immediately accepted by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and his assistants, headed by \'c7ambara and Ari\'f1\'f6anemi, and by all the other residents of Tripura.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.32 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, chastiser of enemies, the demigods and the demons thereafter made an armistice between them. Then, with great enterprise, they arranged to produce nectar, as proposed by Lord Indra.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.33 - Thereafter, with great strength, the demons and demigods, who were all very powerful and who had long, stout arms, uprooted Mandara Mountain. Crying very loudly, they brought it toward the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.34 - Because of conveying the great mountain for a long distance, King Indra, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali and the other demigods and demons became fatigued. Being unable to carry the mountain, they left it on the way.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.35 - The mountain known as Mandara, which was extremely heavy, being made of gold, fell and smashed many demigods and demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.36 - The demigods and demons were frustrated and disheartened, and their arms, thighs and shoulders were broken. Therefore the Supreme Personality of G
odhead, who knows everything, appeared there on the back of His carrier, Garu\'f2a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.37 - Observing that most of the demons and the demigods had been crushed by the falling of the mountain, the Lord glanced over them and brought them back to life. Thus
 they became free from grief, and they even had no bruises on their bodies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.38 - The Lord very easily lifted the mountain with one hand and placed it on the back of Garu\'f2a. Then, He too got on the back of Garu\'f2a and went to the ocean of milk, surrounded by the demigods and demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.39 - Thereafter, Garu\'f2a, the chief of birds, unloaded Mandara Mountain from his shoulder and brought it near the water. Then he was asked by the Lord to leave that place, and he left.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116 The Demigods and Demons Declare a Truce
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King Par\'e9k\'f1
it, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, being thus worshiped with prayers by the demigods and Lord Brahm\'e4, appeared before them. His bodily effulgence resembled the simultaneous rising of thousands of suns.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.2 - The vision of all the demigods was blocked by the Lord's effulgence. Thus they could see neither the sky, the directions, the land, nor even themselves, what to speak of seeing the Lord, who was present before them.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.3-7 - Lord Brahm\'e4, along with Lord \'c7iva
, saw the crystal-clear personal beauty of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose blackish body resembles a marakata gem, whose eyes are reddish like the depths of a lotus, who is dressed with garments that are yellow like molten gold, and whose entire
 body is attractively decorated. They saw His beautiful, smiling, lotuslike face, crowned by a helmet bedecked with valuable jewels. The Lord has attractive eyebrows, and His cheeks are adorned with earrings. Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva saw the belt on the Lo
rd's waist, the bangles on Mis arms, the necklace on His chest, and the ankle bells on His legs. The Lord is bedecked with flower garlands, His neck is decorated with the Kaustubha gem, and He carries with Him the goddess of fortune and His personal weapo
ns, like His disc and club. When Lord Brahm\'e4, along with Lord \'c7iva and the other demigods, thus saw the form of the Lord, they all immediately fell to the ground, offering their obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.8 - Lord Brahm\'e4 said: Although You are never born, Your app
earance and disappearance as an incarnation never cease. You are always free from the material qualities, and You are the shelter of transcendental bliss resembling an ocean. Eternally existing in Your transcendental form, You are the supreme subtle of th
e most extremely subtle. We therefore offer our respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme, whose existence is inconceivable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.9 - O best of persons, O supreme director, those who actually aspire for supreme good fortune worship this form of Your Lordship according to the Vedic Tantras. My Lord, we can see all the three worlds in You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.10 - My dear Lord, who are always fully independent, this entire cosmic manifestation arises from You, rests upon You and ends in You. Your Lordship is the begi
nning, sustenance and end of everything, like the earth, which is the cause of an earthen pot, which supports the pot, and to which the pot, when broken, finally returns.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.11 - O Supreme, You are independent in Your self and do not take help from others. Through Your own potency, You create this cosmic manifestation and enter into it. Those who are advanced in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, who are fully in knowledge of the authoritative \'e7\'e4stra, and who, through the practice of bhakti-yoga, are cleansed of all
 material contamination, can see with clear minds that although You exist within the transformations of the material qualities, Your presence is untouched by these qualities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.12 - As one can derive fire from wood, milk from the milk bag of the cow,
 food grains and water from the land, and prosperity in one's livelihood from industrial enterprises, so, by the practice of bhakti-yoga, even within this material world, one can achieve Your favor or intelligently approach You. Those who are pious all af
firm this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.6.13 - Elephants afflicted by a forest fire become very happy when they get water from the Ganges. Similarly, O my Lord, from whose navel grows a lotus flower, since You have now appeared before us, we have become transcendentally happy. By
 seeing Your Lordship, whom we have desired to see for a very long time, we have achieved our ultimate goal in life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.14 - My Lord, we, the various demigods, the directors of this universe, have come to Your lotus feet. Please fulfill the purpose fo
r which we have come. You are the witness of everything, from within and without. Nothing is unknown to You, and therefore it is unnecessary to inform You again of anything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.15 - I [Lord Brahm\'e4], Lord \'c7iva and all the demigods, accompanied by the praj\'e4patis like Dak\'f1
a, are nothing but sparks illuminated by You, who are the original fire. Since we are particles of You, what can we understand about our welfare? O Supreme Lord, please give us the means of deliverance that is suitable for the br\'e4hma\'ebas 
and demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.16 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When the Lord was thus offered prayers by the demigods, headed by Lord Brahm\'e4
, He understood the purpose for which they had approached Him. Therefore, in a deep voice that resembled the rumbling of clouds, the Lord replied to the demigods, who all stood there attentively with folded hands.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.17 - Although the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the master of the demigods, was capable of performing the activities of the demigods by Himself, He wanted t
o enjoy pastimes in churning the ocean. Therefore He spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.18 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva and other demigods, please hear Me with great attention, for what I say will bring good fortune for all of you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.19 - As long as you are not flourishing, you should make a truce with the demons and asuras, who are now being favored by time.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.20 - O demigods, fulfilling one's own interests is so important that one may even have to make a truce wit
h one's enemies. For the sake of one's self-interest, one has to act according to the logic of the snake and the mouse.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.21 - Immediately endeavor to produce nectar, which a person who is about to die may drink to become immortal.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.22-23 - O demigods, cast into the ocean of milk all kinds of vegetables, grass, creepers and drugs. Then, with My help, making Mandara Mountain the churning rod and V\'e4
suki the rope for churning, churn the ocean of milk with undiverted attention. Thus the demons will be engaged in labor, but you, the demigods, will gain the actual result, the nectar produced from the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.24 - My dear demigods, with patience and peace everything can be done, but if one is agitated by anger, the goal is not achieved. Therefore, whatever the demons ask, agree to their proposal.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.25 - A poison known as k\'e4lak\'fc\'f6a will be generated from the ocean of milk, but you should not fear it. And when various products are churned from the ocean, you should not be greedy for them or an
xious to obtain them, nor should you be angry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.26 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, after advising the demigods in this way, the independent Supreme Personality of Godhead, the best of all living entities, disappeared from their presence.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.27 - Then Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva, after offering their respectful obeisances to the Lord, returned to their abodes. All the demigods then approached Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.28 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, a most celebrated king of the demons, knew very well when to make peace and when to fight. Thus although his commanders and captains were agitated and were about to kill the demigods, Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bali, seeing that the demigods were coming to him without a militant attitude, forbade his commanders to kill them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.29 - The demigods approached Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Virocana, and sat down near him. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was protected by the commanders of the demons and was most opulent, having conquered all the universes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.30 - After pleasing Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja with mild words, Lord Indra, the King of the demigods, who was most intelligent, very politely submitted all the proposals he had learned from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.31 - The proposals submitted by King Indra were immediately accepted by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and his assistants, headed by \'c7ambara and Ari\'f1\'f6anemi, and by all the other residents of Tripura.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.32 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, chastiser of enemies, the demigods and the demons thereafter made an armistice between them. Then, with great enterprise, they arranged to produce nectar, as proposed by Lord Indra.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.33 - Thereafter, with great strength, the demons and demigods, who were all very powerful and who had long, stout arms, uprooted Mandara Mountain. Crying very loudly, they brought it toward the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.34 - Because of conveying the great mountain for a long distance, King Indra, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali and the other demigods and demons became fatigued. Being unable to carry the mountain, they left it on the way.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.35 - The mountain known as Mandara, which was extremely heavy, being made of gold, fell and smashed many demigods and demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.36 - The demigods and demons were frustrated and disheartened, and their arms, thighs and shoulders were br
oken. Therefore the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who knows everything, appeared there on the back of His carrier, Garu\'f2a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.37 - Observing that most of the demons and the demigods had been crushed by the falling of the mountain, the Lord glanced o
ver them and brought them back to life. Thus they became free from grief, and they even had no bruises on their bodies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.38 - The Lord very easily lifted the mountain with one hand and placed it on the back of Garu\'f2a. Then, He too got on the back of Garu\'f2a and went to the ocean of milk, surrounded by the demigods and demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.6.39 - Thereafter, Garu\'f2a, the chief of birds, unloaded Mandara Mountain from his shoulder and brought it near the water. Then he was asked by the Lord to leave that place, and he left.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-39
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O best of the Kurus, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, the demigods and demons summoned V\'e4
suki, king of the serpents, requesting him to come and promising to give him a share of the nectar. They coiled V\'e4suki around Mandara Mountain as a churning rope, and with great pleasure they endeavored to produce nectar by churning the ocean of milk.

\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.2 - The Personality of Godhead, Ajita, grasped the front portion of the snake, and then the demigods followed.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.3 - The
 leaders of the demons thought it unwise to hold the tail, the inauspicious portion of the snake. Instead, they wanted to hold the front, which had been taken by the Personality of Godhead and the demigods, because that portion was auspicious and glorious
. Thus the demons, on the plea that they were all highly advanced students of Vedic knowledge and were all famous for their birth and activities, protested that they wanted to hold the front of the snake.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.4 - Thus the demons remained silent, opposin
g the desire of the demigods. Seeing the demons and understanding their motive, the Personality of Godhead smiled. Without discussion, He immediately accepted their proposal by grasping the tail of the snake, and the demigods followed Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.5 - After thus adjusting how the snake was to be held, the sons of Ka\'e7yapa, both demigods and demons, began their activities, desiring to get nectar by churning the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.6 - O son of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2u dynasty, when Mandara Mountain was thus being used as
 a churning rod in the ocean of milk, it had no support, and therefore although held by the strong hands of the demigods and demons, it sank into the water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.7 - Because the mountain had been sunk by the strength of providence, the demigods and demons were disappointed, and their faces seemed to shrivel.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.8 - Seeing the situation that had been created by the will of the Supreme, the unlimitedly powerful Lord, whose determination is infallible, took the wonderful shape of a tortoise, entered th
e water, and lifted the great Mandara Mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.9 - When the demigods and demons saw that Mandara Mountain had been lifted, they were enlivened and encouraged to begin churning again. The mountain rested on the back of the great tortoise, which ext
ended for eight hundred thousand miles like a large island.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.10 - O King, when the demigods and demons, by the strength of their arms, rotated Mandara Mountain on the back of the extraordinary tortoise, the tortoise accepted the rolling of the mount
ain as a means of scratching His body, and thus He felt a pleasing sensation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.11 - Thereafter, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu entered the demons as the quality of passion, the demigods as the quality of goodness, and V\'e4suki as the quality of ignorance to encourage the
m and increase their various types of strength and energy.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.12 - Manifesting Himself with thousands of hands, the Lord then appeared on the summit of Mandara Mountain, like another great mountain, and held Mandara Mountain with one hand. In the upper planetary systems, Lord Brahm\'e4
 and Lord \'c7iva, along with Indra, King of heaven, and other demigods, offered prayers to the Lord and showered flowers upon Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.13 - The demigods and demons worked almost madly for the nectar, encouraged by the Lord, who was above and below the mountain and who had entered the demigods, the demons, V\'e4
suki and the mountain itself. Because of the strength of the demigods and demons, the ocean of milk was so powerfully agitated that all the alligators in the water were very much perturbed. Nonetheless the churning of the ocean continued in this way.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.14 - V\'e4suki had thousands of eyes and mouths. From his mouths he breathed smoke and blazing fire, which affected the demons, headed by Pauloma, K\'e4leya, Bali and Ilval
a. Thus the demons, who appeared like sarala trees burned by a forest fire, gradually became powerless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.15 - Because the demigods were also affected by the blazing breath of V\'e4suki, their bodily lusters diminished, and their garments, garlands, wea
pons and faces were blackened by smoke. However, by the grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, clouds appeared on the sea, pouring torrents of rain, and breezes blew, carrying particles of water from the sea waves, to give the demigods relief.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.16 - When nectar did not come from the ocean of milk, despite so much endeavor by the best of the demigods and demons, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ajita, personally began to churn the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.17 - The Lord appeared like a blackish cloud. H
e was dressed with yellow garments, His earrings shone on His ears like lightning, and His hair spread over His shoulders. He wore a garland of flowers, and His eyes were pinkish. With His strong, glorious arms, which award fearlessness throughout the uni
verse, He took hold of V\'e4suki and began churning the ocean, using Mandara Mountain as a churning rod. When engaged in this way, the Lord appeared like a beautifully situated mountain named Indran\'e9la.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.18 - The fish, sharks, tortoises and snakes were most agitated and perturbed. The entire ocean became turbulent, and even the large aquatic animals like whales, water elephants, crocodiles and timi\'ec
gila fish [large whales that can swallow small whales] came to the surface. While the ocean was being churned in this way, it first produced a fiercely dangerous poison called h\'e4lahala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.19 - O King, when that uncontrollable poison was forcefully spreading up and down in all directions, all the demigods, along with the Lord Himself, approached Lord \'c7iva [Sad\'e4\'e7
iva]. Feeling unsheltered and very much afraid, they sought shelter of him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.20 - The demigods observed Lord \'c7iva sitting on the summit of Kail\'e4sa Hill with his wife, Bhav\'e4n\'e9, for the auspicious development of the three worlds. He was being wo
rshiped by great saintly persons desiring liberation. The demigods offered him their obeisances and prayers with great respect.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.21 - The praj\'e4patis said: O greatest of all demigods, Mah\'e4deva, Supersoul of all living entities and cause of their happ
iness and prosperity, we have come to the shelter of your lotus feet. Now please save us from this fiery poison, which is spreading all over the three worlds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.22 - O lord, you are the cause of bondage and liberation of the entire universe because y
ou are its ruler. Those who are advanced in spiritual consciousness surrender unto you, and therefore you are the cause of mitigating their distresses, and you are also the cause of their liberation. We therefore worship Your Lordship.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.23 - O lord, you are self-effulgent and supreme. You create this material world by your personal energy, and you assume the names Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7
vara when you act in creation, maintenance and annihilation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.24 - You are the cause of all causes, the self-effulgent, inconceivable, impersonal Brahman, which is originally Parabrahman. You manifest various potencies in this cosmic manifestation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.25 - O lord, you are the original source of Vedic literature. You are the original cause of material creati
on, the life force, the senses, the five elements, the three modes and the mahat-tattva. You are eternal time, determination and the two religious systems called truth [satya] and truthfulness [\'e5ta]. You are the shelter of the syllable o\'e0
, which consists of three letters a-u-m.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.26 - O father of all planets, learned scholars know that fire is your mouth, the surface of the globe is your lotus feet, eternal time is your movement, all the directions are your ears, and Varu\'eb
a, master of the waters, is your tongue.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.7.27 - O lord, the sky is your navel, the air is your breathing, the sun is your eyes, and the water is your semen. You are the shelter of all kinds of living entities, high and low. The god of the moon is your mind, and the upper planeta
ry system is your head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.28 - O lord, you are the three Vedas personified. The seven seas are your abdomen, and the mountains are your bones. All drugs, creepers and vegetables are the hairs on your body, the Vedic mantras like G\'e4yatr\'e9
 are the seven layers of your body, and the Vedic religious system is the core of your heart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.29 - O lord, the five important Vedic mantras are represented by your five faces, from which the thirty-eight most celebrated Vedic mantras have been generated. Your Lordship, being celebrated as Lord \'c7
iva, is self-illuminated. You are directly situated as the supreme truth, known as Param\'e4tm\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.30 - O lord, your shadow is seen in irreligion, which brings about varieties of irreligious creations. The three modes o
f nature-goodness, passion and ignorance-are your three eyes. All the Vedic literatures, which are full of verses, are emanations from you because their compilers wrote the various scriptures after receiving your glance.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.31 - O Lord Gir\'e9\'e7a, since t
he impersonal Brahman effulgence is transcendental to the material modes of goodness, passion and ignorance, the various directors of this material world certainly cannot appreciate it or even know where it is. It is not understandable even to Lord Brahm
\'e4, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu or the King of heaven, Mahendra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.32 - When annihilation is performed by the flames and sparks emanating from your eyes, the entire creation is burned to ashes. Nonetheless, you do not know how this happens. What then is to be said of your destroying the Dak
\'f1a-yaj\'efa, Tripur\'e4sura and the k\'e4lak\'fc\'f6a poison? Such activities cannot be subject matters for prayers offered to you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.33 - Exalted, self-satisfied persons who preach to the entire world think of your lotus feet constantly within their hearts. However, when persons who do not know your austerity see you moving with Um\'e4
, they misunderstand you to be lusty, or when they see you wandering in the crematorium they mistakenly think that you are ferocious and envious. Certainly they are shameless. They cannot understand your activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.34 - Even personalities like Lord Brahm\'e4 and other demigods cannot understand your position, for you are beyond the moving and nonmoving creation. Since no one can understand you in truth, how can 
one offer you prayers? It is impossible. As far as we are concerned, we are creatures of Lord Brahm\'e4's creation. Under the circumstances, therefore, we cannot offer you adequate prayers, but as far as our ability allows, we have expressed our feelings.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB
 8.7.35 - O greatest of all rulers, your actual identity is impossible for us to understand. As far as we can see, your presence brings flourishing happiness to everyone. Beyond this, no one can appreciate your activities. We can see this much, and nothin
g more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.36 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Lord \'c7
iva is always benevolent toward all living entities. When he saw that the living entities were very much disturbed by the poison, which was spreading everywhere, he was very compassionate. Thus he spoke to his eternal consort, Sat\'e9, as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.37 - Lord \'c7iva said: My dear Bhav\'e4n\'e9, just see how all these living entities have been placed in danger because of the poison produced from the churning of the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.38 - It is my duty to give protection and safety to all living entities struggling for existence. Certainly it is the duty of the master to protect his suffering dependents.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.39 - People in general, being bewildered by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality
 of Godhead, are always engaged in animosity toward one another. But devotees, even at the risk of their own temporary lives, try to save them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.40 - My dear gentle wife Bhav\'e4n\'e9, when one performs benevolent activities for others, the Supreme Person
ality of Godhead, Hari, is very pleased. And when the Lord is pleased, I am also pleased, along with all other living creatures. Therefore, let me drink this poison, for all the living entities may thus become happy because of me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.41 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After informing Bhav\'e4n\'e9 in this way, Lord \'c7iva began to drink the poison, and Bhav\'e4n\'e9, who knew perfectly well the capabilities of Lord \'c7
iva, gave him her permission to do so.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.42 - Thereafter, Lord \'c7iva, who is dedicated to auspicious, benevolent work for humanity, compassionately took the whole quantity of poison in his palm and drank it.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.43 - As if in defamation, the poison born from the ocean of milk manifested its potency by marking Lord \'c7iva's neck with a bluish line. That line, however, is now accepted as an ornament of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.44 - It is said that great personalities almost always accept voluntary suffering because of the suffering of people in general. This is considered the highest method of worshiping
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is present in everyone's heart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
