it, the demigods and demons summoned V\'e4suki, king of the serpents, requesting him to come and promising to give him a share of the nectar. They coiled V\'e4
suki around Mandara Mountain as a churning rope, and with great pleasure they endeavored to produce nectar by churning the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.2 - The Personality of Godhead, Ajita, grasped the front portion of the snake, and then the demigods followed.
