\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.7 - Because the mountain had been sunk by the strength of providence, the demigods and demons were disappointed, and their faces seemed to shrivel.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.8 - Seeing the situation that had been created by the will of the Supreme, the unlimitedly powe
rful Lord, whose determination is infallible, took the wonderful shape of a tortoise, entered the water, and lifted the great Mandara Mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.9 - When the demigods and demons saw that Mandara Mountain had been lifted, they were enlivened and enco
uraged to begin churning again. The mountain rested on the back of the great tortoise, which extended for eight hundred thousand miles like a large island.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.10 - O King, when the demigods and demons, by the strength of their arms, rotated Mandara Mo
untain on the back of the extraordinary tortoise, the tortoise accepted the rolling of the mountain as a means of scratching His body, and thus He felt a pleasing sensation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.11 - Thereafter, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu entered the demons as the quality of passion, the demigods as the quality of goodness, and V\'e4
suki as the quality of ignorance to encourage them and increase their various types of strength and energy.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.12 - Manifesting Himself with thousands of hands, the Lord then appeared on the summit of Mandara Mountain, like another great mountain, and held Mandara Mountain with one hand. In the upper planetary systems, Lord Brahm\'e4
 and Lord \'c7iva, along with Indra, King of heaven, and other demigods, offered prayers to the Lord and showered flowers upon Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.13 - The demigods and demons worked almost madly for the nectar, encouraged by the Lord, who was above and below the mountain and who had entered the demigods, the demons, V\'e4
suki and the mountain itself. Because of the strength of the demigods and demons, the ocean of milk was so powerfully agitated that all the alligators in the water were very much perturbed. Nonetheless the churning of the ocean continued in this way.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.14 - V\'e4suki had thousands of eyes and mouths. From his mouths he breathed smoke and blazing fire, which affected the demons, headed by Pauloma, K\'e4
leya, Bali and Ilvala. Thus the demons, who appeared like sarala trees burned by a forest fire, gradually became powerless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.15 - Because the demigods were also affected by the blazing breath of V\'e4
suki, their bodily lusters diminished, and their garments, garlands, weapons and faces were blackened by smoke. However, by the grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, clouds appeared on the sea, pouring torrents of rain, and b
reezes blew, carrying particles of water from the sea waves, to give the demigods relief.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.16 - When nectar did not come from the ocean of milk, despite so much endeavor by the best of the demigods and demons, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ajita, personally began to churn the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.17 - The Lord appeared like a blackish cloud. He was dressed with yellow garments, His earrings shone on His ears like lightning, and His hair spread over His shoulders. He wore a garland of flowers, and His
 eyes were pinkish. With His strong, glorious arms, which award fearlessness throughout the universe, He took hold of V\'e4
suki and began churning the ocean, using Mandara Mountain as a churning rod. When engaged in this way, the Lord appeared like a beautifully situated mountain named Indran\'e9la.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.18 - The fish, sharks, tortoises and snakes were most agitated and perturbed. The entire ocean became turbulent, and even the large aquatic animals like whales, water elephants, crocodiles and timi\'ecgila fish [
large whales that can swallow small whales] came to the surface. While the ocean was being churned in this way, it first produced a fiercely dangerous poison called h\'e4lahala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.19 - O King, when that uncontrollable poison was forcefully spreading up and down in all directions, all the demigods, along with the Lord Himself, approached Lord \'c7iva [Sad\'e4\'e7
iva]. Feeling unsheltered and very much afraid, they sought shelter of him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.20 - The demigods observed Lord \'c7iva sitting on the summit of Kail\'e4sa Hill with his wife, Bhav\'e4n\'e9
, for the auspicious development of the three worlds. He was being worshiped by great saintly persons desiring liberation. The demigods offered him their obeisances and prayers with great respect.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.21 - The praj\'e4patis said: O greatest of all demigods, Mah\'e4
deva, Supersoul of all living entities and cause of their happiness and prosperity, we have come to the shelter of your lotus feet. Now please save us from this fiery poison, which is spreading all over the three worlds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.7.22 - O lord, you are the cause of bondage and liberation of the entire universe because you are its ruler. Those who are advanced in spiritual consciousness surrender unto you, and therefore you are the cause of mitigating their distresses, and you
 are also the cause of their liberation. We therefore worship Your Lordship.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.23 - O lord, you are self-effulgent and supreme. You create this material world by your personal energy, and you assume the names Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7vara when you act i
n creation, maintenance and annihilation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.24 - You are the cause of all causes, the self-effulgent, inconceivable, impersonal Brahman, which is originally Parabrahman. You manifest various potencies in this cosmic manifestation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.25 - O lord
, you are the original source of Vedic literature. You are the original cause of material creation, the life force, the senses, the five elements, the three modes and the mahat-tattva. You are eternal time, determination and the two religious systems call
ed truth [satya] and truthfulness [\'e5ta]. You are the shelter of the syllable o\'e0, which consists of three letters a-u-m.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.26 - O father of all planets, learned scholars know that fire is your mouth, the surface of the globe is your lotus feet, eternal time is your movement, all the directions are your ears, and Varu\'eb
a, master of the waters, is your tongue.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.27 - O lord, the sky is your navel, the air is your breathing, the sun is your eyes, and the water is your semen. You are the shelter of all
 kinds of living entities, high and low. The god of the moon is your mind, and the upper planetary system is your head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.28 - O lord, you are the three Vedas personified. The seven seas are your abdomen, and the mountains are your bones. All drugs, creepers and vegetables are the hairs on your body, the Vedic mantras like G\'e4yatr\'e9
 are the seven layers of your body, and the Vedic religious system is the core of your heart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.29 - O lord, the five important Vedic mantras are represented by your five faces, from which the thirty-eight most celebrated Vedic mantras have been generated. Your Lordship, being celebrated as Lord \'c7
iva, is self-illuminated. You are directly situated as the supreme truth, known as Param\'e4tm\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.30 - O lord, your shadow
 is seen in irreligion, which brings about varieties of irreligious creations. The three modes of nature-goodness, passion and ignorance-are your three eyes. All the Vedic literatures, which are full of verses, are emanations from you because their compil
ers wrote the various scriptures after receiving your glance.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.31 - O Lord Gir\'e9\'e7a, since the impersonal Brahman effulgence is transcendental to the material modes of goodness, passion and ignorance, the various directors of this material world certai
nly cannot appreciate it or even know where it is. It is not understandable even to Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu or the King of heaven, Mahendra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.32 - When annihilation is performed by the flames and sparks emanating from your eyes, the entire creation is burned to ashes. Nonetheless, you do not know how this happens. What then is to be said of your destroying the Dak
\'f1a-yaj\'efa, Tripur\'e4sura and the k\'e4lak\'fc\'f6a poison? Such activities cannot be subject matters for prayers offered to you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.33 - Exalted, self-satisfied persons who preach to the entire world think of your lotus feet constantly within their hearts. However, when persons who do not know your austerity see you moving with Um\'e4
, they misunderstand you to be lusty, or when they see you wandering in the crematorium they mistakenly think that you are ferocious and envious. Certainly they are shameless. They cannot understand your activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.34 - Even personalities like Lord Brahm\'e4 and other demigods cannot understand your position, for you 
are beyond the moving and nonmoving creation. Since no one can understand you in truth, how can one offer you prayers? It is impossible. As far as we are concerned, we are creatures of Lord Brahm\'e4
's creation. Under the circumstances, therefore, we cannot offer you adequate prayers, but as far as our ability allows, we have expressed our feelings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.35 - O greatest of all rulers, your actual identity is impossible for us to understand. As far as we can see, your presence brings flourishing happiness to
 everyone. Beyond this, no one can appreciate your activities. We can see this much, and nothing more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.36 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Lord \'c7iva is always benevolent toward all living entities. When he saw that the living entities were very 
much disturbed by the poison, which was spreading everywhere, he was very compassionate. Thus he spoke to his eternal consort, Sat\'e9, as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.37 - Lord \'c7iva said: My dear Bhav\'e4n\'e9, just see how all these living entities have been placed in danger because of the poison produced from the churning of the ocean of milk.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.38 - It is my duty to give protection and safety to all living entities struggling for existence. Certainly it is the duty of the master to protect his suffering dependents.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 S
B 8.7.39 - People in general, being bewildered by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, are always engaged in animosity toward one another. But devotees, even at the risk of their own temporary lives, try to save them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.40 - My dear gentle wife Bhav\'e4n\'e9
, when one performs benevolent activities for others, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, is very pleased. And when the Lord is pleased, I am also pleased, along with all other living creatures. Therefore, let me drink this po
ison, for all the living entities may thus become happy because of me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.41 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After informing Bhav\'e4n\'e9 in this way, Lord \'c7iva began to drink the poison, and Bhav\'e4n\'e9, who knew perfectly well the capabilities of Lord \'c7i
va, gave him her permission to do so.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.42 - Thereafter, Lord \'c7iva, who is dedicated to auspicious, benevolent work for humanity, compassionately took the whole quantity of poison in his palm and drank it.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.43 - As if in defamation, the poison born from the ocean of milk manifested its potency by marking Lord \'c7iva's neck with a bluish line. That line, however, is now accepted as an ornament of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.44 - It is said that great personalities almost always accept voluntary suffering be
cause of the suffering of people in general. This is considered the highest method of worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is present in everyone's heart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.45 - Upon hearing of this act, everyone, including Bhav\'e4n\'e9 [the daughter of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Dak\'f1a], Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and the people in general, very highly praised this deed performed by Lord \'c7
iva, who is worshiped by the demigods and who bestows benedictions upon the people.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.7.46 - Scorpions, cobras, poisonous drugs and other animals whose bites are poisonous took the opportunity to drink whatever little poison had fallen and scattered from Lord \'c7iva's hand while he was drinking.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-46
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Upon Lord \'c7iva's drinking the poison, both the demigods 
and the demons, being very pleased, began to churn the ocean with renewed vigor. As a result of this, there appeared a cow known as surabhi.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.2 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, great sages who were completely aware of the Vedic ritualistic ceremonies took charge 
of that surabhi cow, which produced all the yogurt, milk and ghee absolutely necessary for offering oblations into the fire. They did this just for the sake of pure ghee, which they wanted for the performance of sacrifices to elevate themselves to the hig
her planetary systems, up to Brahmaloka.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.3 - Thereafter, a horse named Uccai\'f9\'e7rav\'e4, which was as white as the moon, was generated. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja desired to possess this horse, and Indra, the King of heaven, did not protest, for he had previously bee
n so advised by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.4 - As the next result of the churning, the king of elephants, named Air\'e4vata, was generated. This elephant was white, and with its four tusks it defied the glories of Kail\'e4sa Mountain, the glorious abode of Lord \'c7
iva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.5 - Thereafter, O King, eight great elephants, which could go in any direction, were generated. They were headed by Air\'e4va\'eba. Eight she-elephants, headed by Abhramu, were also generated.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.6 - Generated thereafter from the great ocean were the celebrated gems Kaustubha-ma\'ebi and Padmar\'e4ga-ma\'ebi. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, to decorate His chest, desired to possess them. Generated next was the p\'e4rij\'e4
ta flower, which decorates the celestial planets. O King, as you fulfill the desires of everyone on this planet by fulfilling all ambitions, the p\'e4rij\'e4ta fulfills the desires of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.7 - Next there appeared the Apsar\'e4s [who are used as prostitutes on the heavenly planets]. They were fully decorated with golden ornaments and lockets and were dressed in fine and attractive clothing. The Apsar\'e4
s move very slowly in an attractive style that bewilders the inhabitants of the heavenly planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.8 - Then there appeared the goddess of fortune, Ram\'e4, who is absolutely dedicated to being
 enjoyed by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. She appeared like electricity, surpassing the lightning that might illuminate a marble mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.9 - Because of her exquisite beauty, her bodily features, her youth, her complexion and her glories, ev
eryone, including the demigods, the demons and the human beings, desired her. They were attracted because she is the source of all opulences.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.10 - The King of heaven, Indra, brought a suitable sitting place for the goddess of fortune. All the rivers of sacred water, such as the Ganges and Yamun\'e4
, personified themselves, and each of them brought pure water in golden waterpots for mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.11 - The land became a person and collected all the drugs and herbs needed 
for installing the Deity. The cows delivered five products, namely milk, yogurt, ghee, urine and cow dung, and spring personified collected everything produced in spring, during the months of Caitra and Vai\'e7\'e4kha [April and May].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.12 - The great sage
s performed the bathing ceremony of the goddess of fortune as directed in the authorized scriptures, the Gandharvas chanted all-auspicious Vedic mantras, and the professional women dancers very nicely danced and sang authorized songs prescribed in the Ved
as.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.13 - The clouds in personified form beat various types of drums, known as m\'e5da\'ecgas, pa\'ebavas, murajas and \'e4
nakas. They also blew conchshells and bugles known as gomukhas and played flutes and stringed instruments. The combined sound of these instruments was tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.14 - Thereafter, the great elephants from all the directions carried big water jugs full of Ganges water and bathed the goddess of fortune, to the accompaniment of Vedic mantras chanted by learned br\'e4hma\'eb
as. While thus being
 bathed, the goddess of fortune maintained her original style, with a lotus flower in her hand, and she appeared very beautiful. The goddess of fortune is the most chaste, for she does not know anyone but the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.15 - The ocean, which is the source of all valuable jewels, supplied the upper and lower portions of a yellow silken garment. The predominating deity of the water, Varu\'eb
a, presented flower garlands surrounded by six-legged bumblebees, drunken with honey.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.16 - Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4, one of the praj\'e4patis, supplied varieties of decorated ornaments. The goddess of learning, Sarasvat\'e9, supplied a necklace, Lord Brahm\'e4 supplied a lotus flower, and the inhabitants of N\'e4
galoka supplied earrings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.17 - Thereafter, mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, having been properly celebrated with an auspicious ritualistic ceremony, began moving about, holding in her hand a garland of lotus flowers, which were surrounded by humming bumblebees. Smiling with shyness, her cheeks d
ecorated by her earrings, she looked extremely beautiful.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.18 - Her two breasts, which were symmetrical and nicely situated, were covered with sandalwood pulp and ku\'eckuma powder, and her waist was very thin. As she walked here and there, her ankle b
ells jingling softly, she appeared like a creeper of gold.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.19 - While walking among the Gandharvas, Yak\'f1as, asuras, Siddhas, C\'e4ra\'ebas and denizens of heaven, Lak\'f1m\'e9dev\'e9, the goddess of fortune, was scrutinizingly examining them, but she could not fi
nd anyone naturally endowed with all good qualities. None of them was devoid of faults, and therefore she could not take shelter of any of them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.20 - The goddess of fortune, examining the assembly, thought in this way: Someone who has undergone gre
at austerity has not yet conquered anger. Someone possesses knowledge, but he has not conquered material desires. Someone is a very great personality, but he cannot conquer lusty desires. Even a great personality depends on something else. How, then, can 
he be the supreme controller?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.21 - Someone may possess full knowledge of religion but still not be kind to all living entities. In someone, whether human or demigod, there may be renunciation, but that is not the cause of liberation. Someone may pos
sess great power and yet be unable to check the power of eternal time. Someone else may have renounced attachment to the material world, yet he cannot compare to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, no one is completely freed from the influence 
of the material modes of nature.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.22 - Someone may have longevity but not have auspiciousness or good behavior. Someone may have both auspiciousness and good behavior, but the duration of his life is not fixed. Although such demigods as Lord \'c7iva hav
e eternal life, they have inauspicious habits like living in crematoriums. And even if others are well qualified in all respects, they are not devotees of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.23 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: In this way, after full 
deliberation, the goddess of fortune accepted Mukunda as her husband because although He is independent and not in want of her, He possesses all transcendental qualities and mystic powers and is therefore the most desirable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.24 - Approaching the Su
preme Personality of Godhead, the goddess of fortune placed upon His shoulders the garland of newly grown lotus flowers, which was surrounded by humming bumblebees searching for honey. Then, expecting to get a place on the bosom of the Lord, she remained 
standing by His side, her face smiling in shyness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.25 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the father of the three worlds, and His bosom is the residence of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, the proprietor of all opulences. The goddess of fo
rtune, by her favorable and merciful glance, can increase the opulence of the three worlds, along with their inhabitants and their directors, the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.26 - The inhabitants of Gandharvaloka and C\'e4ra\'ebaloka then took the opportunity to play their musical instruments, such as conchshells, bugles and drums. They began dancing and singing along with their wives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.27 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the great sage A\'ecgir\'e4, and similar directors of universal management showered flowers and chanted mantras indicating the transcendental glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.28 - All the demigods, along with the praj\'e4patis and their descendants, being blessed by Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9's glance upon them, were immediately enriched with good behavior and t
ranscendental qualities. Thus they were very much satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.29 - O King, because of being neglected by the goddess of fortune, the demons and R\'e4k\'f1asas were depressed, bewildered and frustrated, and thus they became shameless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.30 - Next appeared V\'e4ru\'eb\'e9, the lotus-eyed goddess who controls drunkards. With the permission of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the demons, headed by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, took possession of this young girl.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.31 - O King, thereafter, while the sons of Ka\'e7yapa, both demons and demigods, were engaged in churning the ocean of milk, a very wonderful male person appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.32 - He was strongly built; his arms were long, stout and strong; his neck, which was marked with three lines, resembled a conchshell; 
his eyes were reddish; and his complexion was blackish. He was very young, he was garlanded with flowers, and his entire body was fully decorated with various ornaments.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.33 - He was dressed in yellow garments and wore brightly polished earrings mad
e of pearls. The tips of his hair were anointed with oil, and his chest was very broad. His body had all good features, he was stout and strong like a lion, and he was decorated with bangles. In his hand he carried a jug filled to the top with nectar.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.34 - This person was Dhanvantari, a plenary portion of a plenary portion of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. He was very conversant with the science of medicine, and as one of the demigods he was permitted to take a share in sacrifices.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.35 - Upon seeing Dhanvantari carrying the jug of nectar, the demons, desiring the jug and its contents, immediately snatched it away by force.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.36 - When the jug of nectar was carried off by the demons, the demigods were morose. Thus they sought shelter at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.37 - When the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who always desires to fulfill the ambitions of His devotees, saw that the demigods were morose, He said to them, "Do not be aggrieved. By My own energy I shall be
wilder the demons by creating a quarrel among them. In this way I shall fulfill your desire to have the nectar."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.38 - O King, a quarrel then arose among the demons over who would get the nectar first. Each of them said, "You cannot drink it first. I must drink it first. Me first, not you!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.39-40 - Some of the demons said, "All the demigods have taken part in churning the ocean of milk. Now, as everyone has an equal right to partake in any public sacrifice, according to the eternal religious 
system it is befitting that the demigods now have a share of the nectar." O King, in this way the weaker demons forbade the stronger demons to take the nectar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.41-46 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu, who can counteract any unfavorable situation, then assumed the form of an extremely beautiful woman. This incarnation as a woman, Mohin\'e9-m\'fc
rti, was most pleasing to the mind. Her complexion resembled in color a newly grown blackish lotus, and every part of Her body was beautifully situated. H
er ears were equally decorated with earrings, Her cheeks were very beautiful, Her nose was raised and Her face full of youthful luster. Her large breasts made Her waist seem very thin. Attracted by the aroma of Her face and body, bumblebees hummed around 
Her, and thus Her eyes were restless. Her hair, which was extremely beautiful, was garlanded with mallik\'e4
 flowers. Her attractively constructed neck was decorated with a necklace and other ornaments, Her arms were decorated with bangles, Her body was covere
d with a clean sari, and Her breasts seemed like islands in an ocean of beauty. Her legs were decorated with ankle bells. Because of the movements of Her eyebrows as She smiled with shyness and glanced over the demons, all the demons were saturated with l
usty desires, and every one of them desired to possess Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  8. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Upon Lord \'c7
iva's drinking the poison, both the demigods and the demons, being very pleased, began to churn the ocean with renewed vigor. As a result of this, there appeared a cow known as surabhi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.2 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, great sages who were completely aware of the Vedic ritualistic ceremonies took charge of that surabhi cow, which produced all the yogurt, milk and ghee absolutely necessary for offering
 oblations into the fire. They did this just for the sake of pure ghee, which they wanted for the performance of sacrifices to elevate themselves to the higher planetary systems, up to Brahmaloka.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.3 - Thereafter, a horse named Uccai\'f9\'e7rav\'e4, which was as white as the moon, was generated. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja desired to possess this horse, and Indra, the King of heaven, did not protest, for he had previously been so advised by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.4 - As the next result of the churning, the king of elephants, named Air\'e4vata, was generated. This elephant was white, and with its four tusks it defied the glories of Kail\'e4sa Mountain, the glorious abode of Lord \'c7
iva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.5 - Thereafter, O King, eight great elephants, which could go in any direction, were generated. They were headed by Air\'e4va\'eba. Eight she-elephants, headed by Abhramu, were also generated.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.6 - Generated thereafter from the great ocean were the celebrated gems Kaustubha-ma\'ebi and Padmar\'e4ga-ma\'ebi. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, to decorate His chest, desired to possess them. Generated next was the p\'e4rij\'e4
ta flower, which decorates the celestial planets. O King, as you fulfill the desires of everyone on this planet by fulfilling all ambitions, the p\'e4rij\'e4ta fulfills the desires of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.7 - Next there appeared the Apsar\'e4s [who are used as prostitutes on the heavenly planets]. They were fully decorated with golden ornaments and lockets and were dressed in fine and attractive clothing. The Apsar\'e4
s move very slowly in an attractive style that bewilders the inhabitants of the heavenly planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.8 - Then there appeared the goddess of fortune, Ram\'e4, who is absolutely dedicated to being enjoyed by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. She appeared like electricity, surpassing the light
ning that might illuminate a marble mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.9 - Because of her exquisite beauty, her bodily features, her youth, her complexion and her glories, everyone, including the demigods, the demons and the human beings, desired her. They were attracted b
ecause she is the source of all opulences.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.10 - The King of heaven, Indra, brought a suitable sitting place for the goddess of fortune. All the rivers of sacred water, such as the Ganges and Yamun\'e4, personified themselves, and each of them brought 
pure water in golden waterpots for mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.11 - The land became a person and collected all the drugs and herbs needed for installing the Deity. The cows delivered five products, namely milk, yogurt, ghee, urine and co
w dung, and spring personified collected everything produced in spring, during the months of Caitra and Vai\'e7\'e4kha [April and May].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.12 - The great sages performed the bathing ceremony of the goddess of fortune as directed in the authorized scriptures
, the Gandharvas chanted all-auspicious Vedic mantras, and the professional women dancers very nicely danced and sang authorized songs prescribed in the Vedas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.13 - The clouds in personified form beat various types of drums, known as m\'e5da\'ecgas, pa\'ebavas, murajas and \'e4
nakas. They also blew conchshells and bugles known as gomukhas and played flutes and stringed instruments. The combined sound of these instruments was tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.14 - Thereafter, the great elephants from all the directions carried big water jugs full of Ganges water and bathed the goddess of fortune, to the accompaniment of Vedic mantras chanted by learned br\'e4hma\'eb
as. While thus being bathed, the goddess of fortune maintained her original style, with a lotus flower in her hand, and
 she appeared very beautiful. The goddess of fortune is the most chaste, for she does not know anyone but the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.15 - The ocean, which is the source of all valuable jewels, supplied the upper and lower portions of a yellow silken garment. The predominating deity of the water, Varu\'eb
a, presented flower garlands surrounded by six-legged bumblebees, drunken with honey.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.16 - Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4, one of the praj\'e4patis, supplied varieties of decorated ornaments. The goddess of learning, Sarasvat\'e9, supplied a necklace, Lord Brahm\'e4 supplied a lotus flower, and the inhabitants of N\'e4
galoka supplied earrings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.17 - Thereafter, mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, having been properly celebrated with an auspicious ritualistic 
ceremony, began moving about, holding in her hand a garland of lotus flowers, which were surrounded by humming bumblebees. Smiling with shyness, her cheeks decorated by her earrings, she looked extremely beautiful.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.18 - Her two breasts, which were symmetrical and nicely situated, were covered with sandalwood pulp and ku\'ec
kuma powder, and her waist was very thin. As she walked here and there, her ankle bells jingling softly, she appeared like a creeper of gold.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.19 - While walking among the Gandharvas, Yak\'f1as, asuras, Siddhas, C\'e4ra\'ebas and denizens of heaven, Lak\'f1m\'e9dev\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, was scrutinizingly examining them, but she could not find anyone naturally endowed with all good qualities. None of them was devoid of faults, and therefore she could not take shelter of any of them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.20 - The goddess of fortune, examining the assembly, thought in this way: Someone who has undergone great austerity has not yet conquered anger. Someone possesses knowledge, but he has not conquered mat
erial desires. Someone is a very great personality, but he cannot conquer lusty desires. Even a great personality depends on something else. How, then, can he be the supreme controller?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.21 - Someone may possess full knowledge of religion but still 
not be kind to all living entities. In someone, whether human or demigod, there may be renunciation, but that is not the cause of liberation. Someone may possess great power and yet be unable to check the power of eternal time. Someone else may have renou
nced attachment to the material world, yet he cannot compare to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, no one is completely freed from the influence of the material modes of nature.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.22 - Someone may have longevity but not have auspiciousness or good behavior. Someone may have both auspiciousness and good behavior, but the duration of his life is not fixed. Although such demigods as Lord \'c7
iva have eternal life, they have inauspicious habits like living in crematoriums. And even if others are well qualified in all respects, they are not devotees of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.23 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: In this way, after full deliberation, the goddess of fortune accepted Mukunda as her husband because although He is indepen
dent and not in want of her, He possesses all transcendental qualities and mystic powers and is therefore the most desirable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.24 - Approaching the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the goddess of fortune placed upon His shoulders the garland of newly
 grown lotus flowers, which was surrounded by humming bumblebees searching for honey. Then, expecting to get a place on the bosom of the Lord, she remained standing by His side, her face smiling in shyness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.25 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the father of the three worlds, and His bosom is the residence of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, the proprietor of all opulences. The goddess of fortune, by her favorable and merciful glance, can increase the opulence of the three worlds, along with their inhabitants and their directors, the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.26 - The inhabitants of Gandharvaloka and C\'e4ra\'ebaloka then took the opportunity to play their musical instruments, such as conchshells, bugles and drums. They began dancing and singing along with their wives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.27 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the great sage A\'ecgir\'e4, and similar directors of universal management showered flowers and chanted mantras indicating the transcendental glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.28 - All the demigods, along with the praj\'e4patis and their descendants, being blessed by Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9
's glance upon them, were immediately enriched with good behavior and transcendental qualities. Thus they were very much satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.29 - O King, because of being neglected by the goddess of fortune, the demons and R\'e4k\'f1asas were depressed, bewildered and frustrated, and thus they became shameless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.30 - Next appeared V\'e4ru\'eb\'e9, the lotus-eyed goddess who controls drunkards. With the permission of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the demons, headed by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, took possession of this young girl.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.31 - O King, thereafter, while the sons of Ka\'e7yapa, both demons and demigods, were engaged in churning the ocean of milk, a very wonderful male person appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.8.32 - He was strongly built; his arms were long, stout and strong; his neck, which was marked with three lines, resembled a conchshell; his eyes were reddish; and his complexion was blackish. He was very young, he was garlanded with fl
owers, and his entire body was fully decorated with various ornaments.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
