\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.19 - While walking among the Gandharvas, Yak\'f1as, asuras, Siddhas, C\'e4ra\'ebas and denizens of heaven, Lak\'f1m\'e9dev\'e9, the goddess of fortun
e, was scrutinizingly examining them, but she could not find anyone naturally endowed with all good qualities. None of them was devoid of faults, and therefore she could not take shelter of any of them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.20 - The goddess of fortune, examining the as
sembly, thought in this way: Someone who has undergone great austerity has not yet conquered anger. Someone possesses knowledge, but he has not conquered material desires. Someone is a very great personality, but he cannot conquer lusty desires. Even a gr
eat personality depends on something else. How, then, can he be the supreme controller?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.21 - Someone may possess full knowledge of religion but still not be kind to all living entities. In someone, whether human or demigod, there may be renunciation
, but that is not the cause of liberation. Someone may possess great power and yet be unable to check the power of eternal time. Someone else may have renounced attachment to the material world, yet he cannot compare to the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
 Therefore, no one is completely freed from the influence of the material modes of nature.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.22 - Someone may have longevity but not have auspiciousness or good behavior. Someone may have both auspiciousness and good behavior, but the duration of his life is not fixed. Although such demigods as Lord \'c7
iva have eternal life, they have inauspicious habits like living in crematoriums. And even if others are well qualified in all respects, they are not devotees of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.23 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 continued: In this way, after full deliberation, the goddess of fortune accepted Mukunda as her husband because although He is independent and not in want of her, He possesses all transcendental qualities and mystic powers and is the
refore the most desirable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.24 - Approaching the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the goddess of fortune placed upon His shoulders the garland of newly grown lotus flowers, which was surrounded by humming bumblebees searching for honey. Then, expecti
ng to get a place on the bosom of the Lord, she remained standing by His side, her face smiling in shyness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.25 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the father of the three worlds, and His bosom is the residence of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of f
ortune, the proprietor of all opulences. The goddess of fortune, by her favorable and merciful glance, can increase the opulence of the three worlds, along with their inhabitants and their directors, the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.26 - The inhabitants of Gandharvaloka and C\'e4ra\'ebaloka then took the opportunity to play their musical instruments, such as conchshells, bugles and drums. They began dancing and singing along with their wives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.27 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the great sage A\'ecgir\'e4, and similar directors of universal management showered flowers and chanted mantras indicating the transcendental glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.28 - All the demigods, along with the praj\'e4patis and their descendants, being blessed by Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9's glance upo
n them, were immediately enriched with good behavior and transcendental qualities. Thus they were very much satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.29 - O King, because of being neglected by the goddess of fortune, the demons and R\'e4k\'f1asas were depressed, bewildered and frustrated, and thus they became shameless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.30 - Next appeared V\'e4ru\'eb\'e9, the lotus-eyed goddess who controls drunkards. With the permission of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the demons, headed by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, took possession of this young girl.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.31 - O King, thereafter, while the sons of Ka\'e7yapa, both demons and demigods, were engaged in churning the ocean of milk, a very wonderful male person appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.32 - He was strongly built; his arms were long, stout and strong; his neck, w
hich was marked with three lines, resembled a conchshell; his eyes were reddish; and his complexion was blackish. He was very young, he was garlanded with flowers, and his entire body was fully decorated with various ornaments.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.33 - He was dressed 
in yellow garments and wore brightly polished earrings made of pearls. The tips of his hair were anointed with oil, and his chest was very broad. His body had all good features, he was stout and strong like a lion, and he was decorated with bangles. In hi
s hand he carried a jug filled to the top with nectar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.34 - This person was Dhanvantari, a plenary portion of a plenary portion of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. He was very conversant with the science of medicine, and as one of the demigods he was permitted to take a share in sacrifices.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.35 - Upon seeing Dhanvantari carrying the jug of nectar, the demons, desiring the jug and its contents, immediately snatched it away by force.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.36 - When the jug of nectar was carried off by the demons, the demigods were morose. Thus they sought shelter at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.37 - When the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who always desires to fulfill the ambitions of His devotees, saw that the demigods were morose, He said 
to them, "Do not be aggrieved. By My own energy I shall bewilder the demons by creating a quarrel among them. In this way I shall fulfill your desire to have the nectar."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.38 - O King, a quarrel then arose among the demons over who would get the nectar first. Each of them said, "You cannot drink it first. I must drink it first. Me first, not you!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.39-40 - Some of the demons said, "All the demigods have taken part in churning the ocean of milk. Now, as everyone has an equal right to partake in
 any public sacrifice, according to the eternal religious system it is befitting that the demigods now have a share of the nectar." O King, in this way the weaker demons forbade the stronger demons to take the nectar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.8.41-46 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu, who can counteract any unfavorable situation, then assumed the form of an extremely beautiful woman. This incarnation as a woman, Mohin\'e9-m\'fc
rti, was most pleasing to the mind. Her complexion resembled in color a newly grown blackish lot
us, and every part of Her body was beautifully situated. Her ears were equally decorated with earrings, Her cheeks were very beautiful, Her nose was raised and Her face full of youthful luster. Her large breasts made Her waist seem very thin. Attracted by
 the aroma of Her face and body, bumblebees hummed around Her, and thus Her eyes were restless. Her hair, which was extremely beautiful, was garlanded with mallik\'e4
 flowers. Her attractively constructed neck was decorated with a necklace and other ornaments,
 Her arms were decorated with bangles, Her body was covered with a clean sari, and Her breasts seemed like islands in an ocean of beauty. Her legs were decorated with ankle bells. Because of the movements of Her eyebrows as She smiled with shyness and gla
nced over the demons, all the demons were saturated with lusty desires, and every one of them desired to possess Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-45
