\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.20 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead as Mohin\'e9-m\'fcrti, the master of the universe, arranged separate lines of sitting places and seated the demigods and demons according to their positions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.21 - Taking the container of nectar in Her hands, She first approached the d
emons, satisfied them with sweet words and thus cheated them of their share of the nectar. Then She administered the nectar to the demigods, who were sitting at a distant place, to make them free from invalidity, old age and death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.22 - O King, sin
ce the demons had promised to accept whatever the woman did, whether just or unjust, now, to keep this promise, to show their equilibrium and to save themselves from fighting with a woman, they remained silent.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.23 - The demons had developed affection for Mohin\'e9-m\'fc
rti and a kind of faith in Her, and they were afraid of disturbing their relationship. Therefore they showed respect and honor to Her words and did not say anything that might disturb their friendship with Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.24 - R\'e4hu, the demon 
who causes eclipses of the sun and moon, covered himself with the dress of a demigod and thus entered the assembly of the demigods and drank nectar without being detected by anyone, even by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The moon and the sun, however
, because of permanent animosity toward R\'e4hu, understood the situation. Thus R\'e4hu was detected.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.25 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, using His disc, which was sharp like a razor, at once cut off R\'e4hu's head. When R\'e4hu's head was severed fr
om his body, the body, being untouched by the nectar, could not survive.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.26 - R\'e4hu's head, however, having been touched by the nectar, became immortal. Thus Lord Brahm\'e4 accepted R\'e4hu's head as one of the planets. Since R\'e4hu is an eternal enemy of t
he moon and the sun, he always tries to attack them on the nights of the full moon and the dark moon.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.27 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the best friend and well-wisher of the three worlds. Thus when the demigods had almost finished drinkin
g the nectar, the Lord, in the presence of all the demons, disclosed His original form.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.28 - The place, the time, the cause, the purpose, the activity and the ambition were all the same for both the demigods and the demons, but the demigods achieve
d one result and the demons another. Because the demigods are always under the shelter of the dust of the Lord's lotus feet, they could very easily drink the nectar and get its result. The demons, however, not having sought shelter at the lotus feet of th
e Lord, were unable to achieve the result they desired.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.29 - In human society there are various activities performed for the protection of one's wealth and life by one's words, one's mind and one's actions, but they are all performed for one's perso
nal or extended sense gratification with reference to the body. All these activities are baffled because of being separate from devotional service. But when the same activities are performed for the satisfaction of the Lord, the beneficial results are dis
tributed to everyone, just as water poured on the root of a tree is distributed throughout the entire tree.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  The Lord Incarnates as Mohin\'e9-M\'fcrti
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Thereafter, the demons became inimical toward one another. Throwing and snatching the container of nectar, they 
gave up their friendly relationship. Meanwhile, they saw a very beautiful young woman coming forward toward them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.2 - Upon seeing the beautiful woman, the demons said, "Alas, how wonderful is Her beauty, how wonderful the luster of Her body, and ho
w wonderful the beauty of Her youthful age!" Speaking in this way, they quickly approached Her, full of lusty desires to enjoy Her, and began to inquire from Her in many ways.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.3 - O wonderfully beautiful girl, You have such nice eyes, resembling th
e petals of a lotus flower. Who are You? Where do You come from? What is Your purpose in coming here, and to whom do You belong? O You whose thighs are extraordinarily beautiful, our minds are becoming agitated simply because of seeing You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.4 - What to speak of human beings, even the demigods, demons, Siddhas, Gandharvas, C\'e4ra\'ebas and the various directors of the universe, the Praj\'e4
patis, have never touched You before. It is not that we are unable to understand Your identity.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.5 - O beautiful girl with beautiful eyebrows, certainly Providence, by His causeless mercy, has sent You to please the senses and minds of all of us. Is this not a fact?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.6 - We are now all engaged in enmity among ourselves because of this one subject matter-the co
ntainer of nectar. Although we have been born in the same family, we are becoming increasingly inimical. O thin-waisted woman, who are so beautiful in Your prestigious position, we therefore request You to favor us by settling our dispute.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.7 - All of us, both demons and demigods, have been born of the same father, Ka\'e7
yapa, and thus we are related as brothers. But now we are exhibiting our personal prowess in dissension. Therefore we request You to settle our dispute and divide the nectar equally among us.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.8 - Having thus been requested by the demons, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who had assumed the form of a beautiful woman, began to smile. Looking at them with attractive feminine gestures, She spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.9 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, in the form of Mohin\'e9, told the demons: O sons of Ka\'e7
yapa Muni, I am only a prostitute. Mow is it that you have so much faith in Me? A learned person never puts his faith in a woman.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.10 - O demons, as monkeys, jackals and d
ogs are unsteady in their sexual relationships and want newer and newer friends every day, women who live independently seek new friends daily. Friendship with such a woman is never permanent. This is the opinion of learned scholars.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.11 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After the demons heard the words of Mohin\'e9-m\'fc
rti, who had spoken as if jokingly, they were all very confident. They laughed with gravity, and ultimately they delivered the container of nectar into Her hands.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.12 - Thereafter, 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead, having taken possession of the container of nectar, smiled slightly and spoke in attractive words. She said: My dear demons, if you accept whatever I may do, whether honest or dishonest, then I can take responsibility f
or dividing the nectar among you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.13 - The chiefs of the demons were not very expert in deciding things. Upon hearing the sweet words of Mohin\'e9-m\'fcrti, they immediately assented. "Yes," they answered. "What You have said is all right." Thus the demon
s agreed to accept Her decision.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.14-15 - The demigods and demons then observed a fast. After bathing, they offered clarified butter and oblations into the fire and gave charity to the cows and to the br\'e4hma\'ebas and members of the other orders of soc
iety, namely the k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas and \'e7\'fcdras, who were all rewarded as they deserved. Thereafter, the demigods and demons performed ritualistic ceremonies under the directions of the br\'e4hma\'eb
as. Then they dressed themselves with new garments according to their own choice, decorated their bodies with ornaments, and sat facing east on seats made of ku\'e7a grass.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.16-17 - O King, as the demigods and demons sat facing east in an arena fully decorated with flower garlands and lamps and fragrant with the sm
oke of incense, that woman, dressed in a most beautiful sari, Her ankle bells tinkling, entered the arena, walking very slowly because of Her big, low hips. Her eyes were restless due to youthful pride, Her breasts were like water jugs, Her thighs resembl
ed the trunks of elephants, and She carried a waterpot in Her hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.18 - Her attractive nose and cheeks and Her ears, adorned with golden earrings, made Her face very beautiful. As She moved, Her sari's border on Her breasts moved slightly aside. Wh
en the demigods and demons saw these beautiful features of Mohin\'e9-m\'fcrti, who was glancing at them and slightly smiling, they were all completely enchanted.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.19 - Demons are by nature crooked like snakes. Therefore, to distribute a share of the necta
r to them was not at all feasible, since this would be as dangerous as supplying milk to a snake. Considering this, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who never falls down, did not deliver a share of nectar to the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.20 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead as Mohin\'e9-m\'fcrti, the master of the universe, arranged separate lines of sitting places and seated the demigods and demons according to their positions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.21 - Taking the container of nectar in Her hands, She first approached the demons
, satisfied them with sweet words and thus cheated them of their share of the nectar. Then She administered the nectar to the demigods, who were sitting at a distant place, to make them free from invalidity, old age and death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.22 - O King, since th
e demons had promised to accept whatever the woman did, whether just or unjust, now, to keep this promise, to show their equilibrium and to save themselves from fighting with a woman, they remained silent.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.23 - The demons had developed affection for Mohin\'e9-m\'fc
rti and a kind of faith in Her, and they were afraid of disturbing their relationship. Therefore they showed respect and honor to Her words and did not say anything that might disturb their friendship with Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.24 - R\'e4hu, the demon who c
auses eclipses of the sun and moon, covered himself with the dress of a demigod and thus entered the assembly of the demigods and drank nectar without being detected by anyone, even by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The moon and the sun, however, bec
ause of permanent animosity toward R\'e4hu, understood the situation. Thus R\'e4hu was detected.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.25 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, using His disc, which was sharp like a razor, at once cut off R\'e4hu's head. When R\'e4hu's head was severed from hi
s body, the body, being untouched by the nectar, could not survive.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.26 - R\'e4hu's head, however, having been touched by the nectar, became immortal. Thus Lord Brahm\'e4 accepted R\'e4hu's head as one of the planets. Since R\'e4hu is an eternal enemy of the mo
on and the sun, he always tries to attack them on the nights of the full moon and the dark moon.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.27 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the best friend and well-wisher of the three worlds. Thus when the demigods had almost finished drinking the
 nectar, the Lord, in the presence of all the demons, disclosed His original form.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.28 - The place, the time, the cause, the purpose, the activity and the ambition were all the same for both the demigods and the demons, but the demigods achieved one
 result and the demons another. Because the demigods are always under the shelter of the dust of the Lord's lotus feet, they could very easily drink the nectar and get its result. The demons, however, not having sought shelter at the lotus feet of the Lor
d, were unable to achieve the result they desired.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.9.29 - In human society there are various activities performed for the protection of one's wealth and life by one's words, one's mind and one's actions, but they are all performed for one's personal o
r extended sense gratification with reference to the body. All these activities are baffled because of being separate from devotional service. But when the same activities are performed for the satisfaction of the Lord, the beneficial results are distribu
ted to everyone, just as water poured on the root of a tree is distributed throughout the entire tree.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-29
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, the demons and Daityas all engaged with full attention and effort in churning the ocean, but because they were not devotees of V\'e4sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, they were not able to drink the nectar.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.2 - O King, after the Supreme Personality of Godhead had brought to completion the affairs of churning the ocean and feeding the nectar
 to the demigods, who are His dear devotees, He left the presence of them all and was carried by Garu\'f2a to His own abode.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.3 - Seeing the victory of the demigods, the demons became intolerant of their superior opulence. Thus they began to march toward the demigods with raised weapons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.4 - Thereafter, being enlivened because of drinking the nectar, the demigods, who are always at the shelter of the lotus feet of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, used their various weapons to counterattack the demons in a fighting s
pirit.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.5 - O King, a fierce battle on the beach of the ocean of milk ensued between the demigods and the demons. The fighting was so terrible that simply hearing about it would make the hair on one's body stand on end.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.6 - Both parties in that fight were extremely angry at heart, and in enmity they beat one another with swords, arrows and varieties of other weapons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.7 - The sounds of the conchshells, bugles, drums, bher\'e9s and \'f2amar\'e9s [kettledrums], as well as the sounds made by the elephants, horses and soldiers, who were both on chariots and on foot, were tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.8 - On that battlefield, the charioteers fought with the opposing charioteers, the infantry soldiers with the opposing infantry, the soldiers on horseback wi
th the opposing soldiers on horseback, and the soldiers on the backs of elephants with the enemy soldiers on elephants. In this way, the fighting took place between equals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.9 - Some soldiers fought on the backs of camels, some on the backs of elephants, some on asses, some on white-faced and red-faced monkeys, some on tigers and some on lions. In this way, they all engaged in fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.10-12 - O King, some soldiers fought on the backs of vultures, eagles, ducks, hawks and bh\'e4sa birds. Some fought on the backs of timi\'ecgilas, which can devour huge whales, some on the backs of \'e7
arabhas, and some on buffalo, rhinoceroses, cows, bulls, jungle cows and aru\'ebas. Others fought on the backs of jackals, rats, lizards, rabbits, human beings, goats, bla
ck deer, swans and boars. In this way, mounted on animals of the water, land and sky, including animals with deformed bodies, both armies faced each other and went forward.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.13-15 - O King, O descendant of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u, the soldiers of both the d
emigods and demons were decorated by canopies, colorful flags, and umbrellas with handles made of valuable jewels and pearls. They were further decorated by fans made of peacock feathers and by other fans also. The soldiers, their upper and lower garments
 waving in the breeze, naturally looked very beautiful, and in the light of the glittering sunshine their shields, ornaments and sharp, clean weapons appeared dazzling. Thus the ranks of soldiers seemed like two oceans with bands of aquatics.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.16-18 - For that battle the most celebrated commander in chief, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, son of Virocana, was seated on a wonderful airplane named Vaih\'e4
yasa. O King, this beautifully decorated airplane had been manufactured by the demon Maya and was equipped with weapons
 for all types of combat. It was inconceivable and indescribable. Indeed, it was sometimes visible and sometimes not. Seated in this airplane under a beautiful protective umbrella and being fanned by the best of c\'e4maras, Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bali, surrounded by his captains and commanders, appeared just like the moon rising in the evening, illuminating all directions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.19-24 - Surrounding Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali on all sides were the commanders and captains of the demons, sitting on their respective chariots. Among them were the following demons: Namuci, \'c7ambara, B\'e4\'eb
a, Vipracitti, Ayomukha, Dvim\'fcrdh\'e4, K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Praheti, Heti, Ilvala, \'c7akuni, Bh\'fctasant\'e4pa, Vajrada\'e0\'f1\'f6ra, Virocana, Hayagr\'e9va, \'c7a\'ecku\'e7ir\'e4, Kapila, Meghadundubhi, T\'e4raka, Cakrad\'e5k, \'c7umbha, Ni\'e7
umbha, Jambha, Utkala, Ari\'f1\'f6a, Ari\'f1\'f6anemi, Tripur\'e4dhipa, Maya, the sons of Puloma, the K\'e4leyas and Niv\'e4
takavaca. All of these demons had been deprived of their share of the nectar and had shared merely in the labor of churning the ocean. Now, they fought against the demigods
, and to encourage their armies, they made a tumultuous sound like the roaring of lions and blew loudly on conchshells. Balabhit, Lord Indra, upon seeing this situation of his ferocious rivals, became extremely angry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.25 - Sitting on Air\'e4vata, an elephant who can go anywhere and who holds water and wine in reserve for showering, Lord Indra looked just like the sun rising from Udayagiri, where there are reservoirs of water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.26 - Surrounding Lord Indra, King of heaven, were the demigods, seated on various types of vehicles and decorated with flags and weapons. Present among them were V\'e4yu, Agni, Varu\'eb
a and other rulers of various planets, along with their associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.27 - The demigods and demons came before each other and reproached one another with words piercing to the heart. Then they drew near and began fighting face to face in pairs.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.28 - O King, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali fought with Indra, K\'e4rttikeya with T\'e4raka, Varu\'eba with Heti, and Mitra with Praheti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.29 - Yamar\'e4ja fought with K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4 with Maya D\'e4nava, Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4 with \'c7ambara, and the sun-god with Virocana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.30-31 - The demigod Apar\'e4jita fought with Namuci, and the two A\'e7vin\'e9-kum\'e4ra brothers fought with V\'e5\'f1aparv\'e4. The sun-god fought with the one hundred sons of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, headed by B\'e4\'eb
a, and the moon-god fought with R\'e4hu. The demigod controlling air fought with Puloma, and \'c7umbha and Ni\'e7umbha fought the supremely powerful material energy, Durg\'e4dev\'e9, who is called Bhadra K\'e4l\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.32-34 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, suppressor of enemies [Arindama], Lord \'c7iva fought with Jambha, and Vibh\'e4vasu fought with Mahi\'f1\'e4sura. Ilvala, along with his brother V\'e4t\'e4
pi, fought the sons of Lord Brahm\'e4. Durmar\'f1a fought with Cupid, the demon Utkala with the M\'e4t\'e5k\'e4 demigoddesses, B\'e5haspati with \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, and \'c7anai\'e7cara [Saturn] with Narak\'e4sura. The Maruts fought Niv\'e4
takavaca, the Vasus fought the K\'e4lakeya demons, the Vi\'e7vedeva demigods fought the Pauloma demons, and the Rudras fought the Krodhava\'e7a demons, who were victims of anger.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.10.35 - All of these demigods and demons assembled on the battlefield with a fighting spirit and attacked one another with great strength. All of them desiring victory, they fought in pairs, hitting one another severely with sharpened arro
ws, swords and lances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.36 - They severed one another's heads, using weapons like bhu\'e7u\'eb\'f2is, cakras, clubs, \'e5\'f1\'f6is, pa\'f6\'f6i\'e7as, \'e7aktis, ulmukas, pr\'e4sas, para\'e7vadhas, nistri\'e0\'e7
as, lances, parighas, mudgaras and bhindip\'e4las.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.37 - The elephants, 
horses, chariots, charioteers, infantry soldiers and various kinds of carriers, along with their riders, were slashed to pieces. The arms, thighs, necks and legs of the soldiers were severed, and their flags, bows, armor and ornaments were torn apart.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 
8.10.38 - Because of the impact on the ground of the legs of the demons and demigods and the wheels of the chariots, particles of dust flew violently into the sky and made a dust cloud that covered all directions of outer space, as far as the sun. But whe
n the particles of dust were followed by drops of blood being sprinkled all over space, the dust cloud could no longer float in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.39 - In the course of the battle, the warfield became strewn with the severed heads of heroes, their eyes still
 staring and their teeth still pressed against their lips in anger. Helmets and earrings were scattered from these severed heads. Similarly, many arms, decorated with ornaments and clutching various weapons, were strewn here and there, as were many legs a
nd thighs, which resembled the trunks of elephants.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.40 - Many headless trunks were generated on that battlefield. With weapons in their arms, those ghostly trunks, which could see with the eyes in the fallen heads, attacked the enemy soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.41 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali then attacked Indra with ten arrows and attacked Air\'e4vata, Indra's carrier elephant, with three arrows. With four arrows he attacked the four horsemen guarding Air\'e4
vata's legs, and with one arrow he attacked the driver of the elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.42 - Before Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's arrows could reach him, Indra, King of heaven, who is expert in dealing with arrows, smiled and counteracted the arrows with arrows of another type, known as bhalla, which were extremely sharp.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.43 - When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw the expert military activities of Indra, he could not restrain his anger. Thus he took up another weapon, known as \'e7
akti, which blazed like a great firebrand. But Indra cut that weapon to pieces while it was still in Bali's hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.44 - Thereafter, one by one, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja used a lance, pr\'e4sa, tomara, \'e5\'f1\'f6is and other weapons, but whatever weapons he took up, Indra immediately cut them to pieces.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.45 - My dear King, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja then disappeared and resorted to demoniac illusions. A giant mountain, generated from illusion, then appeared above the heads of the demigod soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.46 - From that mountain fell trees blazing in a forest fire. Chips of stone, with sharp edges like picks, also fell and smashed the heads of the demigod soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.47 - Scorpions, large snakes and many other poisonous animals, as well as lions, tigers, boars and great elephants, all began falling upon the demigod soldiers, crushing everything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.48 - O my King, many hundreds of male and female carnivorous demons, completely naked and carrying tridents in their hands, then appeared, crying the slogans "Cut them to pieces! Pierce them!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.49 - Fierce clouds, harassed by strong winds, then appeared in the sky. Rumbling very gravely with the sound of thunder, they began to shower live coals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.50 - A great devastating fire created by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja began burning all the soldiers of the demigods. This fire, accompanied by blasting winds, seemed as terrible as the S\'e4\'e0vartaka f
ire, which appears at the time of dissolution.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.51 - Thereafter, whirlpools and sea waves, agitated by fierce blasts of wind, appeared everywhere, before everyone's vision, in a furious flood.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.52 - While this magical atmosphere in the fight was being created by the invisible demons, who were expert in such illusions, the soldiers of the demigods became morose.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.53 - O King, when the demigods could find no way to counteract the activities of the demons, they wholeheartedly meditated upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the creator of the universe, who then immediately appeared.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.54 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose eyes resemble the petals of a newly blossomed lotus, sat on the back of Garu\'f2a, spreading His lotus feet over Garu\'f2
a's shoulders. Dressed in yellow, decorated by the Kaustubha gem and the goddess of fortune, and wearing an invaluable helmet and earrings, the Supreme Lord, holding various weapons in His eight hands, became visible to the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.
10.55 - As the dangers of a dream cease when the dreamer awakens, the illusions created by the jugglery of the demons were vanquished by the transcendental prowess of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as soon as He entered the battlefield. Indeed, simply
 by remembrance of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one becomes free from all dangers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.56 - O King, when the demon K\'e4lanemi, who was carried by a lion, saw that the Supreme Personality of Godhead, carried by Garu\'f2a, was on the battlefield, the d
emon immediately took his trident, whirled it and discharged it at Garu\'f2a's head. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, the master of the three worlds, immediately caught the trident, and with the very same weapon he killed the enemy K\'e4
lanemi, along with his carrier, the lion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.57 - Thereafter, two very powerful demons named M\'e4l\'e9 and Sum\'e4l\'e9 were killed by the Supreme Lord, who severed their heads with His disc. Then M\'e4lyav\'e4
n, another demon, attacked the Lord. With his sharp club, the demon, who was roaring like a lion, attacked Garu\'f2
a, the lord of the birds, who are born from eggs. But the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the original person, used His disc to cut off the head of that enemy also.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  10. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, the de
mons and Daityas all engaged with full attention and effort in churning the ocean, but because they were not devotees of V\'e4sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, they were not able to drink the nectar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.2 - O King, after the Supreme Per
sonality of Godhead had brought to completion the affairs of churning the ocean and feeding the nectar to the demigods, who are His dear devotees, He left the presence of them all and was carried by Garu\'f2a to His own abode.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.3 - Seeing the victory of the demigods, the demons became intolerant of their superior opulence. Thus they began to march toward the demigods with raised weapons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.4 - Thereafter, being enlivened because of drinking the nectar, the demigods, who are always at the shelter of the lotus feet of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, used their various weapons to counterattack the demons in a fighting spirit.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.5 - O King, a fierce battle on the beach of the ocean of milk ensued between the demigods and the demons. The fighting was so terrible that simply hearing about it would make the hair on one's body stand on end.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.6 - Both parties in that fight were extremely angry at heart, and in enmity they beat one another with swords, arrows and varieties of other weapons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.7 - The sounds of the conchshells, bugles, drums, bher\'e9s and \'f2amar\'e9s [kettledrums], as well as the sounds made by the elephants, horses and soldiers, who were both on chariots and on foot, were tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.8 - On that battlefield, the charioteers fought with th
e opposing charioteers, the infantry soldiers with the opposing infantry, the soldiers on horseback with the opposing soldiers on horseback, and the soldiers on the backs of elephants with the enemy soldiers on elephants. In this way, the fighting took pl
ace between equals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.9 - Some soldiers fought on the backs of camels, some on the backs of elephants, some on asses, some on white-faced and red-faced monkeys, some on tigers and some on lions. In this way, they all engaged in fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.10-12 - O King, some soldiers fought on the backs of vultures, eagles, ducks, hawks and bh\'e4sa birds. Some fought on the backs of timi\'ecgilas, which can devour huge whales, some on the backs of \'e7
arabhas, and some on buffalo, rhinoceroses, cows, bulls, jungle cows and aru\'eb
as. Others fought on the backs of jackals, rats, lizards, rabbits, human beings, goats, black deer, swans and boars. In this way, mounted on animals of the water, land and sky, including animals with deformed bodies, both armies faced each other
 and went forward.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.13-15 - O King, O descendant of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2
u, the soldiers of both the demigods and demons were decorated by canopies, colorful flags, and umbrellas with handles made of valuable jewels and pearls. They were further decorated 
by fans made of peacock feathers and by other fans also. The soldiers, their upper and lower garments waving in the breeze, naturally looked very beautiful, and in the light of the glittering sunshine their shields, ornaments and sharp, clean weapons appe
ared dazzling. Thus the ranks of soldiers seemed like two oceans with bands of aquatics.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.16-18 - For that battle the most celebrated commander in chief, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, son of Virocana, was seated on a wonderful airplane named Vaih\'e4yasa. O King, thi
s beautifully decorated airplane had been manufactured by the demon Maya and was equipped with weapons for all types of combat. It was inconceivable and indescribable. Indeed, it was sometimes visible and sometimes not. Seated in this airplane under a bea
utiful protective umbrella and being fanned by the best of c\'e4maras, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, surrounded by his captains and commanders, appeared just like the moon rising in the evening, illuminating all directions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.19-24 - Surrounding Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali on all sides were the commanders and captains of the demons, sitting on their respective chariots. Among them were the following demons: Namuci, \'c7ambara, B\'e4\'eb
a, Vipracitti, Ayomukha, Dvim\'fcrdh\'e4, K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Praheti, Heti, Ilvala, \'c7akuni, Bh\'fctasant\'e4pa, Vajrada\'e0\'f1\'f6ra, Virocana, Hayagr\'e9va, \'c7a\'ecku\'e7ir\'e4, Kapila, Meghadundubhi, T\'e4raka, Cakrad\'e5k, \'c7umbha, Ni\'e7
umbha, Jambha, Utkala, Ari\'f1\'f6a, Ari\'f1\'f6anemi, Tripur\'e4dhipa, Maya, the sons of Puloma, the K\'e4leyas and Niv\'e4takavaca. All of these demons had been deprived of their share of the 
nectar and had shared merely in the labor of churning the ocean. Now, they fought against the demigods, and to encourage their armies, they made a tumultuous sound like the roaring of lions and blew loudly on conchshells. Balabhit, Lord Indra, upon seeing
 this situation of his ferocious rivals, became extremely angry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.25 - Sitting on Air\'e4vata, an elephant who can go anywhere and who holds water and wine in reserve for showering, Lord Indra looked just like the sun rising from Udayagiri, where there are reservoirs of water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.26 - Surrounding Lord Indra, King of heaven, were the demigods, seated on various types of vehicles and decorated with flags and weapons. Present among them were V\'e4yu, Agni, Varu\'eb
a and other rulers of various planets, along with their associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.27 - The demigods and demons came before each other and reproached one another with words piercing to the heart. Then they drew near and began fighting face to face in pairs.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.28 - O King, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali fought with Indra, K\'e4rttikeya with T\'e4raka, Varu\'eba with Heti, and Mitra with Praheti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.29 - Yamar\'e4ja fought with K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4 with Maya D\'e4nava, Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4 with \'c7ambara, and the sun-god with Virocana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.30-31 - The demigod Apar\'e4jita fought with Namuci, and the two A\'e7vin\'e9-kum\'e4ra brothers fought with V\'e5\'f1aparv\'e4. The sun-god fought with the one hundred sons of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, headed by B\'e4\'eb
a, and the moon-god fought with R\'e4hu. The demigod controlling air fought with Puloma, and \'c7umbha and Ni\'e7umbha fought the supremely powerful material energy, Durg\'e4dev\'e9, who is called Bhadra K\'e4l\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.32-34 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, suppressor of enemies [Arindama], Lord \'c7iva fought with Jambha, and Vibh\'e4vasu fought with Mahi\'f1\'e4sura. Ilvala, along with his brother V\'e4t\'e4pi,
 fought the sons of Lord Brahm\'e4. Durmar\'f1a fought with Cupid, the demon Utkala with the M\'e4t\'e5k\'e4 demigoddesses, B\'e5haspati with \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, and \'c7anai\'e7cara [Saturn] with Narak\'e4sura. The Maruts fought Niv\'e4
takavaca, the Vasus fought the K\'e4lakeya demons, the Vi\'e7vedeva demigods fought the Pauloma demons, and the Rudras fought the Krodhava\'e7a demons, who were victims of anger.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.35 - All of these demigods and demons assembled on the battlefield with a fighting spirit and attacked one another with great strength
. All of them desiring victory, they fought in pairs, hitting one another severely with sharpened arrows, swords and lances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.36 - They severed one another's heads, using weapons like bhu\'e7u\'eb\'f2is, cakras, clubs, \'e5\'f1\'f6is, pa\'f6\'f6i\'e7as, \'e7aktis, ulmukas, pr\'e4sas, para\'e7vadhas, nistri\'e0\'e7
as, lances, parighas, mudgaras and bhindip\'e4las.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.37 - The elephants, horses, chariots, charioteers, infantry soldiers and various kinds of carriers, along with their riders, were slashed to pieces. The arms, thighs, necks a
nd legs of the soldiers were severed, and their flags, bows, armor and ornaments were torn apart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.38 - Because of the impact on the ground of the legs of the demons and demigods and the wheels of the chariots, particles of dust flew violently into
 the sky and made a dust cloud that covered all directions of outer space, as far as the sun. But when the particles of dust were followed by drops of blood being sprinkled all over space, the dust cloud could no longer float in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.39 - In t
he course of the battle, the warfield became strewn with the severed heads of heroes, their eyes still staring and their teeth still pressed against their lips in anger. Helmets and earrings were scattered from these severed heads. Similarly, many arms, d
ecorated with ornaments and clutching various weapons, were strewn here and there, as were many legs and thighs, which resembled the trunks of elephants.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.40 - Many headless trunks were generated on that battlefield. With weapons in their arms, those ghostly trunks, which could see with the eyes in the fallen heads, attacked the enemy soldiers.
