\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.7 - The sounds of the conchshells, bugles, drums, bher\'e9s and \'f2amar\'e9s [kettledrums], as well as the sounds made by the elephants, horses and soldiers, who were both on chariots and on foot, were tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.8 - On that battlefield, the charioteers fought with the opposing charioteers, the infantry soldiers with the opposing infantry, the soldiers on horseback with the opposing soldiers on horseback, and the soldi
ers on the backs of elephants with the enemy soldiers on elephants. In this way, the fighting took place between equals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.9 - Some soldiers fought on the backs of camels, some on the backs of elephants, some on asses, some on white-faced and red-faced monkeys, some on tigers and some on lions. In this way, they all engaged in fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.10-12 - O King, some soldiers fought on the backs of vultures, eagles, ducks, hawks and bh\'e4sa birds. Some fought on the backs of timi\'ecgilas, which can devour huge whales, some on the backs of \'e7
arabhas, and some on buffalo, rhinoceroses, cows, bulls, jungle cows and aru\'ebas. Others fought on the backs of jackals, rats, lizards, rabbits, human beings, goats, black deer, swans and boars. In this way, mounted on an
imals of the water, land and sky, including animals with deformed bodies, both armies faced each other and went forward.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.13-15 - O King, O descendant of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja P\'e4\'eb\'f2u, the soldiers of both the demigods and demons were decorated by canopies, color
ful flags, and umbrellas with handles made of valuable jewels and pearls. They were further decorated by fans made of peacock feathers and by other fans also. The soldiers, their upper and lower garments waving in the breeze, naturally looked very beautif
ul, and in the light of the glittering sunshine their shields, ornaments and sharp, clean weapons appeared dazzling. Thus the ranks of soldiers seemed like two oceans with bands of aquatics.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.16-18 - For that battle the most celebrated commander in chief, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, son of Virocana, was seated on a wonderful airplane named Vaih\'e4
yasa. O King, this beautifully decorated airplane had been manufactured by the demon Maya and was equipped with weapons for all types of combat. It was inconceivable and i
ndescribable. Indeed, it was sometimes visible and sometimes not. Seated in this airplane under a beautiful protective umbrella and being fanned by the best of c\'e4maras, Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bali, surrounded by his captains and commanders, appeared just like the moon rising in the evening, illuminating all directions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.19-24 - Surrounding Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali on all sides were the commanders and captains of the demons, sitting on their respective chariots. Among them were the following demons: Namuci, \'c7ambara, B\'e4\'eba, Vi
pracitti, Ayomukha, Dvim\'fcrdh\'e4, K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Praheti, Heti, Ilvala, \'c7akuni, Bh\'fctasant\'e4pa, Vajrada\'e0\'f1\'f6ra, Virocana, Hayagr\'e9va, \'c7a\'ecku\'e7ir\'e4, Kapila, Meghadundubhi, T\'e4raka, Cakrad\'e5k, \'c7umbha, Ni\'e7
umbha, Jambha, Utkala, Ari\'f1\'f6a, Ari\'f1\'f6anemi, Tripur\'e4dhipa, Maya, the sons of Puloma, the K\'e4leyas and Niv\'e4
takavaca. All of these demons had been deprived of their share of the nectar and had shared merely in the labor of churning the ocean. Now, they fought against the demigods, and to encourage their armies, they made a tumultu
ous sound like the roaring of lions and blew loudly on conchshells. Balabhit, Lord Indra, upon seeing this situation of his ferocious rivals, became extremely angry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.25 - Sitting on Air\'e4vata, an elephant who can go anywhere and who holds water and wine in reserve for showering, Lord Indra looked just like the sun rising from Udayagiri, where there are reservoirs of water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.26 - Surrounding Lord Indra, King of heaven, were the demigods, seated on various types of vehicles and decorated with flags and weapons. Present among them were V\'e4yu, Agni, Varu\'eb
a and other rulers of various planets, along with their associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.27 - The demigods and demons came before each other and reproached one another with words piercing to the heart. Then they drew near and began fighting face to face in pairs.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.28 - O King, Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali fought with Indra, K\'e4rttikeya with T\'e4raka, Varu\'eba with Heti, and Mitra with Praheti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.29 - Yamar\'e4ja fought with K\'e4lan\'e4bha, Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4 with Maya D\'e4nava, Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4 with \'c7ambara, and the sun-god with Virocana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.30-31 - The demigod Apar\'e4jita fought with Namuci, and the two A\'e7vin\'e9-kum\'e4ra brothers fought with V\'e5\'f1aparv\'e4. The sun-god fought with the one hundred sons of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, headed by B\'e4\'eb
a, and the moon-god fought with R\'e4hu. The demigod controlling air fought with Puloma, and \'c7umbha and Ni\'e7umbha fought the supremely powerful material energy, Durg\'e4dev\'e9, who is called Bhadra K\'e4l\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.32-34 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, suppressor of enemies [Arindama], Lord \'c7iva fought with Jambha, and Vibh\'e4vasu fought with Mahi\'f1\'e4sura. Ilvala, along with his brother V\'e4t\'e4
pi, fought the sons of Lord Brahm\'e4. Durmar\'f1a fought with Cupid, the demon Utkala with the M\'e4t\'e5k\'e4 demigoddesses, B\'e5haspati with \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, and \'c7anai\'e7cara [Saturn] with Narak\'e4sura. The Maruts fought Niv\'e4
takavaca, the Vasus fought the K\'e4lakeya demons, the Vi\'e7vedeva demigods fought the Pauloma demons, and the Rudras fought the Krodhava\'e7a demons, who were victims of anger.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.35 - All of these demigods and d
emons assembled on the battlefield with a fighting spirit and attacked one another with great strength. All of them desiring victory, they fought in pairs, hitting one another severely with sharpened arrows, swords and lances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.36 - They severed one another's heads, using weapons like bhu\'e7u\'eb\'f2is, cakras, clubs, \'e5\'f1\'f6is, pa\'f6\'f6i\'e7as, \'e7aktis, ulmukas, pr\'e4sas, para\'e7vadhas, nistri\'e0\'e7
as, lances, parighas, mudgaras and bhindip\'e4las.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.37 - The elephants, horses, chariots, charioteers, infantry soldiers and
 various kinds of carriers, along with their riders, were slashed to pieces. The arms, thighs, necks and legs of the soldiers were severed, and their flags, bows, armor and ornaments were torn apart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.38 - Because of the impact on the ground of the
 legs of the demons and demigods and the wheels of the chariots, particles of dust flew violently into the sky and made a dust cloud that covered all directions of outer space, as far as the sun. But when the particles of dust were followed by drops of bl
ood being sprinkled all over space, the dust cloud could no longer float in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.39 - In the course of the battle, the warfield became strewn with the severed heads of heroes, their eyes still staring and their teeth still pressed against their
 lips in anger. Helmets and earrings were scattered from these severed heads. Similarly, many arms, decorated with ornaments and clutching various weapons, were strewn here and there, as were many legs and thighs, which resembled the trunks of elephants.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.40 - Many headless trunks were generated on that battlefield. With weapons in their arms, those ghostly trunks, which could see with the eyes in the fallen heads, attacked the enemy soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.41 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali then attacked Indra with ten arrows and attacked Air\'e4vata, Indra's carrier elephant, with three arrows. With four arrows he attacked the four horsemen guarding Air\'e4
vata's legs, and with one arrow he attacked the driver of the elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.42 - Before Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's arrows coul
d reach him, Indra, King of heaven, who is expert in dealing with arrows, smiled and counteracted the arrows with arrows of another type, known as bhalla, which were extremely sharp.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.43 - When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw the expert military activities of Indra, he could not restrain his anger. Thus he took up another weapon, known as \'e7
akti, which blazed like a great firebrand. But Indra cut that weapon to pieces while it was still in Bali's hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.44 - Thereafter, one by one, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja used a lance, pr\'e4sa, tomara, \'e5\'f1\'f6is and other weapons, but whatever weapons he took up, Indra immediately cut them to pieces.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.45 - My dear King, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja then disappeared and resorted to demoniac illusions. A giant mountain, generated from illusion, then appeared above the heads of the demigod soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.46 - From that mountain fell trees blazing in a forest fire. Chips of stone, with sharp edges like picks, also fell and smashed the heads of the demigod soldiers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.47 - Scorpions, large snakes and many other poisonous animals, as well as lions, tigers, boars and great elephants, all began falling upon the demigod soldiers, crushing everything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.48 - O my King, many hundreds of male and female carnivorous demons, completely naked and carrying tridents in their hands, then appeared, crying the slogans "Cut them to pieces! Pierce them!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.49 - Fierce clouds, harassed by strong winds, then appeared in the sky. Rumbling very gravely with the sound of thunder, they began to shower live coals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.50 - A great devastating fire created by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja began burning all the soldiers of the demigods. This fire, accompanied by blasting winds, seemed as terrible as the S\'e4\'e0
vartaka fire, which appears at the time of dissolution.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.51 - Thereafter, whirlpools and sea waves, agitated by fierce blasts of wind, appeared everywhere, before everyone's vision, in a furious flood.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.52 - While this magical atmosphere in the fight was being created by the invisible demons, who were expert in such illusions, the soldiers of the demigods became morose.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.53 - O King, when the demigods could find no way to counteract the activities of the demons, they wholeheartedly meditated upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the creator of the universe, who then immediately appeared.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.54 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose eyes resemble the petals of a newly blossomed lotus, sat on the back of Garu\'f2a, spreading His lotus feet over Garu\'f2a's shoulders. Dressed in yellow, de
corated by the Kaustubha gem and the goddess of fortune, and wearing an invaluable helmet and earrings, the Supreme Lord, holding various weapons in His eight hands, became visible to the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.55 - As the dangers of a dream cease when the dre
amer awakens, the illusions created by the jugglery of the demons were vanquished by the transcendental prowess of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as soon as He entered the battlefield. Indeed, simply by remembrance of the Supreme Personality of Godhea
d, one becomes free from all dangers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.56 - O King, when the demon K\'e4lanemi, who was carried by a lion, saw that the Supreme Personality of Godhead, carried by Garu\'f2a, was on the battlefield, the demon immediately took his trident, whirled it and di
scharged it at Garu\'f2a's head. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, the master of the three worlds, immediately caught the trident, and with the very same weapon he killed the enemy K\'e4lanemi, along with his carrier, the lion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.10.57 - Thereafter, two very powerful demons named M\'e4l\'e9 and Sum\'e4l\'e9 were killed by the Supreme Lord, who severed their heads with His disc. Then M\'e4lyav\'e4
n, another demon, attacked the Lord. With his sharp club, the demon, who was roaring like a lion, attacked Garu\'f2a, the lord o
f the birds, who are born from eggs. But the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the original person, used His disc to cut off the head of that enemy also.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-57
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Thereafter, by the supreme grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, \'c7r\'e9 Hari, all the demigods, headed by Indra and V\'e4
yu, were brought back to life. Being enlivened, the demigods began severely beating the very same demons who had defeated them before.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.2 - When the most powerful Indra became angry and took his thunderbolt in hand to kill Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali, the demons began lamenting, "Alas, alas!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.3 - Sober and tolerant and well equipped with paraphernalia for fighting, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja moved before Indra on the great battlefield. King Indra, who always carries the thunderbolt in his hand, rebuked Bali Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.4 - Indra said: O rascal, as a cheater sometimes binds the eyes of a child and takes away his possessions, you are trying to defeat us by displaying some mystic power, although yo
u know that we are the masters of all such mystic powers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.5 - Those fools and rascals who want to ascend to the upper planetary system by mystic power or mechanical means, or who endeavor to cross even the upper planets and achieve the spiritual w
orld or liberation, I cause to be sent to the lowest region of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.6 - Today, with my thunderbolt, which has hundreds of sharp edges, I, the same powerful person, shall sever your head from your body. Although you can produce so much jug
glery through illusion, you are endowed with a poor fund of knowledge. Now, try to exist on this battlefield with your relatives and friends.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.7 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja replied: All those present on this battlefield are certainly under the influence of ete
rnal time, and according to their prescribed activities, they are destined to receive fame, victory, defeat and death, one after another.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.8 - Seeing the movements of time, those who are cognizant of the real truth neither rejoice nor lament for di
fferent circumstances. Therefore, because you are jubilant due to your victory, you should be considered not very learned.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.9 - You demigods think that your own selves are the cause of your attaining fame and victory. Because of your ignorance, sai
ntly persons feel sorry for you. Therefore, although your words afflict the heart, we do not accept them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.10 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: After thus rebuking Indra, King of heaven, with sharp words, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who could subdue any other hero, drew back to his ear the arrows known as n\'e4r\'e4
cas and attacked Indra with these arrows. Then he again chastised Indra with strong words.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.11 - Since Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali's rebukes were truthful, King Indra did not at all become sorry, just as an elephant beaten by its driver's rod does not become agitated.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.12 - When Indra, the defeater of enemies, released his infallible thunderbolt scepter at Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja with a desire to kill him, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja indeed fell to the ground with his airplane, like a mou
ntain with its wings cut off.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.13 - When the demon Jambh\'e4sura saw that his friend Bali had fallen, he appeared before Indra, the enemy, just to serve Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja with friendly behavior.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.14 - The greatly powerful Jambh\'e4sura, carried by a lion, approached Indra and forcefully struck him on the shoulder with his club. He also struck Indra's elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.15 - Being beaten by Jambh\'e4sura's club, Indra's elephant was confused and aggrieved. Thus it touched its knees to the ground and fell unconscious.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.16 - Thereafter, M\'e4tali, Indra's chariot driver, brought Indra's chariot, which was drawn by one thousand horses. Indra then left his elephant and got onto the chariot.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.17 - Appreciating M\'e4tali's service, Jambh\'e4sura, the best of the demons, smiled. Nonetheless, he struck M\'e4tali in the battle with a trident of blazing fire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.18 - Although the pain was extremely severe, M\'e4tali tolerated it with great patience. Indra, however, became extremely angry at Jambh\'e4sura. He struck Jambh\'e4
sura with his thunderbolt and thus severed his head from his body.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.19 - When N\'e4rada \'c5\'f1i informed Jambh\'e4sura's friends and relatives that Jambh\'e4sura had been killed, the three demons named Namuci, Bala and P\'e4ka arrived on the battlefield in great haste.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.20 - Rebuking Indra with harsh, cruel words that were piercing to the heart, these demons showered him with arrows, just as torrents of rain wash a great mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.21 - Quickly handling the situation on the battlefield, the demon Bala put all of Indra's one thousand horses into tribulation by simultaneously piercing them all with an equal number of arrows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.22 - P\'e4ka, another demon, attacked both the chariot, with all its paraphernalia, and the chariot driver, M\'e4tali
, by fitting two hundred arrows to his bow and releasing them all simultaneously. This was indeed a wonderful act on the battlefield.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.23 - Then Namuci, another demon, attacked Indra and injured him with fifteen very powerful golden-feathered arrows, which roared like a cloud full of water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.24 - Other demons covered Indra, along with his chariot and chariot driver, with incessant showers of arrows, just as clouds cover the sun in the rainy season.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.25 - The demigods, being severely 
oppressed by their enemies and being unable to see Indra on the battlefield, were very anxious. Having no captain or leader, they began lamenting like traders in a wrecked vessel in the midst of the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.26 - Thereafter, Indra released himself f
rom the cage of the network of arrows. Appearing with his chariot, flag, horses and chariot driver and thus pleasing the sky, the earth and all directions, he shone effulgently like the sun at the end of night. Indra was bright and beautiful in the vision
 of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.27 - When Indra, who is known as Vajra-dhara, the carrier of the thunderbolt, saw his own soldiers so oppressed by the enemies on the battlefield, he became very angry. Thus he took up his thunderbolt to kill the enemies.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.28 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, King Indra used his thunderbolt to cut off the heads of both Bala and P\'e4
ka in the presence of all their relatives and followers. In this way he created a very fearful atmosphere on the battlefield.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.29 - O King, when Namuci, another demon, saw the killing of both Bala and P\'e4ka, he was full of grief and lamentation. Thus he angrily made a great attempt to kill Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.30 - Being angry and roaring like a lion, the demon Namuci took up a steel spear, which was bound with bell
s and decorated with ornaments of gold. He loudly cried, "Now you are killed!" Thus coming before Indra to kill him, Namuci released his weapon.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.31 - O King, when Indra, King of heaven, saw this very powerful spear falling toward the ground like a
 blazing meteor, he immediately cut it to pieces with his arrows. Then, being very angry, he struck Namuci's shoulder with his thunderbolt to cut off Namuci's head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.32 - Although King Indra hurled his thunderbolt at Namuci with great force, it could not even pierce his skin. It is very wonderful that the famed thunderbolt that had pierced the body of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura could not even slightly injure the skin of Namuci's neck.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.33 - When Indra saw the thunderbolt return from the enemy, he was very much afraid. He began to wonder whether this had happened because of some miraculous superior power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.34 - Indra thought: Formerly, when many mountains flying in the sky with wings would fall to the ground and kill people, I cut their wings with this same thunderbolt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.35 - V\'e5tr\'e4sura was the essence of the austerities undergone by Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4
, yet the thunderbolt killed him. Indeed, not only he but also many other stalwart heroes, whose very skin could not be injured even by all kinds of weapons, were killed by the same thunderbolt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.36 - But now, although the same thunderbolt has been released against a less important demon, it has been ineffectual. Therefore, although it was as good as a brahm\'e4stra, it has now become useless like an ordina
ry rod. I shall therefore hold it no longer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.37 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: While the morose Indra was lamenting in this way, an ominous, unembodied voice said from the sky, "This demon Namuci is not to be annihilated by anything dry or moist."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.38 - The voice also said, "O Indra, because I have given this demon the benediction that he will never be killed by any weapon that is dry or moist, you have to think of another way to kill him."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.39 - After hearing the ominous voice, Indra, with great attention, began to meditate on how to kill the demon. He then saw that foam would be the means, for it is neither moist nor dry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.40 - Thus Indra, King of heaven, severed Namuci's head with a weapon of foam, which was neither dry nor
 moist. Then all the sages satisfied Indra, the exalted personality, by showering flowers and garlands upon him, almost covering him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.41 - Vi\'e7v\'e4vasu and Par\'e4vasu, the two chiefs of the Gandharvas, sang in great happiness. The kettledrums of the demigods sounded, and the Apsar\'e4s danced in jubilation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.42 - V\'e4yu, Agni, Varu\'eba and other demigods began killing the demons who opposed them, just as lions kill deer in a forest.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
