\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.19 - When N\'e4rada \'c5\'f1i informed Jambh\'e4sura's friends and relatives that Jambh\'e4sura had been killed, the three demons named Namuci, Bala and P\'e4ka arrived on the battlefield in great haste.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.20 - Rebuking Indra with harsh, cruel words that were piercing to the heart, these demons showered him with arrows, just as torrents of rain wash a great mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.21 - Quickly handling the situation on the battlefield, the demon Bala put all of Indra's one thousand horses into tribulation by simultaneously piercing them all with an equal number of arrows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.22 - P\'e4ka, another demon, attacked both the chariot, with all its paraphernalia, and the chariot driver, M\'e4
tali, by fitting two hundred arrows to his bow and releasing them all simultaneously. This was indeed a wonderful act on the battlefield.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.23 - Then Namuci, another demon, attacked Indra and injured him with fifteen very powerful golden-feathered arrows, which roared like a cloud full of water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.24 - Other demons covered Indra, along with his chariot and chariot driver, with incessant showers of arrows, just as clouds cover the sun in the rainy season.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.25 - The demigods, being severely oppressed by their enemies and being unable to see Indra on the battlefield, were very anxious. Having no captain or leader, they began lamenting like tra
ders in a wrecked vessel in the midst of the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.26 - Thereafter, Indra released himself from the cage of the network of arrows. Appearing with his chariot, flag, horses and chariot driver and thus pleasing the sky, the earth and all directions
, he shone effulgently like the sun at the end of night. Indra was bright and beautiful in the vision of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.27 - When Indra, who is known as Vajra-dhara, the carrier of the thunderbolt, saw his own soldiers so oppressed by the enemies on the battlefield, he became very angry. Thus he took up his thunderbolt to kill the enemies.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.28 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, King Indra used his thunderbolt to cut off the heads of both Bala and P\'e4ka in the presence of all their relatives and followers. In thi
s way he created a very fearful atmosphere on the battlefield.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.29 - O King, when Namuci, another demon, saw the killing of both Bala and P\'e4ka, he was full of grief and lamentation. Thus he angrily made a great attempt to kill Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.30 - 
Being angry and roaring like a lion, the demon Namuci took up a steel spear, which was bound with bells and decorated with ornaments of gold. He loudly cried, "Now you are killed!" Thus coming before Indra to kill him, Namuci released his weapon.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.
31 - O King, when Indra, King of heaven, saw this very powerful spear falling toward the ground like a blazing meteor, he immediately cut it to pieces with his arrows. Then, being very angry, he struck Namuci's shoulder with his thunderbolt to cut off Nam
uci's head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.32 - Although King Indra hurled his thunderbolt at Namuci with great force, it could not even pierce his skin. It is very wonderful that the famed thunderbolt that had pierced the body of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura could not even slightly injure the skin of Namuci's neck.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.33 - When Indra saw the thunderbolt return from the enemy, he was very much afraid. He began to wonder whether this had happened because of some miraculous superior power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.34 - Indra thought: Formerly, when many mountains flying in the sky with wings would fall to the ground and kill people, I cut their wings with this same thunderbolt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.35 - V\'e5tr\'e4sura was the essence of the austerities undergone by Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4, yet the thunderbolt killed him. Indeed, not only he but
 also many other stalwart heroes, whose very skin could not be injured even by all kinds of weapons, were killed by the same thunderbolt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.36 - But now, although the same thunderbolt has been released against a less important demon, it has been ineffectual. Therefore, although it was as good as a brahm\'e4
stra, it has now become useless like an ordinary rod. I shall therefore hold it no longer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.37 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: While the morose Indra was lamenting in this way, an ominous, unembodied voice said from the sky, "This demon Namuci is not to be annihilated by anything dry or moist."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.38 - The voice also said, "O Indra, because I have given this demon the benediction that he will never be killed by any weapon that is dry or moist, you have to think of another way to kill him."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.39 - After hearing the ominous voice, Indra, with great attention, began to meditate on how to kill the demon. He then saw that foam would be the means, for it is neither moist nor dry.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.4
0 - Thus Indra, King of heaven, severed Namuci's head with a weapon of foam, which was neither dry nor moist. Then all the sages satisfied Indra, the exalted personality, by showering flowers and garlands upon him, almost covering him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.41 - Vi\'e7v\'e4vasu and Par\'e4vasu, the two chiefs of the Gandharvas, sang in great happiness. The kettledrums of the demigods sounded, and the Apsar\'e4s danced in jubilation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.42 - V\'e4yu, Agni, Varu\'eba and other demigods began killing the demons who opposed them, just as lions kill deer in a forest.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.43 - O King, when Lord Brahm\'e4 saw the imminent total annihilation of the demons, he sent a message with N\'e4rada, who went before the demigods to make them stop fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.44 - The great sage N\'e4rada said: All of you demigods are protected by the arms of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and by His grace you have gotten the nectar. By the grace of the goddess of fortune, you are glorious in every way. Therefore, please stop this fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.45 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Accepting the words of N\'e4rada, the demigods gave up their anger and stopped fighting. Being praised by their followers, they returned to their heavenly planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.46 - Following the order of N\'e4rada Muni, whatever demons remained on the battlefield took Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who was in a precarious condition, to the hill known as Astagiri.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.47 - There, on that hill, \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya brought to life all the dead demoniac soldiers who had not lost their heads, trunks and limbs. He achieved this by his own mantra, known as Sa\'e0j\'e9van\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.11.48 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was very experienced in universal affairs. When he regained his senses and memory by the grace of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, he could understand everything that had happened. Therefore, a
lthough he had been defeated, he did not lament.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-48
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.1-2 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, in the form of a woman, captivated the demons and enabled the demigods to drink the nectar. After hearing of these pastimes, Lord \'c7
iva, who is carried by a bull, went to the place where Madhus\'fcdana, the Lord, resides. Accompanied by his wife, Um\'e4, and surrounded by his companions, the ghosts, Lord \'c7iva went there to see the Lord's form as a woman.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.3 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead welcomed Lord \'c7iva and Um\'e4 with great respect, and after being seated comfortably, Lord \'c7iva duly worshiped the Lord and smilingly spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.4 - Lord Mah\'e4deva said: O chief demigod among the demigods, O all-pervading Lord,
 master of the universe, by Your energy You are transformed into the creation. You are the root and efficient cause of everything. You are not material. Indeed, You are the Supersoul or supreme living force of everything. Therefore, You are Parame\'e7
vara, the supreme controller of all controllers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.5 - The manifest, the unmanifest, false ego and the beginning, maintenance and annihilation of this cosmic manifestation all come from You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. But because You are the Absolu
te Truth, the supreme absolute spirit soul, the Supreme Brahman, such changes as birth, death and sustenance do not exist in You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.6 - Pure devotees or great saintly persons who desire to achieve the highest goal in life and who are completely free
 from all material desires for sense gratification engage constantly in the transcendental service of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.7 - My Lord, You are the Supreme Brahman, complete in everything. Being completely spiritual, You are eternal, free from the mat
erial modes of nature, and full of transcendental bliss. Indeed, for You there is no question of lamentation. Since You are the supreme cause, the cause of all causes, nothing can exist without You. Yet we are different from You in a relationship of cause
 
and effect, for in one sense the cause and effect are different. You are the original cause of creation, manifestation and annihilation, and You bestow benedictions upon all living entities. Everyone depends upon You for the results of his activities, but
 You are always independent.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.8 - My dear Lord, Your Lordship alone is the cause and the effect. Therefore, although You appear to be two, You are the absolute one. As there is no difference between the gold of a golden ornament and the gold in a mi
ne, there is no difference between cause and effect; both of them are the same. Only because of ignorance do people concoct differences and dualities. You are free from material contamination, and since the entire cosmos is caused by You and cannot exist 
without You, it is an effect of Your transcendental qualities. Thus the conception that Brahman is true and the world false cannot be maintained.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.9 - Those who are known as the impersonalist Ved\'e4ntists regard You as the impersonal Brahman. Others, known as the M\'e9m\'e4\'e0saka philosophers, regard You as religion. The S\'e4\'ec
khya philosophers regard You as the transcendental person who is beyond prak\'e5ti and puru\'f1a and who is the controller of even the demigods. The followers of the codes of devotional service known as the Pa\'efcar\'e4
tras regard You as being endowed with nine different potencies. And the Pata\'efjala philosophers, the followers of Pata\'efjali Muni, regard You as the supreme independent Personality of Godhead, who has no equal or superior.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.10 - O my Lord, I, who am considered to be the best of the demigods, and Lord Brahm\'e4 and the great \'e5\'f1is, headed by Mar\'e9
ci, are born of the mode of goodness. Nonetheless, we are bewildered by Your illusory energy and cannot understand what this creation is. Aside
 from us, what is to be said of others, like the demons and human beings, who are in the base modes of material nature [rajo-gu\'eba and tamo-gu\'eba]? How will they know You?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.11 - My Lord, You are the supreme knowledge personified. You know everything 
about this creation and its beginning, maintenance and annihilation, and You know all the endeavors made by the living entities, by which they are either implicated in this material world or liberated from it. As the air enters the vast sky and also enter
s the bodies of all moving and nonmoving entities, You are present everywhere, and therefore You are the knower of all.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.12 - My Lord, I have seen all kinds of incarnations You have exhibited by Your transcendental qualities, and now that You have appeared as a beautiful young woman, I wish to see that form of Your Lordship.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.13 - My Lord, we have come here desiring to see that form of Your Lordship which You showed to the demons to captivate them completely and in this way enable the demigods to drink nectar. I am very eager to see that form.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.14 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu was thus requested by Lord \'c7iva, who carries a trident in his hand, He smiled with gravity and replied to Lord \'c7iva as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.15 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: When the demons took away the jug of nectar, I assumed the form of a beautiful woman to bewilder them by directly cheating them and thus to act in the interest of the demigods.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.16 - O best of the demigods, I shall now show you My form that is very much appreciated by those who are lusty. Since you want to see that form, I shall reveal it in your presence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.17 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After speaking in this way, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu, immediately disappeared, and Lord \'c7iva remained there with Um\'e4
, looking for Him all around with moving eyes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.18 - Thereafter, in a nice forest nearby, full of trees with reddish-pink leaves and varieties of flowers, Lord \'c7iva saw a beautiful woma
n playing with a ball. Her hips were covered with a shining sari and ornamented with a belt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.19 - Because the ball was falling down and bouncing up, as She played with it Her breasts trembled, and because of the weight of those breasts and Her hea
vy flower garlands, Her waist appeared to be all but breaking at every step, as Her two soft feet, which were reddish like coral, moved here and there.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.20 - The woman's face was decorated by broad, beautiful, restless eyes, which moved as the ball
 bounced here and there from Her hand. The two brilliant earrings on Her ears decorated Her shining cheeks like bluish reflections, and the hair scattered on Her face made Her even more beautiful to see.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.21 - As She played with the ball, the sari 
covering Her body became loose, and Her hair scattered. She tried to bind Her hair with Her beautiful left hand, and at the same time She played with the ball by striking it with Her right hand. This was so attractive that the Supreme Lord, by His interna
l potency, in this way captivated everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.22 - While Lord \'c7iva observed the beautiful woman playing with the ball, She sometimes glanced at him and slightly smiled in bashfulness. As he looked at the beautiful woman and She watched him, he forgot
 both himself and Um\'e4, his most beautiful wife, as well as his associates nearby.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.23 - When the ball leaped from Her hand and fell at a distance, the woman began to follow it, but as Lord \'c7iva observed these activities, a breeze suddenly blew away the fine dress and belt that covered her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.24 - Thus Lord \'c7iva saw the woman, every part of whose body was beautifully formed, and the beautiful woman also looked at him. Therefore, thinking that She was attracted to him, Lord \'c7iva became very muc
h attracted to Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.25 - Lord \'c7iva, his good sense taken away by the woman because of lusty desires to enjoy with Her, became so mad for Her that even in the presence of Bhav\'e4n\'e9 he did not hesitate to approach Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.26 - The beautiful woman was already naked, and when She saw Lord \'c7iva coming toward Her, She became extremely bashful. Thus She kept smiling, but She hid Herself among the trees and did not stand in one place.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.27 - His senses being agitated, Lord \'c7iva, victimized by lusty desires, began to follow Her, just as a lusty elephant follows a she-elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.28 - After following Her with great speed, Lord \'c7iva caught Her by the braid of Her hair and dragged Her near him. Although She was unwilling, he embraced Her with his arms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.29-30 - Being embraced by Lord \'c7iva like a female elephant embraced by a male, the woman, whose hair was scattered, swirled like a snake. O King, this woman, who had large, high hips, was a woman of yogam\'e4y\'e4
 presented by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. She released Herself somehow or other from the fond embrace of Lord \'c7iva's arms and ran away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.31 - As if harassed by an enemy in the form of lusty desires, Lord \'c7iva followed the path of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who acts very wonderfully and who had taken the form of Mohin\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.32 - Just as a maddened bull elephant follows a female elephant who is able to conceive pregnancy, Lord \'c7iva followed the beautiful woman and discharged semen, even though his discharge of semen never goes in vain.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.33 - O King, wheresoever on the surface of the globe fell the semen of the great personality of Lord \'c7iva, mines of gold and silver later appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.34 - Following Mohin\'e9, Lord \'c7iva went everywhere-near the shores of the rivers and lakes, near the mountains, near the forests, near the gardens, and wherever there lived great sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.35 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, best of kings, when Lord \'c7iva had fully discharged semen, he could see how he himself had been victimized by the illusion c
reated by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Thus he restrained himself from any further m\'e4y\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.36 - Thus Lord \'c7iva could understand his position and that of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has unlimited potencies. Having reached this understanding, he was not at all surprised by the wonderful way Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu had acted upon him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.37 - Seeing Lord \'c7iva unagitated and unashamed, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu [Madhus\'fcdana] was very pleased. Thus He resumed His original form and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.
38 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O best of the demigods, although you have been amply harassed because of My potency in assuming the form of a woman, you are established in your position. Therefore, may all good fortune be upon you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.39 - My dear Lord \'c7
ambhu, who within this material world but you can surpass My illusory energy? People are generally attached to sense enjoyment and conquered by its influence. Indeed, the influence of material nature is very difficult for them to surmount.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.40 - The material, external energy [m\'e4y\'e4], who cooperates with Me in creation and who is manifested in the three modes of nature, will not be able to bewilder you any longer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.41 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, having thus been praised by the Supreme Personality, who bears the mark of \'c7r\'e9vatsa on His chest, Lord \'c7
iva circumambulated Him. Then, after taking permission from Him, Lord \'c7iva returned to his abode, Kail\'e4sa, along with his associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.42 - O descendant of Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Lord \'c7iva, in jubilation, then addressed his wife, Bhav\'e4n\'e9, who is accepted by all authorities as the potency of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.43 - Lord \'c7iva said: O Goddess, you have now seen the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is t
he unborn master of everyone. Although I am one of the principal expansions of His Lordship, even I was illusioned by His energy. What then is to be said of others, who are fully dependent on m\'e4y\'e4?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.44 - When I finished performing mystic yoga for one thousand years, you asked me upon whom I was meditating. Now, here is that Supreme Person to whom time has no entrance and who the Vedas cannot understand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.45 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King, the person who bore the great mountain on His back for the churning of the ocean of milk is the same Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as \'c7\'e4r\'ecga-dhanv\'e4
. I have now described to you His prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.46 - The endeavor of one who constantly hears or describes this narration of the churning of th
e ocean of milk will never be fruitless. Indeed, chanting the glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the only means to annihilate all sufferings in this material world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.47 - Assuming the form of a young woman and thus bewildering the dem
ons, the Supreme Personality of Godhead distributed to His devotees, the demigods, the nectar produced from the churning of the ocean of milk. Unto that Supreme Personality of Godhead, who always fulfills the desires of His devotees, I offer my respectful
 obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  12. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.1-2 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said: The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, in the form of a woman, captivated the demons and enabled the demigods to drink the nectar. After hearing of these pastimes, Lord \'c7iva, who is carried by a bull, went to the place where Madhus\'fc
dana, the Lord, resides. Accompanied by his wife, Um\'e4, and surrounded by his companions, the ghosts, Lord \'c7iva went there to see the Lord's form as a woman.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.3 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead welcomed Lord \'c7iva and Um\'e4 with great respect, and after being seated comfortably, Lord \'c7iva duly worshiped the Lord and smilingly spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.4 - Lord Mah\'e4deva said: O chief demigod among the demigods, O all-pervading Lord, master of the universe, by Your ener
gy You are transformed into the creation. You are the root and efficient cause of everything. You are not material. Indeed, You are the Supersoul or supreme living force of everything. Therefore, You are Parame\'e7
vara, the supreme controller of all controllers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.12.5 - The manifest, the unmanifest, false ego and the beginning, maintenance and annihilation of this cosmic manifestation all come from You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. But because You are the Absolute Truth, the supreme absolute spirit
 soul, the Supreme Brahman, such changes as birth, death and sustenance do not exist in You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.6 - Pure devotees or great saintly persons who desire to achieve the highest goal in life and who are completely free from all material desires for sense 
gratification engage constantly in the transcendental service of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.7 - My Lord, You are the Supreme Brahman, complete in everything. Being completely spiritual, You are eternal, free from the material modes of nature, and full of tr
anscendental bliss. Indeed, for You there is no question of lamentation. Since You are the supreme cause, the cause of all causes, nothing can exist without You. Yet we are different from You in a relationship of cause and effect, for in one sense the cau
se and effect are different. You are the original cause of creation, manifestation and annihilation, and You bestow benedictions upon all living entities. Everyone depends upon You for the results of his activities, but You are always independent.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.
8 - My dear Lord, Your Lordship alone is the cause and the effect. Therefore, although You appear to be two, You are the absolute one. As there is no difference between the gold of a golden ornament and the gold in a mine, there is no difference between c
a
use and effect; both of them are the same. Only because of ignorance do people concoct differences and dualities. You are free from material contamination, and since the entire cosmos is caused by You and cannot exist without You, it is an effect of Your 
transcendental qualities. Thus the conception that Brahman is true and the world false cannot be maintained.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.9 - Those who are known as the impersonalist Ved\'e4ntists regard You as the impersonal Brahman. Others, known as the M\'e9m\'e4\'e0saka philosophers, regard You as religion. The S\'e4\'ec
khya philosophers regard You as the transcendental person who is beyond prak\'e5ti and puru\'f1a and who is the controller of even the demigods. The followers of the codes of devotional service known as the Pa\'efcar\'e4tras regard You a
s being endowed with nine different potencies. And the Pata\'efjala philosophers, the followers of Pata\'efjali Muni, regard You as the supreme independent Personality of Godhead, who has no equal or superior.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.10 - O my Lord, I, who am considered to be the best of the demigods, and Lord Brahm\'e4 and the great \'e5\'f1is, headed by Mar\'e9
ci, are born of the mode of goodness. Nonetheless, we are bewildered by Your illusory energy and cannot understand what this creation is. Aside from us, what is to be said of other
s, like the demons and human beings, who are in the base modes of material nature [rajo-gu\'eba and tamo-gu\'eba]? How will they know You?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.11 - My Lord, You are the supreme knowledge personified. You know everything about this creation and its beginning
, maintenance and annihilation, and You know all the endeavors made by the living entities, by which they are either implicated in this material world or liberated from it. As the air enters the vast sky and also enters the bodies of all moving and nonmov
ing entities, You are present everywhere, and therefore You are the knower of all.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.12 - My Lord, I have seen all kinds of incarnations You have exhibited by Your transcendental qualities, and now that You have appeared as a beautiful young woman, I wish to see that form of Your Lordship.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.13 - My Lord, we have come here desiring to see that form of Your Lordship which You showed to the demons to captivate them completely and in this way enable the demigods to drink nectar. I am very eager to see that form.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.14 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu was thus requested by Lord \'c7iva, who carries a trident in his hand, He smiled with gravity and replied to Lord \'c7iva as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.15 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: When the demons took away the jug of nectar, I assumed the form of a beautiful woman to bewilder them by directly cheating them and thus to act in the interest of the demigods.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.16 - O best of the demigods, I shall now show you My form that is very much appreciated by those who are lusty. Since you want to see that form, I shall reveal it in your presence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.17 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After speaking in this way, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu, immediately disappeared, and Lord \'c7iva remained there with Um\'e4
, looking for Him all around with moving eyes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.18 - Thereafter, in a nice forest nearby, full of trees with reddish-pink leaves and varieties of flowers, Lord \'c7iva saw a beautiful woman playing with a ball. Her hips were 
covered with a shining sari and ornamented with a belt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.19 - Because the ball was falling down and bouncing up, as She played with it Her breasts trembled, and because of the weight of those breasts and Her heavy flower garlands, Her waist appeare
d to be all but breaking at every step, as Her two soft feet, which were reddish like coral, moved here and there.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.20 - The woman's face was decorated by broad, beautiful, restless eyes, which moved as the ball bounced here and there from Her hand
. The two brilliant earrings on Her ears decorated Her shining cheeks like bluish reflections, and the hair scattered on Her face made Her even more beautiful to see.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.21 - As She played with the ball, the sari covering Her body became loose, and H
er hair scattered. She tried to bind Her hair with Her beautiful left hand, and at the same time She played with the ball by striking it with Her right hand. This was so attractive that the Supreme Lord, by His internal potency, in this way captivated eve
ryone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.22 - While Lord \'c7
iva observed the beautiful woman playing with the ball, She sometimes glanced at him and slightly smiled in bashfulness. As he looked at the beautiful woman and She watched him, he forgot both himself and Um\'e4, his most beaut
iful wife, as well as his associates nearby.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.23 - When the ball leaped from Her hand and fell at a distance, the woman began to follow it, but as Lord \'c7iva observed these activities, a breeze suddenly blew away the fine dress and belt that covered her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.24 - Thus Lord \'c7iva saw the woman, every part of whose body was beautifully formed, and the beautiful woman also looked at him. Therefore, thinking that She was attracted to him, Lord \'c7
iva became very much attracted to Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.25 - Lord \'c7iva, his good sense taken away by the woman because of lusty desires to enjoy with Her, became so mad for Her that even in the presence of Bhav\'e4n\'e9 he did not hesitate to approach Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.26 - The beautiful woman was already naked, and when She saw Lord \'c7iva coming toward Her, She became extremely bashful. Thus She kept smiling, but She hid Herself among the trees and did not stand in one place.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.27 - His senses being agitated, Lord \'c7iva, victimized by lusty desires, began to follow Her, just as a lusty elephant follows a she-elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.28 - After following Her with great speed, Lord \'c7iva caught Her by the braid of Her hair and dragged Her near him. Although She was unwilling, he embraced Her with his arms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.29-30 - Being embraced by Lord \'c7iva like a female elephant embraced by a male, the woman, whose hair was scattered, swirled like a snake. O King, this woman, who had large, high hips, was a woman of yogam\'e4y\'e4
 presented by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. She released Herself somehow or other from the fond embrace of Lord \'c7iva's arms and ran away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.31 - As if harassed by an enemy in the form of lusty desires, Lord \'c7iva followed the path of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who acts very wonderfully and who had taken the form of Mohin\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.32 - Just as a maddened bull elephant follows a female elephant who is able to conceive pregnancy, Lord \'c7iva followed the beautiful woman and discharged semen, even though his discharge of semen never goes in vain.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.33 - O King, wheresoever on the surface of the globe fell the semen of the great personality of Lord \'c7iva, mines of gold and silver later appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.34 - Following Mohin\'e9, Lord \'c7iva went everywhere-near the shores of the rivers and lakes, near the mountains, near the forests, near the gardens, and wherever there lived great sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.35 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, best of kings, when Lord \'c7iva had fully discharged semen, he could see how he himself had been victimized by the illusion created by the Supreme Personality of 
Godhead. Thus he restrained himself from any further m\'e4y\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.36 - Thus Lord \'c7iva could understand his position and that of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has unlimited potencies. Having reached this understanding, he was not at all surprised by the wonderful way Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu had acted upon him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.37 - Seeing Lord \'c7iva unagitated and unashamed, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu [Madhus\'fcdana] was very pleased. Thus He resumed His original form and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.38 - The Supreme Personality of Godhe
ad said: O best of the demigods, although you have been amply harassed because of My potency in assuming the form of a woman, you are established in your position. Therefore, may all good fortune be upon you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.39 - My dear Lord \'c7ambhu, who within t
his material world but you can surpass My illusory energy? People are generally attached to sense enjoyment and conquered by its influence. Indeed, the influence of material nature is very difficult for them to surmount.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.40 - The material, external energy [m\'e4y\'e4], who cooperates with Me in creation and who is manifested in the three modes of nature, will not be able to bewilder you any longer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.41 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, having thus been praised by the Supreme Personality, who bears the mark of \'c7r\'e9vatsa on His chest, Lord \'c7
iva circumambulated Him. Then, after taking permission from Him, Lord \'c7iva returned to his abode, Kail\'e4sa, along with his associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.42 - O descendant of Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Lord \'c7iva, in jubilation, then addressed his wife, Bhav\'e4n\'e9, who is accepted by all authorities as the potency of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.43 - Lord \'c7iva said: O Goddess, you have now seen the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the unborn master of everyone. Althoug
h I am one of the principal expansions of His Lordship, even I was illusioned by His energy. What then is to be said of others, who are fully dependent on m\'e4y\'e4?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.44 - When I finished performing mystic yoga for one thousand years, you asked me upon whom I was meditating. Now, here is that Supreme Person to whom time has no entrance and who the Vedas cannot understand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.45 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King, the person who bore the great mountain on His back for the churning of the ocean of milk is the same Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as \'c7\'e4r\'ecga-dhanv\'e4
. I have now described to you His prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.46 - The endeavor of one who constantly hears or describes this narration of the churning of the ocean of milk will never be fruitle
ss. Indeed, chanting the glories of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the only means to annihilate all sufferings in this material world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.47 - Assuming the form of a young woman and thus bewildering the demons, the Supreme Personality of Godhe
ad distributed to His devotees, the demigods, the nectar produced from the churning of the ocean of milk. Unto that Supreme Personality of Godhead, who always fulfills the desires of His devotees, I offer my respectful obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
