\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.25 - Lord \'c7iva, his good sense taken away by the woman because of lusty desires to enjoy with Her, became so mad for Her that even in the presence of Bhav\'e4n\'e9 he did not hesitate to approach Her.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.26 - The beautiful woman was already naked, and when She saw Lord \'c7iva coming toward Her, She became extremely bashful. Thus She kept smiling, but She hid Herself among the trees and did not stand in one place.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.27 - His senses being agitated, Lord \'c7iva, victimized by lusty desires, began to follow Her, just as a lusty elephant follows a she-elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.28 - After following Her with great speed, Lord \'c7iva caught Her by the braid of Her hair and dragged Her near him. Although She was unwilling, he embraced Her with his arms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.29-30 - Being embraced by Lord \'c7iva like a female elephant embraced by a male, the woman, whose hair was scattered, swirled like a snake. O King, this woman, who had large, high hips, was a woman of yogam\'e4y\'e4
 presented by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. She released Herself somehow or other from the fond embrace of Lord \'c7iva's arms and ran away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.31 - As if harassed by an enemy in the form of lusty desires, Lord \'c7iva followed the path of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who acts very wonderfully and who had taken the form of Mohin\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.32 - Just as a maddened bull elephant follows a female elephant who is able to conceive pregnancy, Lord \'c7iva followed the beautiful woman and discharged semen, even though his discharge of semen never goes in vain.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.33 - O King, wheresoever on the surface of the globe fell the semen of the great personality of Lord \'c7iva, mines of gold and silver later appeared.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.34 - Following Mohin\'e9, Lord \'c7iva went everywhere-near the shores of the rivers and lakes, near the mountains, near the forests, near the gardens, and wherever there lived great sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.35 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, best of kings, when Lord \'c7
iva had fully discharged semen, he could see how he himself had been victimized by the illusion created by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Thus he restrained himself from any further m\'e4y\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.36 - Thus Lord \'c7iva could understand his position and that of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has unlimited potencies. Having reached this understanding, he was not at all surprised by the wonderful way Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu had acted upon him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.37 - Seeing Lord \'c7iva unagitated and unashamed, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu [Madhus\'fcdana] was very pleased. Thus He resumed His original form and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.38 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O best of the demigods, alth
ough you have been amply harassed because of My potency in assuming the form of a woman, you are established in your position. Therefore, may all good fortune be upon you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.39 - My dear Lord \'c7ambhu, who within this material world but you can surpas
s My illusory energy? People are generally attached to sense enjoyment and conquered by its influence. Indeed, the influence of material nature is very difficult for them to surmount.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.40 - The material, external energy [m\'e4y\'e4], who cooperates with Me in creation and who is manifested in the three modes of nature, will not be able to bewilder you any longer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.41 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, having thus been praised by the Supreme Personality, who bears the mark of \'c7r\'e9vatsa on His chest, Lord \'c7
iva circumambulated Him. Then, after taking permission from Him, Lord \'c7iva returned to his abode, Kail\'e4sa, along with his associates.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.42 - O descendant of Bharata Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Lord \'c7iva, in jubilation, then addressed his wife, Bhav\'e4n\'e9, who is accepted by all authorities as the potency of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.43 - Lord \'c7iva said: O Goddess, you have now seen the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the unborn master of everyone. Although I am one of the principal expansion
s of His Lordship, even I was illusioned by His energy. What then is to be said of others, who are fully dependent on m\'e4y\'e4?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.44 - When I finished performing mystic yoga for one thousand years, you asked me upon whom I was meditating. Now, here is that Supreme Person to whom time has no entrance and who the Vedas cannot understand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.45 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King, the person who bore the great mountain on His back for the churning of the ocean of milk is the same Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as \'c7\'e4r\'ecga-dhanv\'e4
. I have now described to you His prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.46 - The endeavor of one who constantly hears or describes this narration of the churning of the ocean of milk will never be fruitless. Indeed, chanting the glories of t
he Supreme Personality of Godhead is the only means to annihilate all sufferings in this material world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.12.47 - Assuming the form of a young woman and thus bewildering the demons, the Supreme Personality of Godhead distributed to His devotees, the d
emigods, the nectar produced from the churning of the ocean of milk. Unto that Supreme Personality of Godhead, who always fulfills the desires of His devotees, I offer my respectful obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-47
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: The present Manu, who is named \'c7r\'e4ddhadeva, is the son of Vivasv\'e4n, the predominating deity on the sun planet. \'c7r\'e4
ddhadeva is the seventh Manu. Now please hear from me as I describe his sons.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.2-3 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, among the ten sons of Manu are Ik\'f1v\'e4ku, Nabhaga, Dh\'e5\'f1\'f6a, \'c7ary\'e4ti, Nari\'f1yanta and N\'e4bh\'e4ga. The seventh son is known as Di\'f1\'f6a. Then come Tar\'fc\'f1a and P\'e5
\'f1adhra, and the tenth son is known as Vasum\'e4n.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.4 - In this manvantara, O King, the \'c4dityas, the Vasus, the Rudras, the Vi\'e7vedevas, the Maruts, the two A\'e7vin\'e9-kum\'e4ra brothers and the \'c5bhus are the demigods. Their head king [Indra] is Purandara.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.5 - Ka\'e7yapa, Atri, Vasi\'f1\'f6ha, Vi\'e7v\'e4mitra, Gautama, Jamadagni and Bharadv\'e4ja are known as the seven sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.6 - In this manvantara, the Supreme Personality of Godhead appeared as the youngest of all the \'c4dityas, known as V\'e4mana, the dwarf. His father was Ka\'e7yapa and His mother Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.7 - I have briefly explained to you the position of the seven Manus. Now I shall describe the future Manus, along with the incarnations of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.8 - O King, I have previously described [in the Sixth Canto] the two daughters of Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4, named Sa\'e0j\'ef\'e4 and Ch\'e4y\'e4, who were the first two wives of Vivasv\'e4n.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.9 - It is said that the sun-god had a third wife, named Va\'f2av\'e4. Of the three wives, the wife named Sa\'e0j\'ef\'e4 had three children-Yama, Yam\'e9 and \'c7r\'e4ddhadeva. Now let me describe the children of Ch\'e4y
\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.10 - Ch\'e4y\'e4 had a son named S\'e4var\'ebi and a daughter named Tapat\'e9, who later became the wife of King Sa\'e0vara\'eba. Ch\'e4y\'e4's third child is known as \'c7anai\'e7cara [Saturn]. Va\'f2av\'e4
 gave birth to two sons, namely the A\'e7vin\'e9 brothers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.11 - O King, when the period of the eighth Manu arrives, S\'e4var\'ebi will become the Manu. Nirmoka and Virajaska will be among his sons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.12 - In the period of the eighth Manu, among the demigods will be the Sutap\'e4s, the Virajas and the Am\'e5taprabhas. The king of the demigods, Indra, will be Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Virocana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.13 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja gave a gift of three paces of land to Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and because of this charity he lost all the three worlds. Later, however, when Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is pleased because of Bali's giving everything to Him, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja will achieve the perfection of life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.14 - With great affection, the Personality of Godhead bound Bali and then installed him in the kingdom of Sutala, which is more opulent than the heavenly planets. Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja Bali now resides on that planet and is more comfortably situated than Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.15-16 - O King, during the eighth manvantara, the great personalities G\'e4lava, D\'e9ptim\'e4n, Para\'e7ur\'e4ma, A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4, K\'e5p\'e4c\'e4rya, \'c5\'f1ya\'e7\'e5\'ecga and our father, Vy\'e4
sadeva, the incarnation of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, will be the seven sages. For the present, they are all residing in their respective \'e4\'e7ramas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.17 - In the eighth manvantara, the greatly powerful Personality of Godhead S\'e4rvabhauma will take birth. His father will be Devaguhya, and His mother will be Sarasvat\'e9
. He will take the kingdom away from Purandara [Lord Indra] and give it to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.18 - O King, the ninth Manu will be Dak\'f1a-s\'e4var\'ebi, who is born of Varu\'eba. Among his sons will be Bh\'fctaketu, and D\'e9ptaketu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.19 - In this ninth manvantara, the P\'e4ras and Mar\'e9cigarbhas will be among the demigods. The king of heaven, Indra, will be named Adbhuta, and Dyutim\'e4n will be among the seven sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.20 - \'c5\'f1abhadeva, a partial incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, will take birth from his father, \'c4yu\'f1m\'e4n, and his mother, Ambudh\'e4r\'e4. He will enab
le the Indra named Adbhuta to enjoy the opulence of the three worlds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.21 - The son of Upa\'e7loka known as Brahma-s\'e4var\'ebi will be the tenth Manu. Bh\'fcri\'f1e\'eba will be among his sons, and the br\'e4hma\'ebas headed by Havi\'f1m\'e4n will be the seven sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.22 - Havi\'f1m\'e4n, Suk\'e5ta, Satya, Jaya, M\'fcrti and others will be the seven sages, the Suv\'e4sanas and Viruddhas will be among the demigods, and \'c7ambhu will be their king, Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.23 - In the home of Vi\'e7vasra\'f1\'f6\'e4, a plenary portion of the Supreme Personality of Godhead will appear from the womb of Vi\'f1\'fcc\'e9 as the incarnation known as Vi\'f1vaksena. He will make friends with \'c7
ambhu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.24 - In the eleventh manvantara, the Manu will be Dharma-s\'e4var\'ebi, who will be extremely learned in spiritual knowledge. From him there will come ten sons, headed by Satyadharma.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.25 - The Viha\'ecgamas, K\'e4magamas, Nirv\'e4\'ebarucis and others will be the demigods. The king of the demigods, Indra, will be Vaidh\'e5ta, and the seven sages will be headed by Aru\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.26 - The son of \'c4ryaka known as Dharmasetu, a partial incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, will appear from the womb of Vaidh\'e5t\'e4, the wife of \'c4ryaka, and will rule the three worlds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.27 - O King, the twelfth Manu will be named Rudra-s\'e4var\'ebi. Devav\'e4n, Upadeva and Deva\'e7re\'f1\'f6ha will be among his sons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.28 - In this manvantara, the name of Indra will be \'c5tadh\'e4m\'e4, and the demigods will be headed by the Haritas. Among the sages will be Tapom\'fcrti, Tapasv\'e9 and \'c4gn\'e9dhraka.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.29 - From the mother named Sun\'e5t\'e4 and the father named Satyasah\'e4 will come Svadh\'e4m\'e4, a partial incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He will rule that manvantara.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.30 - The thirteenth Manu will be named Deva-s\'e4var\'ebi, and he will be very advanced in spiritual knowledge. Among his sons will be Citrasena and Vicitra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.31 - In the thirteenth manvantara, the Sukarm\'e4s and Sutr\'e4mas will be among the demigods, Divaspati will be the king of heaven, and Nirmoka and Tattvadar\'e7a will be among the seven sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.32 - The son of Devahotra known as Yoge\'e7vara will appear as a partial incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. His mother's name will be B\'e5hat\'e9. He will perform activities for the welfare of Divaspati.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.33 - The name of the fourteenth Manu will be Indra-s\'e4var\'ebi. He will have sons like Uru, Gambh\'e9ra and Budha.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.34 - The Pavitras and C\'e4k\'f1u\'f1as will be among the demigods, and \'c7uci will be Indra, the king of heaven. Agni, B\'e4hu, \'c7uci, \'c7uddha, M\'e4gadha and others of great austerity will be the seven sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.35 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, in the fourteenth manvantara the Supreme Personality of Godhead will appear from the womb of Vit\'e4n\'e4, and His father's name will be Satr\'e4ya\'eba. This incarnation will be celebrated as B
\'e5hadbh\'e4nu, and He will administer spiritual activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.13.36 - O King, I have now described to you the fourteen Manus appearing in the past, present and future. The total duration of time ruled by these Manus is one thousand yuga cycles. This is called a kal
pa, or one day of Lord Brahm\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  13. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
