\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.1 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: O most opulent \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, please explain to me how Manu and the others in each manvantara are engaged in their respective duties, and by whose order they are so engaged.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.2 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: The Manus, the sons of Manu, the great sages, the Indras and all the demigods, O King, are appointed by the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His various incarnations such as Yaj\'efa.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.3 - O King, I have already described to you various incarnations of the Lord, such as Yaj\'efa. The Manus and others are chosen by these incarnations, under whose direction they conduct the universal affairs.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.4 - At the end of every four yugas, the great saintly persons, upon seeing that the eternal occupational duties of mankind have been misused, reestablish the principles of religion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.5 - Thereafter, O King, the Manus, being fully engaged according to the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, directly reestablish the principles of occupational duty in its full four parts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.6 - To enjoy the results of sacrifices [yaj\'ef
as], the rulers of the world, namely the sons and grandsons of Manu, discharge the orders of the Supreme Personality of Godhead until the end of Manu's reign. The demigods also share the results of these sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.7 -
 Indra, King of heaven, receiving benedictions from the Supreme Personality of Godhead and thus enjoying highly developed opulences, maintains the living entities all over the three worlds by pouring sufficient rain on all the planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.8 - In every yuga, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, assumes the form of Siddhas such as Sanaka to preach transcendental knowledge, He assumes the form of great saintly persons such as Y\'e4j\'ef
avalkya to teach the way of karma, and He assumes the form of great yog\'e9s such as Datt\'e4treya to teach the system of mystic yoga.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.9 - In the form of Praj\'e4pati Mar\'e9ci, the Supreme Personality of Godhead creates progeny; becoming the king, He kills the thieves and rogues; and in the form of time, He annihilates everyth
ing. All the different qualities of material existence should be understood to be qualities of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.10 - People in general are bewildered by the illusory energy, and therefore they try to find the Absolute Truth, the
 Supreme Personality of Godhead, through various types of research and philosophical speculation. Nonetheless, they are unable to see the Supreme Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.14.11 - In one kalpa, or one day of Brahm\'e4, there take place the many changes called vikalpas. O K
ing, all of these have been previously described to you by me. Learned scholars who know the past, present and future have ascertained that in one day of Brahm\'e4 there are fourteen Manus.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-11
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.1-2 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the proprietor of everything. Why did He beg three paces of land from Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja like a poor man, and when He got the gift for which He had begged, why did He nonetheless arrest Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja? I am very much anxious to know the mystery of these contradictions.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, when Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja lost all his opulence and died in the fight, \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, a descendant of Bh\'e5
gu Muni, brought him back to life. Because of this, the great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja became a disciple of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya and began to serve him with great faith, offering everything he had.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.4 - The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu Muni were very pleased with Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who desired to conquer the kingdom of Indra. Therefore, after purifying him and
 properly bathing him according to regulative principles, they engaged him in performing the yaj\'efa known as Vi\'e7vajit.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.5 - When ghee [clarified butter] was offered in the fire of sacrifice, there appeared from the fire a celestial chariot covered w
ith gold and silk. There also appeared yellow horses like those of Indra, and a flag marked with a lion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.6 - A gilded bow, two quivers of infallible arrows, and celestial armor also appeared. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja offered Bali a garland of flowers that would never fade, and \'c7ukr\'e4c
\'e4rya gave him a conchshell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.7 - When Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali had thus performed the special ritualistic ceremony advised by the br\'e4hma\'ebas and had received, by their grace, the equipment for fighting, he circumambulated the br\'e4hma\'eb
as and offered them obeisances. He also saluted Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and offered obeisances to him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.8-9 - Then, after getting on the chariot given by \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, decorated with a nice garland, put protect
ive armor on his body, equipped himself with a bow, and took up a sword and a quiver of arrows. When he sat down on the seat of the chariot, his arms decorated with golden bangles and his ears with sapphire earrings, he shone like a worshipable fire.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8
.15.10-11 - When he assembled with his own soldiers and the demon chiefs, who were equal to him in strength, opulence and beauty, they appeared as if they would swallow the sky and burn all directions with their vision. After thus gathering the demoniac s
oldiers, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja departed for the opulent capital of Indra. Indeed, he seemed to make the entire surface of the world tremble.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.12 - King Indra's city was full of pleasing orchards and gardens, such as the Nandana garden. Because of the weight
 of the flowers, leaves and fruit, the branches of the eternally existing trees were bending down. The gardens were visited by pairs of chirping birds and singing bees. The entire atmosphere was celestial.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.13 - Beautiful women protected by the demigods sported in the gardens, which had lotus ponds full of swans, cranes, cakrav\'e4kas and ducks.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.14 - The city was surrounded by trenches full of Ganges water, known as \'c4k\'e4\'e7a-ga\'ecg\'e4, and by a high wall, which was the color of fire. Upon this wall were parapets for fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.15 - The doors were made of solid gold plates, and the gates were of excellent marble. These were linked by various public roads. The entire city had been constructed by Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.16 - The city was full of courtyards, wide roads, assembly houses, and not less than one hundred million airplanes. The crossroads were made of pearl, and there were sitting places made of diamond and coral.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.17 - Everlastingly beautiful and youthful women, who were dressed with clean garments, glittered in the city like fires with flames. They all possessed the quality of \'e7y\'e4m\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.18 - The breezes blowing in the streets of the city bore the fragrance of the flowers falling from the hair of the women of the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.19 - Apsar\'e4s passed on the streets, which were covered with the white, fragrant smoke of aguru incense emanating from windows with golden filigree.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.20 - The city was shaded by canopies decorated with pearls, and the domes of the palaces had 
flags of pearl and gold. The city always resounded with the vibrations of peacocks, pigeons and bees, and above the city flew airplanes full of beautiful women who constantly chanted auspicious songs that were very pleasing to the ear.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.21 - The city was filled with the sounds of m\'e5da\'ec
gas, conchshells, kettledrums, flutes and well-tuned stringed instruments all playing in concert. There was constant dancing and the Gandharvas sang. The combined beauty of Indrapur\'e9 defeated beauty personified.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.22 - No one who was sinful, envious, violent toward other living entities, cunning, falsely proud, lusty or greedy could enter that city. The people who lived there were all devoid of these faults.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.23 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who was the commander of numberless soldiers, gathered his soldiers outside this abode of Indra and attacked it from all directions. He sounded the conchshell given him by his spiritual master, 
\'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, thus creating a fearful situation for the women protected by Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.24 - Seeing Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's indefatigable endeavor and understanding his motive, King Indra, along with the other demigods, approached his spiritual master, B\'e5haspati, and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.25 - My lord, our old enemy Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja now has new enthusiasm, and he has obtained such astonishing power that we think that perhaps we cannot resist his prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.26 - No one anywhere can counteract this military arrangement of Bali's. It now appears that Bali is trying to drink up the entire univer
se with his mouth, lick up the ten directions with his tongue, and raise fire in every direction with his eyes. Indeed, he has arisen like the annihilating fire known as sa\'e0vartaka.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.27 - Kindly inform me. What is the cause for Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's strength, endeavor, influence and victory? How has he become so enthusiastic?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.28 - B\'e5haspati, the spiritual master of the demigods, said: O Indra, I know the cause for your enemy's becoming so powerful. The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu Muni, being pleased by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, their disciple, endowed him with such extraordinary power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.29 - Neither you nor your men can conquer the most powerful Bali. Indeed, no one but the Supreme Personality of Godhead can conquer him, for he is now equipped with
 the supreme spiritual power [brahma-tejas]. As no one can stand before Yamar\'e4ja, no one can now stand before Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.30 - Therefore, waiting until the situation of your enemies is reversed, you should all leave this heavenly planet and go elsewhere, where you will not be seen.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.31 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has now become extremely powerful because of the benedictions given him by the br\'e4hma\'ebas, but when he later insults the br\'e4hma\'eb
as, he will be vanquished, along with his friends and assistants.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.32 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: The demigods, being thus advised by B\'e5
haspati for their benefit, immediately accepted his words. Assuming forms according to their desire, they left the heavenly kingdom and scattered, without being observed by the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.33 - When the demigods had disappeared, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Virocana, entered the heavenly kingdom, and from there he brought the three worlds under his control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.34 - The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu, being very pleased with their disciple, who had conquered the entire universe, now engaged him in performing one hundred a\'e7vamedha sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.35 - When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja performed these sacrifices, he gained a great reputation in all directions, throughout the three worlds. Thus he shone in his position, like the brilliant moon in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.36 - Because of the favor of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, thinking himself very satisfied, became very opulent and prosperous and began to enjoy the kingdom.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
