\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.25 - My lord, our old enemy Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja now has new enthusiasm, and he has obtained such astonishing power that we think that perhaps we cannot resist his prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.26 - No one anywhere can counteract this military arrangement of B
ali's. It now appears that Bali is trying to drink up the entire universe with his mouth, lick up the ten directions with his tongue, and raise fire in every direction with his eyes. Indeed, he has arisen like the annihilating fire known as sa\'e0vartaka.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.27 - Kindly inform me. What is the cause for Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's strength, endeavor, influence and victory? How has he become so enthusiastic?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.28 - B\'e5haspati, the spiritual master of the demigods, said: O Indra, I know the cause for your enemy's becoming so powerful. The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu Muni, being pleased by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, their disciple, endowed him with such extraordinary power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.29 - Neither you nor your men can conquer the most powerful Bali. Indeed, no one but the Supr
eme Personality of Godhead can conquer him, for he is now equipped with the supreme spiritual power [brahma-tejas]. As no one can stand before Yamar\'e4ja, no one can now stand before Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.30 - Therefore, waiting until the situation of your enemies is reversed, you should all leave this heavenly planet and go elsewhere, where you will not be seen.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.31 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has now become extremely powerful because of the benedictions given him by the br\'e4hma\'ebas, but when he later insults the br\'e4hma\'eb
as, he will be vanquished, along with his friends and assistants.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.32 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: The demigods, being thus advised by B\'e5haspati for their benefit, immediately accepted his words. Assuming forms according to their desire, 
they left the heavenly kingdom and scattered, without being observed by the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.33 - When the demigods had disappeared, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Virocana, entered the heavenly kingdom, and from there he brought the three worlds under his control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.34 - The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu, being very pleased with their disciple, who had conquered the entire universe, now engaged him in performing one hundred a\'e7vamedha sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.35 - When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja performed these sacrifices, he gained a great reputation in all directions, throughout the three worlds. Thus he shone in his position, like the brilliant moon in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.36 - Because of the favor of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, thinking himself very satisfied, became very opulent and prosperous and began to enjoy the kingdom.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Conquers the Heavenly Planets
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.1-2 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the proprietor of everything. Why did He beg three paces of land from Bali Mah\'e4
r\'e4ja like a poor man, and when He got the gift for which He had begged, why did He nonetheless arrest Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja? I am very much anxious to know the mystery of these contradictions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, when Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja lost all his opulence and died in the fight, \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, a descendant of Bh\'e5
gu Muni, brought him back to life. Because of this, the great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja became a disciple of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya and began to serve him with great faith, offering everything he had.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.4 - The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu Muni were very pleased with Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who desired to conquer the kingdom of Indra. Therefore, after purifying him and properly bathing him according to regulative principles, they engaged him in performing the yaj\'efa known as Vi\'e7vajit.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.15.5 - When ghee [clarified butter] was offered in the fire of sacrifice, there appeared from the fire a celestial chariot covered with gold and silk. There also appeared yellow horses like those of Indra, and a flag marked with a lion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.6 - A gilded bow, two quivers of infallible arrows, and celestial armor also appeared. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja offered Bali a garland of flowers that would never fade, and \'c7ukr\'e4c
\'e4rya gave him a conchshell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.7 - When Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali had thus performed the special ritualistic ceremony advised by the br\'e4hma\'ebas and had received, by their grace, the equipment for fighting, he circumambulated the br\'e4hma\'eb
as and offered them obeisances. He also saluted Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and offered obeisances to him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.8-9 - Then, after getting on the chariot given by \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, decorated with a nice garland, put protective armor on his body, equipped himself with a bow, and took up a sword and a quiver of arrows. When he sat down o
n the seat of the chariot, his arms decorated with golden bangles and his ears with sapphire earrings, he shone like a worshipable fire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.10-11 - When he assembled with his own soldiers and the demon chiefs, who were equal to him in strength, opule
nce and beauty, they appeared as if they would swallow the sky and burn all directions with their vision. After thus gathering the demoniac soldiers, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja departed for the opulent capital of Indra. Indeed, he seemed to make the entire surface of the world tremble.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.15.12 - King Indra's city was full of pleasing orchards and gardens, such as the Nandana garden. Because of the weight of the flowers, leaves and fruit, the branches of the eternally existing trees were bending down. The gardens wer
e visited by pairs of chirping birds and singing bees. The entire atmosphere was celestial.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.13 - Beautiful women protected by the demigods sported in the gardens, which had lotus ponds full of swans, cranes, cakrav\'e4kas and ducks.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.14 - The city was surrounded by trenches full of Ganges water, known as \'c4k\'e4\'e7a-ga\'ecg\'e4, and by a high wall, which was the color of fire. Upon this wall were parapets for fighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.15 - The doors were made of solid gold plates, and the gates were of excellent marble. These were linked by various public roads. The entire city had been constructed by Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.16 - The city was full of courtyards, wide roads, assembly houses, and not less than one hundred million airplanes. The crossroads were made of pearl, and there were sitting places made of diamond and coral.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.17 - Everlastingly beautiful and youthful women, who were dressed with clean garments, glittered in the city like fires with flames. They all possessed the quality of \'e7y\'e4m\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.18 - The breezes blowing in the streets of the city bore the fragrance of the flowers falling from the hair of the women of the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.19 - Apsar\'e4s passed on the streets, which were covered with the white, fragrant smoke of aguru incense emanating from windows with golden filigree.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.20 - The city was shaded by canopies decorated with pearls, and the domes of the palaces had flags of pearl and gold. The city always resounded with the vibrations of peacocks, pigeons and bees, and above th
e city flew airplanes full of beautiful women who constantly chanted auspicious songs that were very pleasing to the ear.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.21 - The city was filled with the sounds of m\'e5da\'ecgas, conchshells, kettledrums, flutes and well-tuned stringed instruments al
l playing in concert. There was constant dancing and the Gandharvas sang. The combined beauty of Indrapur\'e9 defeated beauty personified.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.22 - No one who was sinful, envious, violent toward other living entities, cunning, falsely proud, lusty or greedy could enter that city. The people who lived there were all devoid of these faults.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.23 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who was the commander of numberless soldiers, gathered his soldiers outside this abode of Indra and attacked it from all directions. He sounded the conchshell given him by his spiritual master, 
\'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, thus creating a fearful situation for the women protected by Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.24 - Seeing Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's indefatigable endeavor and understanding his motive, King Indra, along with the other demigods, approached his spiritual master, B\'e5haspati, and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.25 - My lord, our old enemy Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja now has new enthusiasm, and he has obtained such astonishing power that we think that perhaps we cannot resist his prowess.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 
8.15.26 - No one anywhere can counteract this military arrangement of Bali's. It now appears that Bali is trying to drink up the entire universe with his mouth, lick up the ten directions with his tongue, and raise fire in every direction with his eyes. I
ndeed, he has arisen like the annihilating fire known as sa\'e0vartaka.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.27 - Kindly inform me. What is the cause for Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's strength, endeavor, influence and victory? How has he become so enthusiastic?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.28 - B\'e5haspati, the spiritual master of the demigods, said: O Indra, I know the cause for your enemy's becoming so powerful. The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu Muni, being pleased by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, their disciple, endowed him with such extraordinary power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.29 - Neither you nor y
our men can conquer the most powerful Bali. Indeed, no one but the Supreme Personality of Godhead can conquer him, for he is now equipped with the supreme spiritual power [brahma-tejas]. As no one can stand before Yamar\'e4
ja, no one can now stand before Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.30 - Therefore, waiting until the situation of your enemies is reversed, you should all leave this heavenly planet and go elsewhere, where you will not be seen.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.31 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has now become extremely powerful because of the benedictions given him by the br\'e4hma\'ebas, but when he later insults the br\'e4hma\'eb
as, he will be vanquished, along with his friends and assistants.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.32 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: The demigods, being thus advised by B\'e5haspati for their benefit, imm
ediately accepted his words. Assuming forms according to their desire, they left the heavenly kingdom and scattered, without being observed by the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.33 - When the demigods had disappeared, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, the son of Virocana, entered the heavenly kingdom, and from there he brought the three worlds under his control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.34 - The br\'e4hma\'eba descendants of Bh\'e5gu, being very pleased with their disciple, who had conquered the entire universe, now engaged him in performing one hundred a\'e7vamedha sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.35 - When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja performed these sacrifices, he gained a great reputation in all directions, throughout the three worlds. Thus he shone in his position, like the brilliant moon in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.15.36 - Because of the favor of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, thinking himself very satisfied, became very opulent and prosperous and began to enjoy the kingdom.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-36
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, when Aditi's sons, the demigods, had thus disappeared from heaven and the demons had occupied their places, Aditi began lamenting, as if she had no protector.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.2 - After many, many days, the great powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa Muni arose from a trance of meditation and returned home to see the \'e4\'e7rama of Aditi neither jubilant nor festive.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.3 - O best of the Kurus, when Ka\'e7yapa Muni had been properly received and welcomed, he took his seat and then spoke as follows to his wife, Aditi, who was very morose.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.4 - O most gentle one, I wonder whether anything inauspicious has now taken place in regard to religious principles, the br\'e4hma\'ebas or the people in general, who are subject to the whims of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.5 - O my wife, who are very much attached to household life, if the principles of religion, economic d
evelopment and satisfaction of the senses are properly followed in household life, one's activities are as good as those of a transcendentalist. I wonder whether there have been any discrepancies in following these principles.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.6 - I wonder whether because of being too attached to the members of your family, you failed to properly receive uninvited guests, who therefore were not welcomed and went away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.7 - Homes from which guests go away without having been received even with an offering of a little water are like those holes in the field which are the homes of jackals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.8 - O chaste and auspicious woman, when I left home for other places, were you in so much anxiety that you did not offer oblations of ghee into the fire?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.9 - By worshiping the fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas, a householder can achieve the desired goal of residing in the higher planets, for the sacrificial fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas are to be considered the mouth of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu, who is the Supersoul of all the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.10 - O great-minded lady, are all your sons faring well? Seeing your withered face, I can perceive that your mind is not tranquil. How is this so?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.11 - Aditi said: O my respected br\'e4hma\'eba husband, all is well with the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the cows, religion and the welfare of other people. O master of the house, the three principles of dharma, artha and k\'e4
ma flourish in household life, which is consequently full of good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.12 - O beloved husband, the fires, guests, servants and beggars are all being properly cared for by me. Because I always think of you, there is no possibility that any of the religious principles will be neglected.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.13 - O my lord, since you are a Praj\'e4pati and are personally my instructor in the principles of religion, where is the possibility that all my desires will not be fulfilled?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.14 - O son of Mar\'e9ci, because you are a great personality you are equal toward all the demons and demigods, who are born either from your body or from your mind and who p
ossess one or another of the three qualities-sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba or tamo-gu\'eba. But although the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the supreme controller, is equal toward all living entities, He is especially favorable to the devotees.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.15 - Therefore, most gentle lord, kindly favor your maidservant. We have now been deprived of our opulence and residence by our competitors, the demons. Kindly give us protection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.16 - The demons, our formidably powerful enemies, have taken away our opulence, our beauty, our fame and even our residence. Indeed, we have now been exiled, and we are drowning in an ocean of trouble.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.17 - O best of sages, best of all those who grant auspicious benedictions, please consider our situation and bestow upon my sons the benedictions by which they can regain what they have lost.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When Ka\'e7yapa Muni was thus requested by Aditi, he slightly smiled. "Alas," he said, "how powerful is the illusory energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, by which 
the entire world is bound by affection for children!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.19 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: What is this material body, made of five elements? It is different from the spirit soul. Indeed, the spirit soul is completely different from the material elements 
from which the body is made. But because of bodily attachment, one is regarded as a husband or son. These illusory relationships are caused by misunderstanding.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.20 - My dear Aditi, engage in devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the master of everything, who can subdue everyone's enemies, and who sits within everyone's heart. Only that Supreme Person-K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, or V\'e4sudeva-can bestow all auspicious benedictions upon everyone, for He is the spiritual master of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 S
B 8.16.21 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is very merciful to the poor, will fulfill all of your desires, for devotional service unto Him is infallible. Any method other than devotional service is useless. That is my opinion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.22 - \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Aditi said: O br\'e4hma\'eba, tell me the regulative principles by which I may worship the supreme master of the world so that the Lord will be pleased with me and fulfill all my desires.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.23 - O best of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, kindly instruct me in the perfect
 method of worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead in devotional service, by which the Lord may very soon be pleased with me and save me, along with my sons, from this most dangerous condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.24 - \'c7r\'e9 Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: When I desired offspring, I placed inquiries before Lord Brahm\'e4, who is born from a lotus flower. Now I shall explain to you the same process Lord Brahm\'e4 instructed me, by which Ke
\'e7ava, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.25 - In the bright fortnight of the month of Ph\'e4lguna [February and March], for twelve days ending with Dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9
, one should observe the vow of subsisting only on milk and should worship the lotus-eyed Supreme Personality of Godhead with all devotion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.26 - If dirt dug up by a boar is available, on the day of the dark moon one should smear this dirt on his body and then bathe in a flowing river. While bathing, one should chant the following mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.27 - O mother earth, you were raised by the Supreme Personality of Godhea
d in the form of a boar because of your desiring to have a place to stay. I pray that you kindly vanquish all the reactions of my sinful life. I offer my respectful obeisances unto you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.28 - Thereafter, one should perform his daily spiritual dutie
s and then, with great attention, offer worship to the Deity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and also to the altar, the sun, water, fire and the spiritual master.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.29 - O Supreme Personality of Godhead, greatest of all, who lives in everyone's heart and in whom everyone lives, O witness of everything, O V\'e4
sudeva, supreme and all-pervading person, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.30 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Person. Being very subtle, You are never visible to material eyes. You are the knower of the twenty-four elements, and You are the inaugurator of the s\'e4\'ec
khya-yoga system.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.31 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who have two heads [pr\'e4ya\'eb\'e9ya and ud\'e4yan\'e9
ya], three legs [savana-traya], four horns [the four Vedas] and seven hands [the seven chandas, such as G\'e4yatr\'e9]. I offer my obeisances unto You, whose heart and soul are the three Vedic rituals [karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a, j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2
a and up\'e4san\'e4-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a] and who expand these rituals in the form of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.32 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, Lord \'c7iva, or Rudra, who are the reservoir of all potencies, the reservoir of all knowledge, and the master of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.33 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are situated as Hira\'eb
yagarbha, the source of life, the Supersoul of every living entity. Your body is the source of the opulence of all mystic power. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.34 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are the original Personality of Godhead, the witness in everyone's heart, and the incarnation of Nara-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba \'c5\'f1
i in the form of a human being. O Personality of Godhead, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.35 - My Lord, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are dressed in yellow garments, whose bodily hue resembles the marakata gem, and who have full control over the goddess of fortune. O my Lord Ke\'e7
ava, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.36 - O most exalted and worshipable Lord, best of those who bestow benediction, You can fulfill the desires of everyone, and therefore those who are sober, for their own welfare, worship the dust of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.37 - All the demigods, as well as the goddess of fortune, engage in the service of His lotus feet. Indeed, they respect the fragrance of those lotus feet. May the Supreme Personality of Godhead be pleased with me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.38 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: By chanting all these mantras, welcoming the Supreme Personality of Godhead with faith and devotion, and offering Him items of worship [such as p\'e4dya and arghya], one should worship Ke\'e7
ava, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.39 - In the beginning, the devotee should chant the dv\'e4da\'e7\'e4k\'f1
ara-mantra and offer flower garlands, incense and so on. After worshiping the Lord in this way, one should bathe the Lord with milk and dress Him with proper garments, a sacred thread, and ornaments. After offering water to was
h the Lord's feet, one should again worship the Lord with fragrant flowers, incense and other paraphernalia.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.40 - If one can afford to, one should offer the Deity fine rice boiled in milk with clarified butter and molasses. While chanting the same original mantra, one should offer all this to the fire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.41 - One should offer all the pras\'e4da to a Vai\'f1\'ebava or offer him some of the pras\'e4da and then take some oneself. After this, one should offer the Deity \'e4camana and then betel nut and then ag
ain worship the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.16.42 - Thereafter, one should silently murmur the mantra 108 times and offer prayers to the Lord for His glorification. Then one should circumambulate the Lord and finally, with great delight and satisfaction, offer obeisances,
 falling straight like a rod [da\'eb\'f2avat].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.43 - After touching to one's head all the flowers and water offered to the Deity, one should throw them into a sacred place. Then one should feed at least two br\'e4hma\'ebas with sweet rice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.44-45 - One should perfectly honor the respectable br\'e4hma\'ebas one has fed, and then, after taking their permission, one should take pras\'e4
da with his friends and relatives. For that night, one should observe strict celibacy, and the next morning, after bathing again, with purity and attention one should bathe the Deity of Vi\'f1\'eb
u with milk and worship Him according to the methods formerly stated in detail.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.46 - Worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with great faith and devotion and living only by drinking milk, one should follow this vow. One should also offer oblations to the fire and feed the br\'e4hma\'ebas as mentioned before.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.47 - In this way, until twelve days have passed, one should observe this payo-vrata, worshiping the Lord every day, executing the routine duties, performing sacrifices and feeding the br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.48 - From pratipat until the thirteenth day of the next bright moon [\'e7ukla-trayoda\'e7\'e9], one should observe complete celibacy, sleep on the floor, bathe three times a day and thus execute the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8
.16.49 - During this period, one should not unnecessarily talk of material subjects or topics of sense gratification, one should be completely free from envy of all living entities, and one should be a pure and simple devotee of Lord V\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.50 - Thereafter, following the directions of the \'e7\'e4stra with help from br\'e4hma\'ebas who know the \'e7\'e4stra, on the thirteenth day of the moon one should bathe Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u with five substances [milk, yogurt, ghee, sugar and honey].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.51-52 - Giving up the miserly habit of not spending money, one should arrange for the gorgeous worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who is situated in the heart of every living entity. With great attention, one must prepare an oblation of grains boiled in ghee and milk and must chant the Puru\'f1a-s\'fc
kta mantra. The offerings of food should be of varieties of tastes. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.53 - One should satisfy the spiritual master [\'e4c\'e4rya], who is very learned in Vedic literature, and should satisfy his assistant priests [known as hot\'e4, udg\'e4t\'e4
, adhvaryu and brahma]. One should please them by offering them clothing, ornaments and cows. This is the ceremony called vi\'f1\'ebu-\'e4r\'e4dhana, or worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.54 - O most auspicious lady, one should perform all the ceremonies under the direction of learned \'e4c\'e4ryas and should satisfy them and their priests. By distributing pras\'e4da, one should also satisfy the br\'e4hma
\'ebas and others who have assembled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.55 - One should satisfy the spiritual master and assistant priests by giving them cloth, ornaments, cows and also some monetary contribution. And by distributing pras\'e4
da one should satisfy everyone assembled, including even the lowest of men, the ca\'eb\'f2\'e4las [eaters of dog flesh].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.56 - One should distribute vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da to everyone, including the poor man, the blind man, the nondevotee and the non-br\'e4hma\'eba. Knowing that Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is very pleased when everyone is sumptuously fed with vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da, the performer of yaj\'efa should then take pras\'e4da with his friends and relatives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.57 - Every day from pratipat to trayoda\'e7\'e9, one should continue the ceremony, to the accompaniment of dancing, singing, the beating of a drum, the chanting of prayers and all-auspicious mantras, and recitation of \'c7r
\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.58 - This is the religious ritualistic ceremony known as payo-vrata, by which one may worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead. I received this information from Brahm\'e4
, my grandfather, and now I have described it to you in all details.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.59 - O most fortunate lady, establishing your mind in a good spirit, execute this process of payo-vrata and thus worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ke\'e7ava, who is inexhaustible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.60 - This payo-vrata is also known as sarva-yaj\'efa. In other words, by performing this sacrifice one can perform all other sacrifices automatically. This is also acknowledged to be the best of
 all ritualistic ceremonies. O gentle lady, it is the essence of all austerities, and it is the process of giving charity and pleasing the supreme controller.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.61 - This is the best process for pleasing the transcendental Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as Adhok\'f1
aja. It is the best of all regulative principles, the best austerity, the best process of giving charity, and the best process of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.62 - Therefore, my dear gentle lady, follow this ritualistic vow, strictly observing the regulative principles. By this process, the Supreme Person will very soon be pleased with you and will satisfy all your desires.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  16. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said: O King, when Aditi's sons, the demigods, had thus disappeared from heaven and the demons had occupied their places, Aditi began lamenting, as if she had no protector.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.2 - After many, many days, the great powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa Muni arose from a trance of meditation and returned home to see the \'e4\'e7rama of Aditi neither jubilant nor festive.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.3 - O best of the Kurus, when Ka\'e7yapa Muni had been properly received and welcomed, he took his seat and then spoke as follows to his wife, Aditi, who was very morose.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.4 - O most gentle one, I wonder whether anything inauspicious has now taken place in regard to religious principles, the br\'e4hma\'ebas or the people in general, who are subject to the whims of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.5 - O my wife, who are very much attached to household life, if the principles of religion, economic development 
and satisfaction of the senses are properly followed in household life, one's activities are as good as those of a transcendentalist. I wonder whether there have been any discrepancies in following these principles.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.6 - I wonder whether because of being too attached to the members of your family, you failed to properly receive uninvited guests, who therefore were not welcomed and went away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.7 - Homes from which guests go away without having been received even with an offering of a little water are like those holes in the field which are the homes of jackals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.8 - O chaste and auspicious woman, when I left home for other places, were you in so much anxiety that you did not offer oblations of ghee into the fire?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.9 - By worshiping the fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas, a householder can achieve the desired goal of residing in the higher planets, for the sacrificial fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas are to be considered the mouth of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu, who is the Supersoul of all the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.10 - O great-minded lady, are all your sons faring well? Seeing your withered face, I can perceive that your mind is not tranquil. How is this so?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.11 - Aditi said: O my respected br\'e4hma\'eba husband, all is well with the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the cows, religion and the welfare of other people. O master of the house, the three principles of dharma, artha and k\'e4
ma flourish in household life, which is consequently full of good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.12 - O beloved husband, the fires, guests, servants and beggars are all being properly cared for by me. Because I always think of you, there is no possibility that any of the religious principles will be neglected.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.13 - O my lord, since you are a Praj\'e4pati and are personally my instructor in the principles of religion, where is the possibility that all my desires will not be fulfilled?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.14 - O son of Mar\'e9ci, because you are a great personality you are equal toward all the demons and demigods, who are born either from your body or from your mind and who possess one 
or another of the three qualities-sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba or tamo-gu\'eba. But although the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the supreme controller, is equal toward all living entities, He is especially favorable to the devotees.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.15 - Therefore, most gentle lord, kindly favor your maidservant. We have now been deprived of our opulence and residence by our competitors, the demons. Kindly give us protection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.16 - The demons, our formidably powerful enemies, have taken away our opulence, our beauty, our fame and even our residence. Indeed, we have now been exiled, and we are drowning in an ocean of trouble.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.17 - O best of sages, best of all those who grant auspicious benedictions, please consider our situation and bestow upon my sons the benedictions by which they can regain what they have lost.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When Ka\'e7yapa Muni was thus requested by Aditi, he slightly smiled. "Alas," he said, "how powerful is the illusory energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, by which the entire 
world is bound by affection for children!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.19 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: What is this material body, made of five elements? It is different from the spirit soul. Indeed, the spirit soul is completely different from the material elements from which 
the body is made. But because of bodily attachment, one is regarded as a husband or son. These illusory relationships are caused by misunderstanding.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.20 - My dear Aditi, engage in devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the master of everything, who can subdue everyone's enemies, and who sits within everyone's heart. Only that Supreme Person-K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, or V\'e4sudeva-can bestow all auspicious benedictions upon everyone, for He is the spiritual master of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.21 -
 The Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is very merciful to the poor, will fulfill all of your desires, for devotional service unto Him is infallible. Any method other than devotional service is useless. That is my opinion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.22 - \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Aditi said: O br\'e4hma\'eba, tell me the regulative principles by which I may worship the supreme master of the world so that the Lord will be pleased with me and fulfill all my desires.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.23 - O best of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, kindly instruct me in the perfect method of 
worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead in devotional service, by which the Lord may very soon be pleased with me and save me, along with my sons, from this most dangerous condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.24 - \'c7r\'e9 Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: When I desired offspring, I placed inquiries before Lord Brahm\'e4, who is born from a lotus flower. Now I shall explain to you the same process Lord Brahm\'e4 instructed me, by which Ke
\'e7ava, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.25 - In the bright fortnight of the month of Ph\'e4lguna [February and March], for twelve days ending with Dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9
, one should observe the vow of subsisting only on milk and should worship the lotus-eyed Supreme Personality of Godhead with all devotion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.26 - If dirt dug up by a boar is available, on the day of the dark moon one should smear this dirt on his body and then bathe in a flowing river. While bathing, one should chant the following mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.27 - O mother earth, you were raised by the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the fo
rm of a boar because of your desiring to have a place to stay. I pray that you kindly vanquish all the reactions of my sinful life. I offer my respectful obeisances unto you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.28 - Thereafter, one should perform his daily spiritual duties and then,
 with great attention, offer worship to the Deity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and also to the altar, the sun, water, fire and the spiritual master.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.29 - O Supreme Personality of Godhead, greatest of all, who lives in everyone's heart and in whom everyone lives, O witness of everything, O V\'e4
sudeva, supreme and all-pervading person, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.30 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Person. Being very subtle, You are never visible to material eyes. You are the knower of the twenty-four elements, and You are the inaugurator of the s\'e4\'ec
khya-yoga system.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.31 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who have two heads [pr\'e4ya\'eb\'e9ya and ud\'e4yan\'e9
ya], three legs [savana-traya], four horns [the four Vedas] and seven hands [the seven chandas, such as G\'e4yatr\'e9]. I offer my obeisances unto You, whose heart and soul are the three Vedic rituals [karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a, j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2
a and up\'e4san\'e4-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a] and who expand these rituals in the form of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.32 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, Lord \'c7iva, or Rudra, who are the reservoir of all potencies, the reservoir of all knowledge, and the master of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.33 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are situated as Hira\'eb
yagarbha, the source of life, the Supersoul of every living entity. Your body is the source of the opulence of all mystic power. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.34 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are the original Personality of Godhead, the witness in everyone's heart, and the incarnation of Nara-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba \'c5\'f1
i in the form of a human being. O Personality of Godhead, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.35 - My Lord, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are dressed in yellow garments, whose bodily hue resembles the marakata gem, and who have full control over the goddess of fortune. O my Lord Ke\'e7
ava, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.36 - O most exalted and worshipable Lord, best of those who bestow benediction, You can fulfill the desires of everyone, and therefore those who are sober, for their own welfare, worship the dust of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.37 - All the demigods, as well as the goddess of fortune, engage in the service of His lotus feet. Indeed, they respect the fragrance of those lotus feet. May the Supreme Personality of Godhead be pleased with me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.38 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: By chanting all these mantras, welcoming the Supreme Personality of Godhead with faith and devotion, and offering Him items of worship [such as p\'e4dya and arghya], one should worship Ke\'e7
ava, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.39 - In the beginning, the devotee should chant the dv\'e4da\'e7\'e4k\'f1
ara-mantra and offer flower garlands, incense and so on. After worshiping the Lord in this way, one should bathe the Lord with milk and dress Him with proper garments, a sacred thread, and ornaments. After offering water to wash the Lord'
s feet, one should again worship the Lord with fragrant flowers, incense and other paraphernalia.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.40 - If one can afford to, one should offer the Deity fine rice boiled in milk with clarified butter and molasses. While chanting the same original mantra, one should offer all this to the fire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.41 - One should offer all the pras\'e4da to a Vai\'f1\'ebava or offer him some of the pras\'e4da and then take some oneself. After this, one should offer the Deity \'e4camana and then betel nut and then again worship
 the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.16.42 - Thereafter, one should silently murmur the mantra 108 times and offer prayers to the Lord for His glorification. Then one should circumambulate the Lord and finally, with great delight and satisfaction, offer obeisances, falling st
raight like a rod [da\'eb\'f2avat].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.43 - After touching to one's head all the flowers and water offered to the Deity, one should throw them into a sacred place. Then one should feed at least two br\'e4hma\'ebas with sweet rice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.44-45 - One should perfectly honor the respectable br\'e4hma\'ebas one has fed, and then, after taking their permission, one should take pras\'e4
da with his friends and relatives. For that night, one should observe strict celibacy, and the next morning, after bathing again, with purity and attention one should bathe the Deity of Vi\'f1\'eb
u with milk and worship Him according to the methods formerly stated in detail.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.46 - Worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with great faith and devotion and living only by drinking milk, one should follow this vow. One should also offer oblations to the fire and feed the br\'e4hma\'ebas as mentioned before.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.47 - In this way, until twelve days have passed, one should observe this payo-vrata, worshiping the Lord every day, executing the routine duties, performing sacrifices and feeding the br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.48 - From pratipat until the thirteenth day of the next bright moon [\'e7ukla-trayoda\'e7\'e9], one should observe complete celibacy, sleep on the floor, bathe three times a day and thus execute the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.49 - Du
ring this period, one should not unnecessarily talk of material subjects or topics of sense gratification, one should be completely free from envy of all living entities, and one should be a pure and simple devotee of Lord V\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.50 - Thereafter, following the directions of the \'e7\'e4stra with help from br\'e4hma\'ebas who know the \'e7\'e4stra, on the thirteenth day of the moon one should bathe Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u with five substances [milk, yogurt, ghee, sugar and honey].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.51-52 - Giving up the miserly habit of not spending money, one should arrange for the gorgeous worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who is situated in the heart of every living entity. With great attention, one must prepare an oblation of grains boiled in ghee and milk and must chant the Puru\'f1a-s\'fc
kta mantra. The offerings of food should be of varieties of tastes. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.53 - One should satisfy the spiritual master [\'e4c\'e4rya], who is very learned in Vedic literature, and should satisfy his assistant priests [known as hot\'e4, udg\'e4t\'e4
, adhvaryu and brahma]. One should please them by offering them clothing, ornaments and cows. This is the ceremony called vi\'f1\'ebu-\'e4r\'e4dhana, or worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.54 - O most auspicious lady, one should perform all the ceremonies under the direction of learned \'e4c\'e4ryas and should satisfy them and their priests. By distributing pras\'e4da, one should also satisfy the br\'e4hma
\'ebas and others who have assembled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.55 - One should satisfy the spiritual master and assistant priests by giving them cloth, ornaments, cows and also some monetary contribution. And by distributing pras\'e4
da one should satisfy everyone assembled, including even the lowest of men, the ca\'eb\'f2\'e4las [eaters of dog flesh].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.56 - One should distribute vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da to everyone, including the poor man, the blind man, the nondevotee and the non-br\'e4hma\'eba. Knowing that Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is very pleased when everyone is sumptuously fed with vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da, the performer of yaj\'efa should then take pras\'e4da with his friends and relatives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.57 - Every day from pratipat to trayoda\'e7\'e9, one should continue the ceremony, to the accompaniment of dancing, singing, the beating of a drum, the chanting of prayers and all-auspicious mantras, and recitation of \'c7r
\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.58 - This is the religious ritualistic ceremony known as payo-vrata, by which one may worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead. I received this information from Brahm\'e4
, my grandfather, and now I have described it to you in all details.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.59 - O most fortunate lady, establishing your mind in a good spirit, execute this process of payo-vrata and thus worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ke\'e7ava, who is inexhaustible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.60 - This payo-vrata is also known as sarva-yaj\'efa. In other words, by performing this sacrifice one can perform all other sacrifices automatically. This is also acknowledged to be the best of all ritual
istic ceremonies. O gentle lady, it is the essence of all austerities, and it is the process of giving charity and pleasing the supreme controller.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.61 - This is the best process for pleasing the transcendental Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as Adhok\'f1
aja. It is the best of all regulative principles, the best austerity, the best process of giving charity, and the best process of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.62 - Therefore, my dear gentle lady, follow this ritualistic vow, strictly observing the regulative principles. By this process, the Supreme Person will very soon be pleased with you and will satisfy all your desires.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116 Executing the Payo-vrata Process of Worship
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, when Aditi's sons, the demigods, had thus disappeared from heaven and the demons had occ
upied their places, Aditi began lamenting, as if she had no protector.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.2 - After many, many days, the great powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa Muni arose from a trance of meditation and returned home to see the \'e4\'e7rama of Aditi neither jubilant nor festive.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.3 - O best of the Kurus, when Ka\'e7yapa Muni had been properly received and welcomed, he took his seat and then spoke as follows to his wife, Aditi, who was very morose.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.4 - O most gentle one, I wonder whether anything inauspicious has now taken place in regard to religious principles, the br\'e4hma\'ebas or the people in general, who are subject to the whims of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.5 - O my wife, who are very much attached to household life, if the principles of religion, economic development and satisfa
ction of the senses are properly followed in household life, one's activities are as good as those of a transcendentalist. I wonder whether there have been any discrepancies in following these principles.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.6 - I wonder whether because of being too attached to the members of your family, you failed to properly receive uninvited guests, who therefore were not welcomed and went away.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.7 - Homes from which guests go away without having been received even with an offering of a little water are like those holes in the field which are the homes of jackals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.8 - O chaste and auspicious woman, when I left home for other places, were you in so much anxiety that you did not offer oblations of ghee into the fire?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.9 - By worshiping the fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas, a householder can achieve the desired goal of residing in the higher planets, for the sacrificial fire and the br\'e4hma\'ebas are to be considered the mouth of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu, who is the Supersoul of all the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.10 - O great-minded lady, are all your sons faring well? Seeing your withered face, I can perceive that your mind is not tranquil. How is this so?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.11 - Aditi said: O my respected br\'e4hma\'eba husband, all is well with the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the cows, religion and the welfare of other people. O master of the house, the three principles of dharma, artha and k\'e4
ma flourish in household life, which is consequently full of good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.12 - O beloved husband, the fires, guests, servants and beggars are all being properly cared for by me. Because I always think of you, there is no possibility that any of the religious principles will be neglected.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.13 - O my lord, since you are a Praj\'e4pati and are personally my instructor in the principles of religion, where is the possibility that all my desires will not be fulfilled?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.14 - O son of Mar\'e9ci, because you are a great personality you are equal toward all the demons and demigods, who are born either from your body or from your mind and who possess one or another 
of the three qualities-sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba or tamo-gu\'eba. But although the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the supreme controller, is equal toward all living entities, He is especially favorable to the devotees.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.15 - Therefore, most gentle lord, kindly favor your maidservant. We have now been deprived of our opulence and residence by our competitors, the demons. Kindly give us protection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.16 - The demons, our formidably powerful enemies, have taken away our opulence, our beauty, our fame and even our residence. Indeed, we have now been exiled, and we are drowning in an ocean of trouble.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.17 - O best of sages, best of all those who grant auspicious benedictions, please consider our situation and bestow upon my sons the benedictions by which they can regain what they have lost.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When Ka\'e7yapa Muni was thus requested by Aditi, he slightly smiled. "Alas," he said, "how powerful is the illusory energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, by which the entire world is bo
und by affection for children!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.19 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: What is this material body, made of five elements? It is different from the spirit soul. Indeed, the spirit soul is completely different from the material elements from which the body is
 made. But because of bodily attachment, one is regarded as a husband or son. These illusory relationships are caused by misunderstanding.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.20 - My dear Aditi, engage in devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the master of everything, who can subdue everyone's enemies, and who sits within everyone's heart. Only that Supreme Person-K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, or V\'e4sudeva-can bestow all auspicious benedictions upon everyone, for He is the spiritual master of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.21 - The Suprem
e Personality of Godhead, who is very merciful to the poor, will fulfill all of your desires, for devotional service unto Him is infallible. Any method other than devotional service is useless. That is my opinion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.22 - \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Aditi said: O br\'e4hma\'eba, tell me the regulative principles by which I may worship the supreme master of the world so that the Lord will be pleased with me and fulfill all my desires.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.23 - O best of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, kindly instruct me in the perfect method of worshiping 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead in devotional service, by which the Lord may very soon be pleased with me and save me, along with my sons, from this most dangerous condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.24 - \'c7r\'e9 Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: When I desired offspring, I placed inquiries before Lord Brahm\'e4, who is born from a lotus flower. Now I shall explain to you the same process Lord Brahm\'e4 instructed me, by which Ke
\'e7ava, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is satisfied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.25 - In the bright fortnight of the month of Ph\'e4lguna [February and March], for twelve days ending with Dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9
, one should observe the vow of subsisting only on milk and should worship the lotus-eyed Supreme Personality of Godhead with all devotion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.26 - If dirt dug up by a boar is available, on the day of the dark moon one should smear this dirt on his body and then bathe in a flowing river. While bathing, one should chant the following mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.27 - O mother earth, you were raised by the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of a boa
r because of your desiring to have a place to stay. I pray that you kindly vanquish all the reactions of my sinful life. I offer my respectful obeisances unto you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.28 - Thereafter, one should perform his daily spiritual duties and then, with great
 attention, offer worship to the Deity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and also to the altar, the sun, water, fire and the spiritual master.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.29 - O Supreme Personality of Godhead, greatest of all, who lives in everyone's heart and in whom everyone lives, O witness of everything, O V\'e4
sudeva, supreme and all-pervading person, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.30 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Person. Being very subtle, You are never visible to material eyes. You are the knower of the twenty-four elements, and You are the inaugurator of the s\'e4\'ec
khya-yoga system.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.31 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who have two heads [pr\'e4ya\'eb\'e9ya and ud\'e4yan\'e9ya], thre
e legs [savana-traya], four horns [the four Vedas] and seven hands [the seven chandas, such as G\'e4yatr\'e9]. I offer my obeisances unto You, whose heart and soul are the three Vedic rituals [karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a, j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a and up\'e4san
\'e4-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a] and who expand these rituals in the form of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.32 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, Lord \'c7iva, or Rudra, who are the reservoir of all potencies, the reservoir of all knowledge, and the master of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.33 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are situated as Hira\'eb
yagarbha, the source of life, the Supersoul of every living entity. Your body is the source of the opulence of all mystic power. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.34 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are the original Personality of Godhead, the witness in everyone's heart, and the incarnation of Nara-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba \'c5\'f1
i in the form of a human being. O Personality of Godhead, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.35 - My Lord, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are dressed in yellow garments, whose bodily hue resembles the marakata gem, and who have full control over the goddess of fortune. O my Lord Ke\'e7
ava, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.36 - O most exalted and worshipable Lord, best of those who bestow benediction, You can fulfill the desires of everyone, and therefore those who are sober, for their own welfare, worship the dust of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.37 - All the demigods, as well as the goddess of fortune, engage in the service of His lotus feet. Indeed, they respect the fragrance of those lotus feet. May the Supreme Personality of Godhead be pleased with me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.38 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: By chanting all these mantras, welcoming the Supreme Personality of Godhead with faith and devotion, and offering Him items of worship [such as p\'e4dya and arghya], one should worship Ke\'e7
ava, H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.39 - In the beginning, the devotee should chant the dv\'e4da\'e7\'e4k\'f1
ara-mantra and offer flower garlands, incense and so on. After worshiping the Lord in this way, one should bathe the Lord with milk and dress Him with proper garments, a sacred thread, and ornaments. After offering water to wash the Lord's feet, one
 should again worship the Lord with fragrant flowers, incense and other paraphernalia.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.40 - If one can afford to, one should offer the Deity fine rice boiled in milk with clarified butter and molasses. While chanting the same original mantra, one should offer all this to the fire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.41 - One should offer all the pras\'e4da to a Vai\'f1\'ebava or offer him some of the pras\'e4da and then take some oneself. After this, one should offer the Deity \'e4
camana and then betel nut and then again worship the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.16.42 - Thereafter, one should silently murmur the mantra 108 times and offer prayers to the Lord for His glorification. Then one should circumambulate the Lord and finally, with great delight and satisfaction, offer obeisances, falling straight like
 a rod [da\'eb\'f2avat].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.43 - After touching to one's head all the flowers and water offered to the Deity, one should throw them into a sacred place. Then one should feed at least two br\'e4hma\'ebas with sweet rice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.44-45 - One should perfectly honor the respectable br\'e4hma\'ebas one has fed, and then, after taking their permission, one should take pras\'e4
da with his friends and relatives. For that night, one should observe strict celibacy, and the next morning, after bathing again, with purity and attention one should bathe the Deity of Vi\'f1\'eb
u with milk and worship Him according to the methods formerly stated in detail.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.46 - Worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with great faith and devotion and living only by drinking milk, one should follow this vow. One should also offer oblations to the fire and feed the br\'e4hma\'ebas as mentioned before.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.47 - In this way, until twelve days have passed, one should observe this payo-vrata, worshiping the Lord every day, executing the routine duties, performing sacrifices and feeding the br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.48 - From pratipat until the thirteenth day of the next bright moon [\'e7ukla-trayoda\'e7\'e9], one should observe complete celibacy, sleep on the floor, bathe three times a day and thus execute the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.49 - During this p
eriod, one should not unnecessarily talk of material subjects or topics of sense gratification, one should be completely free from envy of all living entities, and one should be a pure and simple devotee of Lord V\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.50 - Thereafter, following the directions of the \'e7\'e4stra with help from br\'e4hma\'ebas who know the \'e7\'e4stra, on the thirteenth day of the moon one should bathe Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u with five substances [milk, yogurt, ghee, sugar and honey].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.51-52 - Giving up the miserly habit of not spending money, one should arrange for the gorgeous worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who is situated in the heart of every living entity. With great attention, one must prepare an oblation of grains boiled in ghee and milk and must chant the Puru\'f1a-s\'fc
kta mantra. The offerings of food should be of varieties of tastes. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.53 - One should satisfy the spiritual master [\'e4c\'e4rya], who is very learned in Vedic literature, and should satisfy his assistant priests [known as hot\'e4, udg\'e4t\'e4
, adhvaryu and brahma]. One should please them by offering them clothing, ornaments and cows. This is the ceremony called vi\'f1\'ebu-\'e4r\'e4dhana, or worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.54 - O most auspicious lady, one should perform all the ceremonies under the direction of learned \'e4c\'e4ryas and should satisfy them and their priests. By distributing pras\'e4da, one should also satisfy the br\'e4hma
\'ebas and others who have assembled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.55 - One should satisfy the spiritual master and assistant priests by giving them cloth, ornaments, cows and also some monetary contribution. And by distributing pras\'e4
da one should satisfy everyone assembled, including even the lowest of men, the ca\'eb\'f2\'e4las [eaters of dog flesh].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.56 - One should distribute vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da to everyone, including the poor man, the blind man, the nondevotee and the non-br\'e4hma\'eba. Knowing that Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is very pleased when everyone is sumptuously fed with vi\'f1\'ebu-pras\'e4da, the performer of yaj\'efa should then take pras\'e4da with his friends and relatives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.57 - Every day from pratipat to trayoda\'e7\'e9, one should continue the ceremony, to the accompaniment of dancing, singing, the beating of a drum, the chanting of prayers and all-auspicious mantras, and recitation of \'c7r
\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam. In this way, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.58 - This is the religious ritualistic ceremony known as payo-vrata, by which one may worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead. I received this information from Brahm\'e4
, my grandfather, and now I have described it to you in all details.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.59 - O most fortunate lady, establishing your mind in a good spirit, execute this process of payo-vrata and thus worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ke\'e7ava, who is inexhaustible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.60 - This payo-vrata is also known as sarva-yaj\'efa. In other words, by performing this sacrifice one can perform all other sacrifices automatically. This is also acknowledged to be the best of all ritualistic cerem
onies. O gentle lady, it is the essence of all austerities, and it is the process of giving charity and pleasing the supreme controller.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.61 - This is the best process for pleasing the transcendental Supreme Personality of Godhead, known as Adhok\'f1a
ja. It is the best of all regulative principles, the best austerity, the best process of giving charity, and the best process of sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.16.62 - Therefore, my dear gentle lady, follow this ritualistic vow, strictly observing the regulative principles. By this process, the Supreme Person will very soon be pleased with you and will satisfy all your desires.

