\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, after Aditi was thus advised by her husband, Ka\'e7yapa Muni, she strictly followed his instructions without laziness and in this way performed the payo-vrata ritualistic ceremony.

\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.2-3 - With full, undiverted attention, Aditi thought of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and in this way brought under full control her mind and senses, which resembl
ed forceful horses. She concentrated her mind upon the Supreme Lord, V\'e4sudeva. Thus she performed the ritualistic ceremony known as payo-vrata.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.4 - My dear King, the original Supreme Personality of Godhead, dressed in yellow garments and bearing a conchshell, disc, club and lotus in His four hands, then appeared before Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.5 - When the Supreme Personality of Godhead became visible to Aditi's eyes, Aditi was so overwhelmed by transcendental bliss that she at once stood up and then fell t
o the ground like a rod to offer the Lord her respectful obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.6 - Aditi stood silently with folded hands, unable to offer prayers to the Lord. Because of transcendental bliss, tears filled her eyes, and the hairs on her body stood on end. B
ecause she could see the Supreme Personality of Godhead face to face, she felt ecstasy, and her body trembled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.7 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, the demigoddess Aditi then began offering her prayers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead in a faltering voic
e and with great love. She appeared as though drinking through her eyes the Supreme Lord, who is the husband of the goddess of fortune, the enjoyer of all sacrificial ceremonies, and the master and Lord of the entire universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.8 - The goddess Adit
i said: O master and enjoyer of all sacrificial ceremonies, O infallible and most famous person, whose name, when chanted, spreads all good fortune! O original Supreme Personality of Godhead, supreme controller, shelter of all holy places, You are the she
lter of all poor, suffering living entities, and You have appeared to diminish their suffering. Please be kind to us and spread our good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.9 - My Lord, You are the all-pervading universal form, the fully independent creator, maintainer and d
estroyer of this universe. Although You engage Your energy in matter, You are always situated in Your original form and never fall from that position, for Your knowledge is infallible and always suitable to any situation. You are never bewildered by illus
ion. O my Lord, let me offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.10 - O unlimited one, if Your Lordship is satisfied, one can very easily obtain a lifetime as long as that of Lord Brahm\'e4, a body either in the upper, lower or middle planetary systems
, unlimited material opulence, religion, economic development and satisfaction of the senses, full transcendental knowledge, and the eight yogic perfections, what to speak of such petty achievements as conquering one's rivals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.11 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, best of the Bharata dynasty, when the lotus-eyed Lord, the Supersoul of all living entities, was thus worshiped by Aditi, He replied as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.12 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O mother of the demigods, I hav
e already understood your long-cherished desires for the welfare of your sons, who have been deprived of all opulences and driven from their residence by their enemies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.13 - O Dev\'e9, O goddess, I can understand that you want to regain your sons and be together with them to worship Me, after defeating the enemies in battle and retrieving your abode and opulences.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.14 - You want to see the wives of the demons lamenting for the death of their husbands when those demons, the enemies of your sons, are killed in battle by the demigods, of whom Indra is the chief.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.15 - You want your sons to regain their lost reputation and opulence and live again on their heavenly planet as usual.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.16 - O mother of the demigods, in My opinion almost all the chiefs of the demons are now unconquerable, for they are being protected by br\'e4hma\'eb
as, whom the Supreme Lord always favors. Thus the use of power against them now will not at all be a source of happiness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.17 - Yet because I have been sati
sfied by the activities of your vow, O goddess Aditi, I must find some means to favor you, for worship of Me never goes in vain but certainly gives the desired result according to what one deserves.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.18 - You have prayed to Me and properly worshiped Me by performing the great payo-vrata ceremony for the sake of protecting your sons. Because of Ka\'e7
yapa Muni's austerities, I shall agree to become your son and thus protect your other sons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.19 - Always thinking of Me as being situated within the body of your husband, Ka\'e7yapa, go worship your husband, who has been purified by his austerity.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.20 - O lady, even if someone inquires, you should not disclose this fact to anyone. That which is very confidential is successful if kept secret.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.21 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said: After speaking in this way, the Supreme Personality of Godhead disappeared from that very spot. Aditi, having received the extremely valuable benediction that the Lord would appear as her son, considered herself very succe
ssful, and with great devotion she approached her husband.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.22 - Being situated in a meditational trance, Ka\'e7yapa Muni, whose vision is never mistaken, could see that a plenary portion of the Supreme Personality of Godhead had entered within him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.23 - O King, as the wind promotes friction between two pieces of wood and thus gives rise to fire, Ka\'e7
yapa Muni, whose transcendental position was fully absorbed in the Supreme Personality of Godhead, transferred his potency into the womb of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.24 - When Lord Brahm\'e4 understood that the Supreme Personality of Godhead was now within the womb of Aditi, he began to offer prayers to the Lord by reciting transcendental names.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.25 - Lord Brahm\'e4 said: O Supreme Personality of Godhead, a
ll glories unto You, who are glorified by all and whose activities are all uncommon. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, O Lord of the transcendentalists, controller of the three modes of nature. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You again and 
again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.26 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, the all-pervading Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who have entered the cores of the hearts of all living entities. All the three worlds reside within Your navel, yet You are above the three worlds. Formerly You appeared as the son of P\'e5\'e7
ni. To You, the supreme creator, who are understood only through Vedic knowledge, I offer my respectful obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.27 - O my Lord, You are the beginning, the manifestation and the ultimate dissolution of the three worlds, 
and You are celebrated in the Vedas as the reservoir of unlimited potencies, the Supreme Person. O my Lord, as waves attract branches and leaves that have fallen into deep water, You, the supreme eternal time factor, attract everything in this universe.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.17.28 - My Lord, You are the original generator of all living entities, stationary or moving, and You are also the generator of the Praj\'e4
patis. O my Lord, as a boat is the only hope for a person drowning in the water, You are the only shelter for the demigods, who are now bereft of their heavenly position.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
