{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: After Lord Brahm\'e4
 had thus spoken, glorifying the Supreme Lord's activities and prowess, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is never subject to death like an ordinary living being, appeared from the womb of Aditi. His four hands were decorated with a conchshell, club
, lotus and disc, He was dressed in yellow garments, and His eyes appeared like the petals of a blooming lotus.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.2 - The body of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, blackish in complexion, was free from all inebrieties. His lotus face, decorated wi
th earrings resembling sharks, appeared very beautiful, and on His bosom was the mark of \'c7r\'e9
vatsa. He wore bangles on His wrists, armlets on His arms, a helmet on His head, a belt on His waist, a sacred thread across His chest, and ankle bells decorating His lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.18.3 - An uncommonly beautiful garland of flowers decorated His bosom, and because the flowers were extremely fragrant, a large group of bees, making their natural humming sounds, invaded them for honey. When the Lord appeared, wearing
 the Kaustubha gem on His neck, His effulgence vanquished the darkness in the home of the Praj\'e4pati Ka\'e7yapa.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.4 - At that time, there was happiness in all directions, in the reservoirs of water like the rivers and oceans, and in the core of everyon
e's heart. The various seasons displayed their respective qualities, and all living entities in the upper planetary system, in outer space and on the surface of the earth were jubilant. The demigods, the cows, the br\'e4hma\'eb
as and the hills and mountains were all filled with joy.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.5 - On the day of \'c7rava\'eba-dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9 [the twelfth day of the bright fortnight in the month of Bh\'e4dra], when the moon came into the lunar mansion \'c7rava\'eb
a, at the auspicious moment of Abhijit, the Lord appeared in this universe. Considering the Lord's appearance very auspicious, all the stars and planets, from the sun to Saturn, were munificently charitable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.6 - O King, when the Lord appeared-on dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9, the twelfth day of the moon-the sun was at the meridian, as every learned scholar knows. This dv\'e4da\'e7\'e9 is called Vijay\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.7 - Conchshells, kettledrums, drums, pa\'ebavas and \'e4nakas vibrated in concert. The sound of these and various other instruments was tumultuous.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.8 - Being very pleased, the celestial dancing girls [Apsar\'e4s] danced in jubilation, the best of the Gandharvas sang songs, and the great sages, demigods, Manus, Pit\'e4s and fire-gods offered prayers to satisfy the Lord.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.9-10 - The Siddhas, Vidy\'e4dharas, Kimpuru\'f1as, Kinnaras, C\'e4ra\'ebas, Yak\'f1as, R\'e4k\'f1asas, Supar\'eb
as, the best of serpents, and the followers of the demigods all showered flowers on Aditi's residence, covering the entire house, while glorifying and praising the Lord and dancing.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.11 - When Aditi saw the Supreme Personality of Godh
ead, who had appeared from her own womb, having accepted a transcendental body by His own spiritual potency, she was struck with wonder and was very happy. Upon seeing the child, Praj\'e4pati Ka\'e7
yapa exclaimed, "Jaya! Jaya!" in great happiness and wonder.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB
 8.18.12 - The Lord appeared in His original form, with ornaments and weapons in His hands. Although this ever-existing form is not visible in the material world, He nonetheless appeared in this form. Then, in the presence of His father and mother, He ass
umed the form of V\'e4mana, a br\'e4hma\'eba-dwarf, a brahmac\'e4r\'e9, just like a theatrical actor.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.13 - When the great sages saw the Lord as the brahmac\'e4r\'e9-dwarf V\'e4mana, they were certainly very pleased. Thus they placed before them Ka\'e7yapa Muni, the Praj\'e4pati
, and performed all the ritualistic ceremonies, such as the birthday ceremony.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.14 - At the sacred thread ceremony of V\'e4manadeva, the sun-god personally uttered the G\'e4yatr\'e9 mantra, B\'e5haspati offered the sacred thread, and Ka\'e7yapa Muni offered a straw belt.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.15 - Mother earth gave Him a deerskin, and the demigod of the moon, who is the king of the forest, gave Him a brahma-da\'eb\'f2a [the rod of a brahmac\'e4r\'e9
]. His mother, Aditi, gave Him cloth for underwear, and the deity presiding over the heavenly kingdom offered Him an umbrella.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.16 - O King, Lord Brahm\'e4 offered a waterpot to the inexhaustible Supreme Personality of Godhead, the seven sages offered Him ku\'e7a grass, and mother Sarasvat\'e9 gave Him a string of Rudr\'e4k\'f1a beads.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.17 - When V\'e4manadeva had thus been given the sacred thread, Kuvera, King of the Yak\'f1as, gave Him a pot for begging alms, and mother Bhagavat\'e9, the wife of Lord \'c7
iva and most chaste mother of the entire universe, gave Him His first alms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.18 - Having thus been welcomed by everyone, Lord V\'e4manadeva, the best of the brahmac\'e4r\'e9s, exhibited His Brahman effulgence. Thus He surpassed in beauty that entire assembly, which was filled with great saintly br
\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.19 - After Lord \'c7r\'e9 V\'e4manadeva set a sacrificial fire, He offered worship and performed a fire sacrifice on the sacrificial field.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.20 - When the Lord heard that Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was performing a\'e7vamedha sacrifices under the patronage of br\'e4hma\'ebas belonging to the Bh\'e5gu dynasty, the Supreme Lo
rd, who is full in every respect, proceeded there to show His mercy to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja. By His weight, He pushed down the earth with every step.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.21 - While engaged in performing the sacrifice in the field known as Bh\'e5gukaccha, on the northern bank of the Narmad\'e4 River, the brahminical priests, the descendants of Bh\'e5gu, saw V\'e4
manadeva to be like the sun rising nearby.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.22 - O King, because of V\'e4manadeva's bright effulgence, the priests, along with Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and all the members of the assem
bly, were robbed of their splendor. Thus they began to ask one another whether the sun-god himself, Sanat-kum\'e4ra or the fire-god had personally come to see the sacrificial ceremony.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.23 - While the priests of the Bh\'e5gu dynasty and their disciples talked and argued in various ways, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4
manadeva, holding in His hands the rod, the umbrella and a waterpot full of water, entered the arena of the a\'e7vamedha sacrifice.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.24-25 - Appearing as a br\'e4hma\'eba boy, wearing a belt of straw, a sacred thread, an upper garment of deerskin, and matted locks of hair, Lord V\'e4
manadeva entered the arena of sacrifice. His brilliant effulgence diminished the brilliance of all the priests and their disciples, who thus stood from their seats and welcomed the Lord properly by offering obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.26 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, jubilant at seeing Lord V\'e4manadeva, whose beautiful limbs contributed equally to the beauty of His entire body, offered Him a seat with great satisfaction.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.27 - Thus offering a proper reception to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is always beautiful to the liberated souls, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja worshiped Him by washing His lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.28 - Lord \'c7iva, the best of demigods, who carries on his forehead the emblem of the moon, receives on his head with great devotion the Ganges water emanating from the toe of Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Being aware of religious principles, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja knew this. Consequently, following in the footsteps of Lord \'c7iva, he also placed on his head the water that had washed the Lord's lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.29 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja then said to Lord V\'e4manadeva: O br\'e4hma\'eba, I offer You my hearty welcome and my respectful obeisances. Please let us know what we may do for You. We think of You as the personified 
austerity of the great br\'e4hma\'eba-sages.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.30 - O my Lord, because You have kindly arrived at our home, all my forefathers are satisfied, our family and entire dynasty have been sanctified, and the sacrifice we are performing is now complete because o
f Your presence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.31 - O son of a br\'e4hma\'eba, today the fire of sacrifice is ablaze according to the injunction of the \'e7\'e4
stra, and I have been freed from all the sinful reactions of my life by the water that has washed Your lotus feet. O my Lord, by the touch of Your small lotus feet the entire surface of the world has been sanctified.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.18.32 - O son of a br\'e4hma\'eba, it appears that You have come here to ask me for something. Therefore, whatever You want You may take from me. O best of those who ar
e worshipable. You may take from me a cow, gold, a furnished house, palatable food and drink, the daughter of a br\'e4hma\'eba for Your wife, prosperous villages, horses, elephants, chariots or whatever You desire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
