{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When Lord Brahm\'e4, who was born of a lotus flower, saw that the effulgence of his residence, Brahmaloka, had been reduced by the glaring effulgence from the toenails of Lord V\'e4
manadeva, he approached the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Lord Brahm\'e4 was accompanied by all the great sages, headed by Mar\'e9ci, and by yog\'e9s like Sanandana, but in the presence of that glaring effulgence, O King, even Lord Brahm\'e4
 and his associates seemed insignificant.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.2-3 - Among the great personalities who came to worship the lotus feet of t
he Lord were those who had attained perfection in self-control and regulative principles, as well as experts in logic, history, general education and the Vedic literature known as kalpe [dealing with old historical incidents]. Others were experts in the V
edic corollaries like Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4, all the other knowledge of the Vedas [S\'e4ma, Yajur, \'c5g and Atharva], and also the supplementary Vedic knowledge [\'c4
yur-veda, Dhanur-veda, etc.]. Others were those who had been freed of the reactions to fruitive activities
 by transcendental knowledge awakened by practice of yoga. And still others were those who had attained residence in Brahmaloka not by ordinary karma but by advanced Vedic knowledge. After devotedly worshiping the upraised lotus feet of the Supreme Lord w
ith oblations of water, Lord Brahm\'e4, who was born of the lotus emanating from Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's navel, offered prayers to the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.4 - O King, the water from Lord Brahm\'e4's kama\'eb\'f2alu washed the lotus feet of Lord V\'e4manadeva, who is known as Urukrama, th
e wonderful actor. Thus that water became so pure that it was transformed into the water of the Ganges, which went flowing down from the sky, purifying the three worlds like the pure fame of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.5 - Lord Brahm\'e4 and all the predominating deities of the various planetary systems began to worship Lord V\'e4
manadeva, their supreme master, who had reduced Himself from His all-pervading form to His original form. They collected all the ingredients and paraphernalia for this worship.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.6-7 - They worshiped the Lord by offering fragrant flowers, water, p\'e4
dya and arghya, sandalwood pulp and aguru pulp, incense, lamps, fused rice, unbroken grains, fruits, roots and sprouts. While so doing, they offered prayers indicating th
e glorious activities of the Lord and shouted "Jaya! Jaya!" They also danced, played instruments, sang, sounded conchshells and beat kettledrums, in this way worshiping the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.8 - J\'e4mbav\'e4n, king of the bears, also joined in the ceremony. Sounding his bugle in all directions, he declared a great festival for Lord V\'e4manadeva's victory.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.9 - When the demoniac followers of Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali saw that their master, who had been determined in performing sacrifice, had lost all his possessions to V\'e4
manadeva, who had taken them away on the plea of begging three paces of land, they were very angry and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.10 - "This V\'e4mana is certainly not a br\'e4hma\'eba but the best of cheaters, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Assuming the form of a br\'e4hma\'eba, He has co
vered His own form, and thus He is working for the interests of the demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.21.11 - "Our lord, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, because of his position in performing the yaj\'efa, has given up the power to punish. Taking advantage of this, our eternal enemy, Vi\'f1\'ebu, dressed in the form of a brahmac\'e4r\'e9
