ja, without duplicity, has now offered everything in the three worlds. How then can he deserve to suffer from arrest?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.24 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: My dear Lord Brahm\'e4, because of material opulence a foolish person becomes dull-witted and mad. Thus he has no respect for anyone within the three worlds and defies even 
My authority. To such a person I show special favor by first taking away all his possessions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.25 - While rotating in the cycle of birth and death again and again in different species because of his own fruitive activities, the dependent living ent
ity, by good fortune, may happen to become a human being. This human birth is very rarely obtained.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.26 - If a human being is born in an aristocratic family or a higher status of life, if he performs wonderful activities, if he is youthful, if he h
as personal beauty, a good education and good wealth, and if he is nonetheless not proud of his opulences, it is to be understood that he is especially favored by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.27 - Although aristocratic birth and other such 
opulences are impediments to advancement in devotional service because they are causes of false prestige and pride, these opulences never disturb a pure devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.28 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has become the most famous among the demons and nonbelievers, for in spite of being bereft of all material opulences, he is fixed in his devotional service.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.29-30 - Although bereft of his riches, fallen from his original position, defeated and arrested by his enemies, rebuke
d and deserted by his relatives and friends, although suffering the pain of being bound and although rebuked and cursed by his spiritual master, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, being fixed in his vow, did not give up his truthfulness. It was certainly with pretension that I spoke about religious principles, but he did not give up religious principles, for he is true to his word.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.31 - The Lord continued: Because of his great tolerance, I have given him a place not obtainable even by the demigods. He will become King of the heavenly planets during the period of the Manu known as S\'e4var\'ebi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.32 - Until Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja achieves the position of King of heaven, he shall live on the planet Sutala, which was made by Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4 according to My order. Because it is especi
ally protected by Me, it is free from mental and bodily miseries, fatigue, dizziness, defeat and all other disturbances. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, you may now go live there peacefully.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.33 - O Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja [Indrasena], now you may go to the planet Sutala, which is desired even by the demigods. Live there peacefully, surrounded by your friends and relatives. All good fortune unto you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.34 - On the planet Sutala, not even the predominating deities of other planets, what to speak of ordinary people, will
 be able to conquer you. As far as the demons are concerned, if they transgress your rule, My disc will kill them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.35 - O great hero, I shall always be with you and give you protection in all respects along with your associates and paraphernalia. Moreover, you will always be able to see Me there.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.36 - Because there you will see My supreme prowess, your materialistic ideas and anxieties that have arisen from your association with the demons and D\'e4navas will immediately be vanquished.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116 Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Surrenders His Life
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid4605116   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, although the Supreme Personality of Godhead was superficially seen to have acted mischievously toward Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was fixed in his determination. Considering himself not to have fulfilled his promise, he spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.2 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja said: O best Personality of Godhead, most worshipable for all the demigods, if You think that my promise has become false, I shall certainly rectify matters to make it truthful. I cannot allow my promise to
 be false. Please, therefore, place Your third lotus footstep on my head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.3 - I do not fear being deprived of all my possessions, living in hellish life, being arrested for poverty by the ropes of Varu\'eba or being punished by You as much as I fear defamation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.22.4 - Although a father, mother, brother or friend may sometimes punish one as a well-wisher, they never punish their subordinate like this. But because You are the most worshipable Lord, I regard the punishment You have given me as most exalted.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.22.5 - Since Your Lordship is indirectly the greatest well-wisher of us demons, You act for our best welfare by posing as if our enemy. Because demons like us always aspire for a position of false prestige, by chastising us You give us the 
eyes by which to see the right path.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.6-7 - Many demons who were continuously inimical toward You finally achieved the perfection of great mystic yog\'e9s. Your Lordship can perform one work to serve many purposes, and consequently, although You have 
punished me in many ways, I do not feel ashamed of having been arrested by the ropes of Varu\'eba, nor do I feel aggrieved.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.8 - My grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja is famous, being recognized by all Your devotees. Although harassed in many ways by his father, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu, he still remained faithful, taking shelter at Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.9 - What is the use of the material body, which automatically leaves its owner at the end of life? And what is the use of all one's family members, who are actual
ly plunderers taking away money that is useful for the service of the Lord in spiritual opulence? What is the use of a wife? She is only the source of increasing material conditions. And what is the use of family, home, country and community? Attachment f
or them merely wastes the valuable energy of one's lifetime.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.10 - My grandfather, the best of all men, who achieved unlimited knowledge and was worshipable for everyone, was afraid of the common men in this world. Being fully convinced of the subst
antiality afforded by shelter at Your lotus feet, He took shelter of Your lotus feet, against the will of his father and demoniac friends, who were killed by Your own self.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.11 - Only by providence have I been forcibly brought under Your lotus feet
 and deprived of all my opulence. Because of the illusion created by temporary opulence, people in general, who live under material conditions, facing accidental death at every moment, do not understand that this life is temporary. Only by providence have
 I been saved from that condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.12 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O best of the Kurus, while Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was describing his fortunate position in this way, the most dear devotee of the Lord, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, appeared there, like the moon rising in the nighttime.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.13 - Then Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw his grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, the most fortunate personality, whose dark body resembled black ointment for the eyes. His tall, elegant figure was dressed in yellow garments, he had long arms, and hi
s beautiful eyes were like the petals of a lotus. He was very dear and pleasing to everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.14 - Being bound by the ropes of Varu\'eba, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja could not offer befitting respect to Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja as he had before. Rather, he simply offered 
respectful obeisances with his head, his eyes being inundated with tears and his face lowered in shame.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.15 - When the great personality Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw that the Supreme Lord was sitting there, surrounded and worshiped by His intimate associa
tes like Sunanda, he was overwhelmed with tears of jubilation. Approaching the Lord and falling to the ground, he offered obeisances to the Lord with his head.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.16 - Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said: My Lord, it is Your Lordship who gave this Bali the very g
reat opulence of the post of heavenly king, and now, today, it is You who have taken it all away. I think You have acted with equal beauty in both ways. Because his exalted position as King of heaven was putting him in the darkness of ignorance, You have 
done him a very merciful favor by taking away all his opulence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.17 - Material opulence is so bewildering that it makes even a learned, self-controlled man forget to search for the goal of self-realization. But the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, the Lord of the universe, can see everything by His will. Therefore I offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Lord Brahm\'e4 then began to speak to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, within the hearing of Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who stood nearby with folded hands.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.19 - But Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's chaste wife, afraid and aggrieved at seeing her husband arrested, immediately offered obeisances to Lord V\'e4manadeva [Upendra]. She folded her hands and spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.20 - \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Vindhy\'e4
vali said: O my Lord, You have created the entire universe for the enjoyment of Your personal pastimes, but foolish, unintelligent men have claimed proprietorship for material enjoyment. Certainly they are sha
meless agnostics. Falsely claiming proprietorship, they think they can give charity and enjoy. In such a condition, what good can they do for You, who are the independent creator, maintainer and annihilator of this universe?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.21 - Lord Brahm\'e4 said:
 O well-wisher and master of all living entities, O worshipable Deity of all the demigods, O all-pervading Personality of Godhead, now this man has been sufficiently punished, for You have taken everything. Now You can release him. He does not deserve to 
be punished more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.22 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja had already offered everything to Your Lordship. Without hesitation, he has offered his land, the planets and whatever else he earned by his pious activities, including even his own body.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.23 - By offering even water, newly grown grass, or flower buds at Your lotus feet, those who maintain no mental duplicity can achieve the most exalted position within the spiritual world. This Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, without duplicity, has now offered everything in the three worlds. How then can he deserve to suffer from arrest?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.24 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: My dear Lord Brahm\'e4, because of material opulence a foolish person becomes dull-witted and mad. Thus he has no respect for anyone within the three wo
rlds and defies even My authority. To such a person I show special favor by first taking away all his possessions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.25 - While rotating in the cycle of birth and death again and again in different species because of his own fruitive activities, the
 dependent living entity, by good fortune, may happen to become a human being. This human birth is very rarely obtained.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.26 - If a human being is born in an aristocratic family or a higher status of life, if he performs wonderful activities, if he
 is youthful, if he has personal beauty, a good education and good wealth, and if he is nonetheless not proud of his opulences, it is to be understood that he is especially favored by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.27 - Although aristocratic 
birth and other such opulences are impediments to advancement in devotional service because they are causes of false prestige and pride, these opulences never disturb a pure devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.28 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja has become the most famous among the demons and nonbelievers, for in spite of being bereft of all material opulences, he is fixed in his devotional service.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.29-30 - Although bereft of his riches, fallen from his original position, defeated and arrested b
y his enemies, rebuked and deserted by his relatives and friends, although suffering the pain of being bound and although rebuked and cursed by his spiritual master, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, being fixed in his vow, did not give up his truthfulness. It was certainly with pretension that I spoke about religious principles, but he did not give up religious principles, for he is true to his word.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.31 - The Lord continued: Because of his great tolerance, I have given him a place not obtainable even by the demigods. He will become King of the heavenly planets during the period of the Manu known as S\'e4var\'ebi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.32 - Until Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja achieves the position of King of heaven, he shall live on the planet Sutala, which was made by Vi\'e7vakarm\'e4 according to My order.
 Because it is especially protected by Me, it is free from mental and bodily miseries, fatigue, dizziness, defeat and all other disturbances. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, you may now go live there peacefully.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.33 - O Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja [Indrasena], now you may go to the planet Sutala, which is desired even by the demigods. Live there peacefully, surrounded by your friends and relatives. All good fortune unto you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.34 - On the planet Sutala, not even the predominating deities of other planets, what to speak of 
ordinary people, will be able to conquer you. As far as the demons are concerned, if they transgress your rule, My disc will kill them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.35 - O great hero, I shall always be with you and give you protection in all respects along with your associates and paraphernalia. Moreover, you will always be able to see Me there.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.22.36 - Because there you will see My supreme prowess, your materialistic ideas and anxieties that have arisen from your association with the demons and D\'e4navas will immediately be vanquished.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-36
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When the supreme, ancient, eternal Personality of Godhead had thus spoken to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who is universally accepted as a pure devotee of the Lord and therefore a great soul, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, his eyes filled with tears, his hands folded and his voice faltering in devotional ecstasy, responded as follows.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.2 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said: What a wonderful effect there is in even attempting to offer respectful obeisances to You! I merely endeavored to offer
 You obeisances, but nonetheless the attempt was as successful as those of pure devotees. The causeless mercy You have shown to me, a fallen demon, was never achieved even by the demigods or the leaders of the various planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After speaking in this way, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja offered his obeisances first to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, and then to Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva. Thus he was released from the bondage of the n\'e4ga-p\'e4\'e7a [the ropes of Varu\'eba], and in full satisfaction he entered the planet known as Sutala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.4 - Thus having delivered the proprietorship of the heavenly planets to Indra and having fulfilled the desire of Aditi, mother of the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead ruled the affairs of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.5 - When Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja heard how Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, his grandson and descendant, had been released from bondage and had achieved the benediction of the Lord, he spoke as follows in a tone of greatly ecstatic devotion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.6 - Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said: O Supreme Personality of Godhead, You are universally worshiped; even Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva worship Your lotus feet. Yet although You are such a great personality, You have kindly promised to protect us, the demons. I think that such kindness has never been achieved even by Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva or the goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9
, what to speak of other demigods or common people.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.7 - O supreme shelter of everyone, great personalities like Brahm\'e4 enjoy their perfectio
n simply by tasting the honey of rendering service at Your lotus feet. But as for us, who are all rogues and debauchees born of an envious family of demons, how have we received Your mercy? It has been possible only because Your mercy is causeless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.2
3.8 - O my Lord, Your pastimes are all wonderfully performed by Your inconceivable spiritual energy; and by her perverted reflection, the material energy, You have created all the universes. As the Supersoul of all living entities, You are aware of everyt
hing, and therefore You are certainly equal toward everyone. Nonetheless, You favor Your devotees. This is not partiality, however, for Your characteristic is just like that of a desire tree, which yields everything according to one's desire.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.9 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: My dear son Prahl\'e4
da, all good fortune unto you. For the time being, please go to the place known as Sutala and there enjoy happiness with your grandson and your other relatives and friends.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.10 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead assured Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja: You shall be able to see Me there in My usual feature with conchshell, disc, club and lotus in My hand. Because of your transcendental bliss due to always personally seeing Me, you will have no further bondage to fruitive activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.11-12 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Accompanied by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, my dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, the master of all the chiefs of the demons, took the Supreme Lord's order on his head with folded hands. After saying yes to the Lord, circumambulating Him and offering Him respectful obeisances, he entered the lower planetary system known as Sutala.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.13 - Hari, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, thereafter addressed \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, who was sitting nearby in the midst of the assembly with the priests [brahma, hot\'e4, udg\'e4t\'e4
 and adhvaryu]. O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, these priests were all brahma-v\'e4d\'e9s, followers of the Vedic principles for performing sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.14 - O best of the br\'e4hma\'ebas, \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, please describe the fault or discrepancy in your disciple Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, who engaged in performing sacrifices. This fault will be nullified when judged in the presence of qualified br\'e4hma\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.15 - \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya said: My Lord, You are the enjoyer and lawgiver in all performances of sacrifice, and You are the yaj\'efa-puru\'f1
a, the person to whom all sacrifices are offered. If one has fully satisfied You, where is the chance of discrepancies or faults in his performances of sacrifice?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.16 - Ther
e may be discrepancies in pronouncing the mantras and observing the regulative principles, and, moreover, there may be discrepancies in regard to time, place, person and paraphernalia. But when Your Lordship's holy name is chanted, everything becomes faul
tless.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.17 - Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, I must nonetheless act in obedience to Your order because obeying Your order is most auspicious and is the first duty of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: In this way, the most powerful \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya accepted the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead with full respect. Along with the best br\'e4hma\'eb
as, he began to compensate for the discrepancies in the sacrifices performed by Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.19 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, thus having taken all the land of Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja by begging, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord V\'e4manadeva, delivered to His brother Indra all the land taken away by Indra's enemy.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.20-21 - Lord Brahm\'e4 [the master of King Dak\'f1a and all other Praj\'e4patis], accompanied by all the demigods, the great saintly persons, the inhabitants of Pit\'e5loka, the Manus, the munis, and such leaders as Dak\'f1
a, Bh\'e5gu and A\'ecgir\'e4, as well as K\'e4rttikeya and Lord \'c7iva, accepted Lord V\'e4manadeva as the protector of everyone. He did this for the pleasure of Ka\'e7
yapa Muni and his wife Aditi and for the welfare of all the inhabitants of the universe, including their various leaders.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
