\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said: When the supreme, ancient, eternal Personality of Godhead had thus spoken to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, who is universally accepted as a pure devotee of the Lord and therefore a great soul, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, his eyes filled with tears, his hands folded and his voice faltering in devotional ecstasy, responded as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.2 - Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja said: What a wonderful
 effect there is in even attempting to offer respectful obeisances to You! I merely endeavored to offer You obeisances, but nonetheless the attempt was as successful as those of pure devotees. The causeless mercy You have shown to me, a fallen demon, was 
never achieved even by the demigods or the leaders of the various planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After speaking in this way, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja offered his obeisances first to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, and then to Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7
iva. Thus he was released from the bondage of the n\'e4ga-p\'e4\'e7a [the ropes of Varu\'eba], and in full satisfaction he entered the planet known as Sutala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.4 - Thus having delivered the proprietorship of the heavenly planets to Indra and having fulfilled the desire of Aditi, mother of the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead ruled the affairs of the universe.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
