\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.23.31 - Whenever the activities of V\'e4manadeva are described in the course of a ritualistic ceremony, whether the ceremony be performed to please the demigods, to please one's forefathers in Pit\'e5
loka, or to celebrate a social event like a marriage, that ceremony should be understood to be extremely auspicious.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Translations 1-31
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10883103\charrsid4605116 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.1 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it said: The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, is eternally situated in His transcendental position, yet He descends to this material world and manifests 
Himself in various incarnations. His first incarnation was that of a great fish. O most powerful \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, I wish to hear from you the pastimes of that fish incarnation.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.2-3 - What was the purpose for which the Supreme Personality of Godhe
ad accepted the abominable form of a fish, exactly as an ordinary living being accepts different forms under the laws of karma? The form of a fish is certainly condemned and full of terrible pain. O my lord, what was the purpose of this incarnation? Kindl
y explain this to us, for hearing about the pastimes of the Lord is auspicious for everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.4 - S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja thus inquired from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, that most powerful saintly person began describing the pastimes of the Lord's incarnation as a fish.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.5 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, for the sake of protecting the cows, br\'e4hma\'eb
as, demigods, devotees, the Vedic literature, religious principles, and principles to fulfill the purpose of life, the Supreme Personality of Godhead accepts the forms of incarnations.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.6 - Like the air passing through different types of atmosphere, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although appearing sometimes as a human being and sometimes as a lower animal, is always transcen
dental. Because He is above the material modes of nature, He is unaffected by higher and lower forms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.7 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, at the end of the past millennium, at the end of Brahm\'e4's day, because Lord Brahm\'e4 sleeps during the night, annihilation too
k place, and the three worlds were covered by the water of the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.8 - At the end of Brahm\'e4's day, when Brahm\'e4 felt sleepy and desired to lie down, the Vedas were emanating from his mouth, and the great demon named Hayagr\'e9va stole the Vedic knowledge.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.9 - Understanding the acts of the great demon Hayagr\'e9va, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, who is full of all opulences, assumed the form of a fish and saved the Vedas by killing the demon.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.10 - During the C\'e4k\'f1u\'f1a-manvantara there was a great king named Satyavrata who was a great devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Satyavrata performed austerities by subsisting only on water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.11 - In this [the present] millennium King Satyavrata later became the son of Vivasv\'e4n, the king of the sun planet, and was known as \'c7r\'e4
ddhadeva. By the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he was given the post of Manu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.12 - One day while King Satyavrata was performing austerities by offering water on the bank of the River K\'e5tam\'e4l\'e4, a small fish appeared in the water in his palms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.13 - Satyavrata, the King of Dravi\'f2ade\'e7a, threw the fish into the water of the river along with the water in his palm, O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, descendant of Bharata.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.14 - With an
 appealing voice, the poor small fish said to King Satyavrata, who was very merciful: My dear King, protector of the poor, why are you throwing Me in the water of the river, where there are other aquatics who can kill Me? I am very much afraid of them.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.15 - To please himself, King Satyavrata, not knowing that the fish was the Supreme Personality of Godhead, decided with great pleasure to give the fish protection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.16 - The merciful King, being moved by the pitiable words of the fish, placed the fish in a water jug and brought Him to his own residence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.17 - But in one night that fish grew so much that He could not move His body comfortably in the water of the pot. He then spoke to the King as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.18 - O My dear King, I do not like living in this waterpot with such great difficulty. Therefore, please find some better reservoir of water where I can live comfortably.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.19 - Then, taking the fish out of the waterpot, the King threw Him in a large well. But within a moment the fish developed to the length of three cubits.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.20 - The fish then said: My dear King, this reservoir of water is not fit for My happy residence. Please give Me a more extensive pool of water, for I have taken shelter of you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.21 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, the King took the fish from the well and threw Him in a lake, but the fish then assumed a gigantic form exceeding the extent of the water.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.22 - The fish then said: O King, I am a large aquatic, and this water is not at all suitable for Me. Now kindly find some way to save Me. It would be better to put Me in the water of a lake that will never reduce.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.23 - When thus requested, King Satyavrata took the fish to the largest reservoir of water. But when that also proved insufficient, the King at last threw the gigantic fish into the ocean.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.24 - While being thrown in the ocean, the fish said to King Satyavrata: O hero, in this water there are very powerful and dangerous sharks that will eat Me. Therefore you should not throw Me in this place.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.25 - After hearing these sweet words from the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of a fish, the King, being bewildered, asked Him: Who are You, sir? You simply bewilder us.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.26 - My Lord, in one day You have expanded Yourself for hundreds of miles, covering the water of the river and the ocean. Before this I had never seen or heard of such an aquatic animal.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.27 - My Lord, You are certainly the inexhaustible Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, \'c7r\'e9 Hari. It is to show Your mercy to the living entities that You have now assumed the form of an aquatic.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.28 - O my Lord, master of creation, maintenance and annihilation, O best of enjoyers, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, You are the leader and destination of s
urrendered devotees like us. Therefore let me offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.29 - All Your pastimes and incarnations certainly appear for the welfare of all living entities. Therefore, my Lord, I wish to know the purpose for which You have assumed this form of a fish.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.30 - O my Lord, possessing eyes like the petals of a lotus, the worship of the demigods, who are in the bodily concept of life, is fruitless in all respects. But because You are the supreme friend and dearmost Super
soul of everyone, worship of Your lotus feet is never useless. You have therefore manifested Your form as a fish.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.31 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When King Satyavrata spoke in this way, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who at the end of the yuga ha
d assumed the form of a fish to benefit His devotee and enjoy His pastimes in the water of inundation, responded as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.32 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O King, who can subdue your enemies, on the seventh day from today the three worlds-Bh\'fc\'f9, Bhuva\'f9 and Sva\'f9-will all merge into the water of inundation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.33 - When all the three worlds merge into the water, a large boat sent by Me will appear before you.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.34-35 - Thereafter, O King, you shall collect all types of herbs and seeds and load them on that great boat. Then, accompanied by the seven \'e5\'f1
is and surrounded by all kinds of living entities, you shall get aboard that boat, and without moroseness you shall easily travel with your companions on the ocean of inundation, the only illumination being the effulgence of the great \'e5\'f1is.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.36 - Then, as the boat is tossed about by the powerful winds, attach the vessel to My horn by means of the great serpent V\'e4suki, for I shall be present by your side.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.37 - Pulling the boat, with you and all the \'e5\'f1is in it, O King, I shall travel in the water of devastation until the night of Lord Brahm\'e4's slumber is over.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.38 - You will be thoroughly advised and favored by Me, and because of your inquiries, everything about My glories, which are known as para\'e0
 brahma, will be manifest within your heart. Thus you will know everything about Me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.39 - After thus instructing the King, the Supreme Personality of Godhead immediately disappeared. Then King Satyavrata began to wait for that time of which the Lord had instructed.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.40 - After spreading ku\'e7a with its tips pointing east, the saintly King, himself facing the northeast, sat down on the grass and began to meditate upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who had assumed the form of a fish.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.41 - Thereafter, gigantic clouds pouring incessant water swelled the ocean more and more. Thus the ocean began to overflow onto the land and inundate the entire world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.42 - As Satyavrata remembered the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he saw a boat coming near him. Thus he collected herbs and creepers, and, accompanied by saintly br\'e4hma\'ebas, he got aboard the boat.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.43 - The saintly br\'e4hma\'ebas, being pleased with the King, said to him: O King, please meditate upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Ke\'e7
ava. He will save us from this impending danger and arrange for our well-being.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.44 - Then, while the King constantly meditated upon the Supreme Personality of Godhead, a large golden fish appeared in the ocean of inundation. The fish had one horn and was eight million miles long.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.45 - Following the instructions formerly given by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the King anchored the boat to the fish's horn, using the serpent V\'e4
suki as a rope. Thus being satisfied, he began offering prayers to the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.46 - The King said: By the grace of the Lord, those who have lost their self-knowledge since time immemorial, and who because of this ignorance are invol
ved in a material, conditional life full of miseries, obtain the chance to meet the Lord's devotee. I accept that Supreme Personality of Godhead as the supreme spiritual master.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.47 - In hopes of becoming happy in this material world, the foolish c
onditioned soul performs fruitive activities that result only in suffering. But by rendering service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one becomes free from such false desires for happiness. May my supreme spiritual master cut the knot of false desir
es from the core of my heart.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.48 - One who wants to be free of material entanglement should take to the service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and give up the contamination of ignorance, involving pious and impious activities. Thus one regai
ns his original identity, just as a block of gold or silver sheds all dirt and becomes purified when treated with fire. May that inexhaustible Supreme Personality of Godhead become our spiritual master, for He is the original spiritual master of all other
 spiritual masters.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 
SB 8.24.49 - Neither all the demigods, nor the so-called gurus nor all other people, either independently or together, can offer mercy that equals even one ten-thousandth of Yours. Therefore I wish to take shelter of Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 S
B 8.24.50 - As a blind man, being unable to see, accepts another blind man as his leader, people who do not know the goal of life accept someone as a guru who is a rascal and a fool. But we are interested in self-realization. Therefore we accept You, the 
Supreme Personality of Godhead, as our spiritual master, for You are able to see in all directions and are omniscient like the sun.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.51 - A materialistic so-called guru instructs his materialistic disciples about economic development and sense grati
fication, and because of such instructions the foolish disciples continue in the materialistic existence of ignorance. But Your Lordship gives knowledge that is eternal, and the intelligent person receiving such knowledge is quickly situated in his origin
al constitutional position.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.52 - My Lord, You are the supreme well-wishing friend of everyone, the dearmost friend, the controller, the Supersoul, the supreme instructor and the giver of supreme knowledge and the fulfillment of all desires. But alt
hough You are within the heart, the foolish, because of lusty desires in the heart, cannot understand You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.53 - O Supreme Lord, for self-realization I surrender unto You, who are worshiped by the demigods as the supreme controller of everything. B
y Your instructions, exposing life's purpose, kindly cut the knot from the core of my heart and let me know the destination of my life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.54 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: When Satyavrata had thus prayed to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who had
 assumed the form of a fish, the Lord, while moving in the water of inundation, explained to him the Absolute Truth.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.55 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead thus explained to King Satyavrata the spiritual science known as s\'e4\'eckhya-yoga, the science
 by which one distinguishes between matter and spirit [in other words, bhakti-yoga], along with the instructions contained in the Pur\'e4\'ebas [the old histories] and the sa\'e0hit\'e4s. The Lord explained Himself in all these literatures.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.56 - While sitting
 in the boat, King Satyavrata, accompanied by the great saintly persons, listened to the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in regard to self-realization. These instructions were all from the eternal Vedic literature [brahma]. Thus the Kin
g and sages had no doubt about the Absolute Truth.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.57 - At the end of the last inundation [during the period of Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu] the Supreme Personality of Godhead killed the demon named Hayagr\'e9va and delivered all the Vedic literatures to Lord Brahm\'e4
 when Lord Brahm\'e4 awakened from sleeping.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.58 - King Satyavrata was illuminated with all Vedic knowledge by the mercy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and in this period he has now taken birth as Vaivasvata Manu, the son of the sun-god.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.59 - This story concerning the great King Satyavrata and the fish incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, is a great transcendental narration. Anyone who hears it is delivered from the reactions of sinful life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.60 - One who narrates this description of the Matsya incarnation and King Satyavrata will certainly have all his ambitions fulfilled, and he will undoubtedly return home, back to Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid10883103 SB 8.24.61 - I offer my respectful obeisances unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who pretended to be a gigantic fish, who restored the Vedic literature to Lord Brahm\'e4 when Lord Brahm\'e4
 awakened from sleep, and who explained the essence of Vedic literature to King Satyavrata and the great saintly persons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid10883103 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  24. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid4605116\charrsid4605116 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
