}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4v\'e4syam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash living everywhere; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 idam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash this universe; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 
vi\'e7vam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all universes, all places; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash whatever; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ki\'efcit}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash everything that exists; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jagaty\'e4m}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash in this world, everywhere; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jagat}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash everything, animate and inanimate; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tena}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by Him; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tyaktena}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash allotted; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bhu\'efj\'e9th\'e4\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash you may enjoy; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 m\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash do not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 g\'e5dha\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash accept; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 kasya svit}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash of anyone else; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 dhanam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the property.
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4283093 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
Within this universe, the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His Supersoul feature is present everywhere, wherever there are animat
e or inanimate beings. Therefore, one should accept only that which is allotted to him; one should not desire to infringe upon the property of others.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
Having described the situation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as transcendental, Sv\'e4yambhu
va Manu, for the instruction of the sons and grandsons in his dynasty, is now describing all the property of the universe as belonging to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Manu's instructions are not only for his own sons and grandsons, but for all of h
uman society. The word "man"\emdash or, in Sanskrit, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 manu\'f1ya}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
has been derived from the name Manu, for all the members of human society are descendants of the original Manu. Manu is also mentioned in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 (4.1), where the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ima\'e0 vivasvate yoga\'e0\line proktav\'e4n aham avyayam\line vivasv\'e4n manave pr\'e4
ha\line manur ik\'f1v\'e4kave 'brav\'e9t
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "I instructed this imperishable science of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yoga}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  to the sun-god, Vivasv\'e4n, and Vivasv\'e4n instructed it to Manu, the father of mankind, and Manu in turn instructed it to Ik\'f1v\'e4ku." Sv\'e4yambhuva 
Manu and Vaivasvata Manu have similar duties. Vaivasvata Manu was born of the sun-god, Vivasv\'e4n, and his son was Ik\'f1v\'e4
ku, the King of the earth. Since Manu is understood to be the original father of humanity, human society should follow his instructions.
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu instructs that whatever exists, not only in the spiritual world but even within this material world, is the property of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is present everywhere as the Superconsciousness. As confirmed in }{
\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (13.3), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 k\'f1etra-j\'efam}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 c\'e4pi m\'e4\'e0 viddhi sarva-k\'f1etre\'f1u bh
\'e4rata:}{\insrsid4605116  in every field\emdash in other words, in every body\emdash the Supreme Lord is existing as the Supersoul. The individual soul is given a body in which to live and act according to the instructions of the Supreme
 Person, and therefore the Supreme Person also exists within every body. We should not think that we are independent; rather, we should understand that we are allotted a certain portion of the total property of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par This unde
rstanding will lead to perfect communism. Communists think in terms of their own nations, but the spiritual communism instructed here is not only nationwide but universal. Nothing belongs to any nation or any individual person; everything belongs to the S
upreme Personality of Godhead. That is the meaning of this verse. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'c4tm\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 vi\'e7vam:}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 whatever exists within this universe is the property of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The modern communistic theory, and also the idea of the United Nations, can be reformed\emdash indeed, rectified\emdash 
by the understanding that everything belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The Lord is not a creation of our intelligence; rather, He has created us. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'c4tm\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 vi\'e7vam.}{
\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 sarvam.}{\insrsid4605116  This universal communism can solve all the problems of the world.
\par One should learn from the Vedic literature that one's body is also not the property of the individual soul, but is given to the individual soul according to his }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 karma.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Karma\'eb\'e4 daiva-netre\'eba jantur dehopapattaye.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The 8,400,000 different bodily forms are machines given to the individual soul. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (18.61):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati
\line bhr\'e4mayan sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "The Supreme Lord is situated in eve
ryone's heart, O Arjuna, and is directing the wanderings of all living entities, who are seated as on a machine, made of the material energy." The Lord, as the Supersoul, sits in everyone's heart and observes the various desires of the individual soul. Th
e Lord is so merciful that He gives the living entity the opportunity to enjoy varieties of desires in suitable bodies, which are nothing but machines (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
). These machines are manufactured by the material ingredients of the external energy, and thus the living entity enjoys or suffers according to his desires. This opportunity is given by the Supersoul.
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
Everything belongs to the Supreme, and therefore one should not usurp another's property. We have a tendency to manufacture many things. Es
pecially nowadays, we are building skyscrapers and developing other material facilities. We should know, however, that the ingredients of the skyscrapers and machines cannot be manufactured by anyone but the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The whole world
 is nothing but a combination of the five material elements (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 tejo-v\'e4ri-m\'e5d\'e4\'e0 yath\'e4 vinimaya\'f9}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
). A skyscraper is a transformation of earth, water and fire. Earth and water are combined and burnt into bricks by fire, and a skyscraper is essentially a tall cons
truction of bricks. Although the bricks may be manufactured by man, the ingredients of the bricks are not. Of course, man, as a manufacturer, may accept a salary from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. That is stated here: }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 
tena tyaktena bhu\'efj\'e9th\'e4\'f9.}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  One ma
y construct a big skyscraper, but neither the constructor, the merchant nor the worker can claim proprietorship. Proprietorship belongs to the person who has spent for the building. The Supreme Personality of Godhead has manufactured water, earth, air, fi
re and the sky, and one can use these and take a salary (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 tena tyaktena bhu\'efj\'e9th\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid4605116 
). However, one cannot claim proprietorship. This is perfect communism. Our tendency to construct great buildings should be used only for constructing large and valuable temple
s in which to install the Deity of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Then our desire for construction will be fulfilled.
\par Since all property belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, everything should be offered to the Lord, and we should take only }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 pras\'e4da}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 tena tyaktena bhu\'efj
\'e9th\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). We should not fight among ourselves to take more than we need. As N\'e4rada said to Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Yudhi\'f1\'f6hira:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 y\'e4vad bhriyeta ja\'f6hara\'e0\line t\'e4vat svatva\'e0 hi dehin\'e4m\line adhika\'e0
 yo 'bhimanyeta\line sa steno da\'eb\'f2am arhati
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "One may claim propriet
orship to as much wealth as required to maintain body and soul together, but one who desires proprietorship over more than that must be considered a thief, and he deserves to be punished by the laws of nature." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 B}{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309 h}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309 \'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  7.14.8) Of course, we need to be maintained in eating, sleeping, mating and defending (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4h\'e4
ra-nidra-bhaya-maithuna}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ), but since the Supreme Lord, the Personality of Godhead, has provided these necessities of life for the birds and bees, why not for mankind? There is no need for economic developm
ent; everything is provided. Therefore one should understand that everything belongs to K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and with this idea, one may take }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pras\'e4da.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 However, if one interferes with the allotments of others, he is a thief. We should not accept more than what we actuall
y need. Therefore, if by chance we get an abundance of money, we should always consider that it belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness we are getting sufficient money, but we should never think that the money belongs to us; i
t belongs to the Supreme Personality of Godhead and should be equally distributed to the workers, the devotees. No devotee should claim that any money or property belongs to him. If one thinks that any portion of property of this huge universe belongs to 
anyone, he is to be considered a thief and is punishable by the laws of nature. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9 mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 no one can surpass the vigilance of material nature or hide his intentions from material nature. If human society unlawfully claims t
hat the property of the universe, either partially or wholly, belongs to mankind, all of human society will be cursed as a society of thieves and will be punished by the laws of nature.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.1.11
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 11
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\v\f70\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 Ya& PaXYaiTa Na PaXYaNTa& c+auYaRSYa Na irZYaiTa )\line 
Ta& >aUTaiNal/Ya& dev& SauPa<aRMauPaDaavTa )) 11 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 ya\'e0 pa\'e7yati na pa\'e7yanta\'e0
\par cak\'f1ur yasya na ri\'f1yati
\par ta\'e0 bh\'fcta-nilaya\'e0 deva\'e0
\par supar\'ebam upadh\'e4vata
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10300851 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash He who; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 pa\'e7yati}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the living entity sees; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 pa\'e7yantam
}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash although always seeing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 cak\'f1u\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash eye; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yasya}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash whose; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash never; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ri\'f1yati}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
diminishes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash Him; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bh\'fcta-nilayam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the original source of all living entities; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 devam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 supar\'ebam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
who accompanies the living entity as a friend; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 upadh\'e4vata}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash everyone should worship.
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4283093 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
Although the Supreme Personality of Godhead constantly watches the activities of the world, no one sees Him. However, one should not think that because no one sees Him, He does not see, for His power to see is never diminished. Therefore, everyone should 
worship the Supersoul, who always stays with the individual soul as a friend.
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4283093 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 Offering prayers to K\'e5\'f1\'eba, \'c7r\'e9mat\'e9 Kunt\'e9dev\'e9
, the mother of the P\'e4\'eb\'f2avas, said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 alak\'f1ya\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m antar bahir avasthitam:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  "K\'e5\'f1\'eba, You reside both inside and outside 
of everything, yet the unintelligent conditioned souls cannot see You." In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  it is said that one can see the Supreme Personality of Godhead through }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4na-cak\'f1u\'f1a\'f9,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  eyes of knowledge. He who opens these eyes of knowledge is called a spiritual ma
ster. Thus we offer our prayers to the spiritual master with the following }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7loka:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 om aj\'ef\'e4na-timir\'e4ndhasya\line j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'efjana-\'e7al\'e4kay\'e4\line cak
\'f1ur unm\'e9lita\'e0 yena\line tasmai \'e7r\'e9-gurave nama\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "I offer my respectful obeisances unto my spiritual master, who with the torchlight 
of knowledge has opened my eyes, which were blinded by the darkness of ignorance." (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Gautam\'e9ya Tantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ) The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru's}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 task is to open the disciple's eyes of knowledge. When the disciple is awakened from ignorance to knowledge, he can see the Supreme Personality of Godhead everywhere because the Lord actually is everywhere. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 A\'eb\'f2
\'e4ntara-stha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntara-stham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  The Lord resides within this universe, He resides within the hearts of all living entities, and He resides even within the atom. Because we lack perfec
t knowledge, we cannot see God, but a little deliberation can help us to see God everywhere. This requires training. With a little deliberation, even the most degraded person can perceive the presence of God. If we take into account whose property is the 
v
ast ocean, whose property is the vast land, how the sky exists, how the numberless millions of stars and planets are set in the sky, who has made this universe and whose property it is, we should certainly come to the conclusion that there is a proprietor
 
of everything. When we claim proprietorship over a certain piece of land, whether individually or for our families or nations, we should also consider how we became the proprietors. The land was there before our birth, before we came to the land. How did 
it become our property? Such deliberation will help us understand that there is a supreme proprietor of everything\emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
The Supreme Godhead is always awake. In the conditioned stage we forget things because we change our bodies, but because the Supreme Personality of Godhead does not change His body, He remembers past, present and future. K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{
\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (4.1), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 ima\'e0 vivasvate yoga\'e0 proktav\'e4n aham avyayam:}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  "I spoke this science of God\emdash }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 \emdash to the sun-god at least forty million years ago." When Arjuna inquired from K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a how He could remember incidents that had taken place so long ago, the Lord answered that Arjuna was also present at that time. Because Arjuna is K\'e5\'f1\'eba's friend, wherever K\'e5\'f1\'eba goes, Arjuna goes. But the difference is that K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a remembers everything, whereas the living entity like Arjuna, being a minute particle of the Supreme Lord, forgets. Therefore it is said, the Lord's vigilance is never diminished. This is also confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (15.15). }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Sarvasya c\'e4ha\'e0 h\'e5di sannivi\'f1\'f6o matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca:}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His Param\'e4tm\'e4 feature is always present within the hearts of all living entities, and from Him come memory, knowledge and forgetfulness. This is also indicated in this verse by the word }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 supar\'ebam,}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  which means "friend." In the }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 \'c7vet\'e4\'e7vatara Upani\'f1ad}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (4.6) it is therefore said, }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 dv\'e4 supar\'eba-sayuj\'e4 sakh\'e4y\'e4 sam\'e4na\'e0 v\'e5k\'f1a\'e0 pari\'f1asvaj\'e4te:}{\insrsid4605116  two birds are sitting on the same tree as friends. One bird is eating
 the fruit of the tree, and the other is simply observing. This observing bird is always present as a friend to the eating bird and giving him remembrance of things he wanted to do. Thus if we take into account the Supreme Personality of Godhead in our da
ily affairs, we can see Him or at least perceive His presence everywhere.
\par The words }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 cak\'f1ur yasya na ri\'f1yati}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  mean that although we cannot see Him, this does not mean that He cannot see us. Nor does He die when the cosmic manifestation is annihilated. The exa
mple is given in this connection that the sunshine is present when the sun is present, but when the sun is not present, or when we cannot see the sun, this does not mean that the sun is lost. The sun is there, but we cannot see it. Similarly, although we 
cannot see the Supreme Personality of Godhead in our present darkness, our lack of knowledge, He is always present, seeing our activities. As the Param\'e4tm\'e4, He is the witness and adviser (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 upadra\'f1\'f6\'e4}{
\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 anumant\'e4}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). Therefore, by following the instructions of 
the spiritual master and studying authorized literatures, one can understand that God is present before us, seeing everything, although we have no eyes with which to see Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.1.12
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 12
