others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash nor; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 antaram}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash inside; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bahi\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash outside; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vi\'e7vasya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash of the whole cosmic manifestation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 am\'fcni}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all such considerations; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash whose form; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yasm\'e4t}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash from He who is the cause of everything; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vi\'e7vam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the whole universe; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ca}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash and; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all of them; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e5tam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
truth; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mahat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash very, very great.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead has no beginning, no end and no middle. Nor does He belong to a particular person or nation. He has no inside or outside. The dualities found within thi
s material world, such as beginning and end, mine and theirs, are all absent from the personality of the Supreme Lord. The universe, which emanates from Him, is another feature of the Lord. Therefore the Supreme Lord is the ultimate truth, and He is compl
ete in greatness.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 The Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, is described in the }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (5.1):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9\line sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9\line 
an\'e4dir \'e4dir govinda\'f9\line sarva-k\'e4ra\'eba-k\'e4ra\'ebam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "K\'e5\'f1\'eba, known as Govinda, is the supreme controller. He h
as an eternal, blissful, spiritual body. He is the origin of all. He has no other origin, for He is the prime cause of all causes." For the Lord's existence there is no cause, for He is the cause of everything. He is in everything (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarvam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ), He is expanded in everything, but He is not everything. He is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 simultaneously one and different. That is explained in this verse. In the material condition we have a conception of beginning, end and middle, but for the Supreme Personali
ty of Godhead there are no such things. The universal cosmic manifestation is also the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vir\'e4}{\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid13309698\charrsid13309698 \'f2}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 -r\'fcpa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 that was shown to Arjuna in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Therefore, since the Lord is present everywhere and all the time, He is the Absolute Truth and the greatest. He is 
complete in greatness. God is great, and how He is great is explained here.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.1.13
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 13
