In that garden there was a very large lake filled with shining golden lotus flowers and the flowers known as kumuda, kahl\'e4ra, utpala and \'e7atapatra, which added excellent beauty to the mountain. There were also bilva, kapittha, jamb\'e9ra and bhall
\'e4taka trees. Intoxicated bumblebees drank honey and hummed with the chirping of the birds, whose songs were very melodious. The lake was crowded with swans, k\'e4ra\'eb\'f2avas, cakr\'e4vakas, cranes, and flocks of water chickens, d\'e4ty\'fchas, koya
\'f1\'f6is and other murmuring birds. Because of the agitating movements of the fish and tortoises, the water was decorated with pollen that had fallen from the lotus flowers. The lake was surrounded by kadamba flowers, vetasa flowers, nalas, n\'e9pas, va
\'efjulakas, kundas, kurubakas, a\'e7okas, \'e7ir\'e9\'f1as, k\'fc\'f6ajas, i\'ecgudas, kubjakas, svar\'eba-y\'fcth\'e9s, n\'e4gas, punn\'e4gas, j\'e4t\'e9s, mallik\'e4s, \'e7atapatras, j\'e4lak\'e4s and m\'e4dhav\'e9-lat\'e4
s. The banks were also abundantly adorned with varieties of trees that yielded flowers and fruits in all seasons. Thus the entire mountain stood gloriously decorated.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
