\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e7r\'e9-b\'e4dar\'e4ya\'ebi\'f9 uv\'e4ca}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 evam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash thus; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vyavasita\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash fixed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 buddhy\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by intelligence; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sam\'e4dh\'e4ya}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash for concentration; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mana\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the mind; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 h\'e5di}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash in consciousness or in the heart; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jaj\'e4pa}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash he chanted; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 paramam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash a supreme; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 j\'e4pyam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mantra}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 he had learned from great devotees; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 pr\'e4k-janmani}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash in his previous birth; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 anu\'e7ik\'f1itam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash practiced.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid12063162 TRANSLATION}{\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3012\fs28\cf9\insrsid4605116\charrsid8146024 \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued:}{
\cs3005\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  Thereafter, the King of the elephants, Gajendra, fixed his mind in his heart with perfect intelligence and chanted a mantra which he had learned in his previous birth 
as Indradyumna and which he remembered by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 Such remembrance is described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (6.43-44):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tatra ta\'e0 buddhi-sa\'e0yoga\'e0\line labhate paurva-dehikam\line yatate ca tato bh
\'fcya\'f9\line sa\'e0siddhau kuru-nandana
\par p\'fcrv\'e4bhy\'e4sena tenaiva\line hriyate hy ava\'e7o 'pi sa\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
In these verses it is assured that even if a person engaged in devotional service falls down, he is not degraded, but is placed in a position in which he will in due course of time remember the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As explained lat
er, Gajendra was formerly King Indradyumna, and somehow or other in his next life he became King of the elephants. Now Gajendra was in danger, and although he was in a body other than that of a human being, he remembered the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 stotra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  he had chanted in his previous life. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Yatate ca tato bh\'fcya\'f9 sa\'e0siddhau kuru-nandana.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 To enable one to achieve perfection, K\'e5\'f1\'eba gives one the chance to remember Him again. This is proved here, for although the King of the elephants, Gajendra, was put in danger, this was a chance f
or him to remember his previous devotional activities so that he could immediately be rescued by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 It is imperative, therefore, that all devotees in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness practice chanting some }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Certainly one should chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  which is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4-mantra,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  and also one should practice chanting }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 cint\'e4ma\'ebi-prakara-sadmasu}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or the N\'e5si\'e0ha }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 strotra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ito n\'e5si\'e0ha\'f9 parato n\'e5si\'e0ho yato yato y\'e4mi tato n\'e5si\'e0ha\'f9}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). Every devotee should practice in order to chant some }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 perfectly so that even though he may be imperfect in spiritual consciousness in this life, in his next life he will not forget K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, even if he becomes an animal. Of course, a devotee should try to perfect his K\'e5\'f1\'eba con
sciousness in this life, for simply by understanding K\'e5\'f1\'eba and His instructions, after giving up this body one can return home, back to Godhead. Even if there is some falldown, practice of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness never goes in vain. For example, Aj\'e4mila, in his boyhood, practiced chanting the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a under the direction of his father, but later, in his youth, he fell down and became a drunkard, woman-hunter, rogue and thief. Nonetheless, because of chanting the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba for the purpose of calling his son, whom he had named N\'e4r
\'e4ya\'eba, he became advanced, even though he was involved in sinful activities. Therefore, we should not forget the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 under any circumstances. It will help us in the greatest danger, as we find in the life of Gajendra.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.2
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 2
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116\charrsid14029921 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\v\f70\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116\charrsid14029921 \'e9[qGaJaeNd] ovac\line p NaMaae >aGavTae TaSMaE YaTa WTai\'c0
daTMak-Ma( )\line Pau\'e5zaYaaidbqJaaYa PareXaaYaai>aDaqMaih )) 2 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s1428\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid14029921 \'e7r\'e9-gajendra uv\'e4ca}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 o\'e0 namo bhagavate tasmai
\par yata etac cid-\'e4tmakam
\par puru\'f1\'e4y\'e4di-b\'e9j\'e4ya
\par pare\'e7\'e4y\'e4bhidh\'e9mahi
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e7r\'e9-gajendra\'f9 uv\'e4ca}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash Gajendra, the King of elephants, said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 o\'e0}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash O my Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my respectful obeisances unto You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bhagavate}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tasmai}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto Him; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yata\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash from whom; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 etat}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash this body and the material manifestation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 cit-\'e4tmakam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash is moving due to consciousness (the spirit soul); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 puru\'f1\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the Supreme Person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4di-b\'e9j\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
who is the origin or root cause of everything; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 para-\'e9\'e7\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who is supreme, transcendental and worshipable for such exalted persons as Brahm\'e4 and \'c7iva; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 abhidh\'e9mahi}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash let me meditate upon Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3012\fs28\cf9\insrsid4605116\charrsid8146024 The King of the elephants, Gajendra, said:}{
\cs3005\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  I offer my respectful obeisances unto the Supreme Person, V\'e4sudeva [o\'e0 namo bhagavate v\'e4sudev\'e4ya]. Because of Him this material body acts due to the 
presence of spirit, and He is therefore the root cause of everyone. He is worshipable for such exalted persons as Brahm\'e4 and \'c7iva, and He has entered the heart of every living being. Let me meditate upon Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 In this verse the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 etac cid-
\'e4tmakam}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  are very important. The material body certainly consists only of material elements, but when one awakens to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious understanding, the body is no longer material but spiritual. The material body is meant for sense enjoyment, whereas the spiritual
 body engages in the transcendental loving service of the Lord. Therefore, a devotee who engages in the service of the Supreme Lord and who constantly thinks of Him should never be considered to have a material body. It is therefore enjoined, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru\'f1u nara-mati\'f9:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  one should stop thinking of the spiritual master as an ordinary human being with a material body. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Arcye vi\'f1
\'ebau \'e7il\'e4-dh\'e9\'f9:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  everyone knows that the Deity in the temple is made of stone, but to think that the Deity is merely stone is an offense. Similar
ly, to think that the body of the spiritual master consists of material ingredients is offensive. Atheists think that devotees foolishly worship a stone statue as God and an ordinary man as the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  The fact is, however, that by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba's omnip
otence, the so-called stone statue of the Deity is directly the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the body of the spiritual master is directly spiritual. A pure devotee who is engaged in unalloyed devotional service should be understood to be situated o
n the transcendental platform (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sa gu\'eb\'e4n samat\'e9tyait\'e4n brahma-bh\'fcy\'e4ya kalpate}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
). Let us therefore offer our obeisances unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead, by whose mercy so-called material things also become spiritual when they are engaged in spiritual activity.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 O\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pra\'ebava}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ) is the symbolic sound representation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 O\'e0 tat sad iti nirde\'e7o brahma\'eb
as tri-vidha\'f9 sm\'e5ta\'f9:}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  the three words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0 tat sat}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  immediately invoke the Supreme Person. Therefore K\'e5\'f1
\'eba says that He is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  in all the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pra\'ebava\'f9 sarva-vede\'f1u}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). The Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  are pronounced beginning with }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  to indicate immediately the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  for example, begins with the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0 namo bhagavate v\'e4sudev\'e4ya.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Ther
e is no difference between the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4sudeva, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pra\'ebava}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). We should be careful to understand that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  does not indicate anything }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
nir\'e4k\'e4ra,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or formless. Indeed, this verse immediately says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0 namo bhagavate.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Bhagav\'e4n is a person. Thus }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is the representation of the Supreme Person. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 O\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 is not meant to be impersonal, as the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers consider it to be. This is distinctly expressed here by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 puru\'f1\'e4ya.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 The supreme truth addressed by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0k\'e4ra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 puru\'f1a,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 the Supreme Person; He is not impersonal. Unless He is a person, how can He control the great, stalwart controllers of this universe? Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Lord \'c7iva are the supreme controllers of this universe, but Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u is offered obeisances even by Lord \'c7iva and Lord Brahm\'e4. Therefore this verse uses the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pare\'e7\'e4ya,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
