\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  Thus it is 
indicated that one can find the Supreme Lord within one's heart. There are many, many }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yog\'e9s}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  trying to find Him. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Dhy\'e4n\'e4
vasthita-tad-gatena manas\'e4 pa\'e7yanti ya\'e0 yogina\'f9.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  Nonetheless, even great }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yog\'e9s,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 demigods, saints and sages have been unable to understand 
the bodily features of that great artist, nor could they understand the meaning of His movements. What then is to be said of ordinary speculators like the so-called philosophers of this material world? For them He is impossible to understand. Therefore we
 must accept the statements given by the Supreme when He kindly incarnates to instruct us. We must simply accept the word of Lord R\'e4macandra, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu and follow in Their footsteps. Then it may be possible for us to know the purpose of Their incarnations.
\par }\pard\plain \s1434\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
