\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4tma-prad\'e9p\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto Him who is self-effulgent or who gives enlightenment to the living entities; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 s\'e4k\'f1i\'ebe}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who is situated in everyone's heart as a witness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 parama-\'e4tmane}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
unto the Supreme Soul, the Supersoul; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gir\'e4m}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash by words; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vid\'fcr\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who is impossible to reach; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 manasa\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by the mind; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 cetas\'e4m}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash or by consciousness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 api}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash even.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
I offer my respectful obeisances unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the self-effulgent Supersoul, who is the witness in everyone's heart, who enlightens the individual soul and who cannot be reached by exercises of the mind, words or consciousness.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 The Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, cannot be understood by the individual soul through mental, physical or intellectual exercises. It is by the grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead that the individual soul is enlightened. Therefore, the Lord is described here as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4tma-prad\'e9pa.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  The Lord is like the sun, which illuminates everything and cannot be illuminated by anyone. Therefore, if one is serious about understanding t
he Supreme, one must receive enlightenment from Him, as instructed in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 One cannot understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead by one's mental, physical or intellectual powers.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.11
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 11
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\v\f70\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SatveNa Pa[iTal/>YaaYa NaEZk-MYaeR<a ivPai}{\f0\insrsid4605116 \'ea}{
\f35\insrsid4605116 Taa )\line NaMa" kE-vLYaNaaQaaYa iNavaR<aSau%Sa&ivde )) 11 ))}{\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 sattvena pratilabhy\'e4ya
\par nai\'f1karmye\'eba vipa\'e7cit\'e4
\par nama\'f9 kaivalya-n\'e4th\'e4ya
\par nirv\'e4\'eba-sukha-sa\'e0vide
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sattvena}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
by pure devotional service; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 prati-labhy\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is achieved by such devotional activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nai
\'f1karmye\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by transcendental activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vipa\'e7cit\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by persons who are sufficiently learned; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 kaivalya-n\'e4th\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
unto the master of the transcendental world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nirv\'e4\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash for one completely freed from material activities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sukha}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash of happiness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sa\'e0vide}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who is the bestower.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead is realized by pure devotees who act in the transcendental existence of bhakti-yoga. He is the bestower of uncontaminated happiness and is the master of the transcendental world. Therefore I offer my respect unto Him.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid13057648 PURPORT}{\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,
}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  the Supreme Personality of Godhead can be understood only by devotional service. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti y\'e4v\'e4n ya\'e7 c\'e4smi tattvata\'f9.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  If one wants to know the Supreme Personality of Godhead in truth, one must take to the activities of devotional service. These activities are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sattva}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7uddha-sattva.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  In the material world, activities of goodness, which are symptomatic of a pure }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  are appreciated. But the activities of devotional service are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7uddha-sattva;}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  in other words, they are on the transcendental platform. Only by devotional service can one understand the Supreme.
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Devotional service is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 
nai\'f1karmya.}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Mere negation of material activity will not endure. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Nai\'f1karmyam apy acyuta-bh\'e4va-varjitam.}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 Unless one performs activities with reference to K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, cessation of material activities will not be helpful. In hopes of achieving }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 nai\'f1karmya,}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  freedom fro
m material action, many highly elevated }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 sanny\'e4s\'e9s}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 stopped their activities, yet they failed and returned to the material platform to act as materialistic persons. But once one is engaged in the spiritual activities of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga,}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 one does not fall down. Our K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is therefore an attempt to engage everyone always in spiritual activity, by which one becomes transcendental to material actions. The spiritual activities of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 
bhakti-m\'e4rga}{\cs3010\cf9\insrsid13057648\charrsid6049549 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 smara\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 \emdash lead o
ne to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, as stated here, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 sattvena pratilabhy\'e4ya nai\'f1karmye\'eba vipa\'e7cit\'e4:}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 "The Supreme Personality of Godhead is realized by pure devotees who act in the transcendental existence of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga.}{\insrsid4605116 "
\par The }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Gop\'e4la-t\'e4pan\'e9 Upani\'f1ad}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (15) says, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhaktir asya bhajana\'e0 tad ih\'e4mutrop\'e4dhi-nair\'e4syenaiv\'e4mu\'f1min manasa\'f9 kalpanam etad eva ca nai\'f1
karmyam.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  This is a definition of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 nai\'f1karmya.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  One acts in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 nai\'f1karmya}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 when he fully engages in K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious activities without material desires to enjoy, either here or in the upper planetary systems, in the present life or in a future life (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 iha-amutra}{
\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnyam.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  When one is freed from all contamination and he acts in devotional service under the direction of the spiritua
l master, one is on the platform of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 nai\'f1karma.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  By such transcendental devotional service, the Lord is served. I offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.12
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 12
