\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
all obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e7\'e4nt\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto Him who is above all material qualities and completely peaceful, or unto V\'e4sudeva, the Supersoul in every living entity; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ghor\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the fierce forms of the Lord like J\'e4madagnya and }{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid12929836 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the form of the Lord as an animal, such as the boar; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gu\'eba-dharmi\'ebe}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash who accepts different qualities within the material world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nirvi\'e7e\'f1\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who is without material qualities, being fully spiritual; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 s\'e4my\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash Lord Buddha, the form of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nirv\'e4\'eba,}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  wherein the material qualities stop; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4na-ghan\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
who is knowledge or the impersonal Brahman; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ca}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash also.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 I offer my respectful obeisances to Lord V\'e4
sudeva, who is all-pervading, to the Lord's fierce form as Lord }{\insrsid12929836 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\insrsid4605116 , to the Lord's form as an animal [Lord Var\'e4hadeva], to Lord Datt\'e4
treya, who preached impersonalism, to Lord Buddha, and to all the other incarnations. I 
offer my respectful obeisances unto the Lord, who has no material qualities but who accepts the three qualities goodness, passion and ignorance within this material world. I also offer my respectful obeisances unto the impersonal Brahman effulgence.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
In the previous verses it has been described that although the Supreme Personality of Godhead has no material form, He accepts innumerable forms to favor His devotees and kill the demons. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh
\'e4gavatam,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  there are so many incarnations of 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead that they are like the waves of a river. The waves of a river flow incessantly, and no one can count how many waves there are. Similarly, no one can calculate when and how the different incarnations of the Lord appear ac
cording to the necessities of time, place and candidates. The Lord appears perpetually. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (4.7):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yad\'e4 yad\'e4 hi dharmasya\line gl\'e4nir bhavati bh\'e4rata\line abhyutth\'e4
nam adharmasya\line tad\'e4tm\'e4na\'e0 s\'e5j\'e4my aham
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "Whenever and wherever there is a decl
ine in religious practice, O descendant of Bharata, and a predominant rise of irreligion\emdash at that time I descend Myself." In the material world there is always the possibility of deviation from K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, and therefore K\'e5\'f1
\'eba and His devotees always act in various forms to curb such godlessness.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
Even impersonalists who stress the knowledge feature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead want to merge in the effulgence of the Lord. Therefore, here the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4na-ghan\'e4ya}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  indicates that for atheists who 
disbelieve in the form and existence of the Lord, all these various incarnations appear. Since the Lord comes to teach in so many forms, no one can say that there is no God. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4na-ghan\'e4ya}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is especially used here to refer to those whose knowledge h
as become solidified by dint of their searching for the Lord through speculative philosophical understanding. Superficial knowledge is useless for understanding the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but when one's knowledge becomes extremely intense and dee
p, one understands V\'e4sudeva (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  attains this stage after many, many births. Therefore the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4na-ghan\'e4ya}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is used here. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7ant\'e4ya}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  indicates that Lord V\'e4sudeva is situated in everyone's heart but does not act with the living entity. Impersonalist }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j
\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  realize V\'e4sudeva when they are fully mature in knowledge (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.13
