I beg to offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are the Supersoul, the superintendent of everything, and the witness of all that occurs. You are the Supreme Person, the origin o
f material nature and of the total material energy. You are also the owner of the material body. Therefore, You are the supreme complete. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (13.3) the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'f1etra-j\'efa\'e0 c\'e4pi m\'e4\'e0 viddhi sarva-k\'f1etre\'f1u bh\'e4rata:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 "O scion of Bharata, you should understand that I am also the knower in all bodies." Every one of us is thinking, "I am this body" or "This is my body," but actually the truth is different. Our bodies are given to us by the supreme 
proprietor. The living entity, who is also }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'f1etra j\'efa,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 or the knower of the body, is not the body's only proprietor; the actual proprietor of the body is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the supreme }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'f1etra j\'efa.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  For example, we may rent and occupy
 a house, but actually the owner of the house is the landlord. Similarly, we may be allotted a certain type of body as a facility with which to enjoy this material world, but the actual proprietor of the body is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He is c
alled }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarv\'e4dhyak\'f1a}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  because everything in the material world works under His supervision. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (9.10), wherein the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9 s\'fcyate sacar\'e4caram:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 "This material nature, working under My direction, O son of Kunt\'e9, is producing all moving and unmoving beings." From }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 prak\'e5ti,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 or material nature, come so many varieties of living entities, including aquatics, plants, trees, insects, birds, animals, human beings and demigods. }{\cs3008\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid6362093\charrsid6362093 P}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 rak\'e5ti}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  is the mother, and the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the father (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 aha\'e0 b\'e9ja-prada\'f9 pit\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Prak\'e5ti}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 can give us material bodies, but as spirit souls we are parts and parcels of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (15.7): }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4tana\'f9.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 The living entity, being part and parcel of God, is not a product of this material world. Therefore the Lord is described in this verse as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4tma-m\'fcla,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 the original source of everything. He is the seed of all existences (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 b\'e9ja\'e0 m\'e4\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (14.4) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva-yoni\'f1u kaunteya\line m\'fcrtaya\'f9 sambhavanti y\'e4\'f9\line t\'e4s\'e4\'e0
 brahma mahad yonir\line aha\'e0 b\'e9ja-prada\'f9 pit\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "It should be understood that all living entities, in all species of life, O son of Kunt\'e9
, are made possible by birth 
in this material nature, and that I am the seed-giving father." Plants, trees, insects, aquatics, demigods, beasts, birds and all other living entities are sons or parts and parcels of the Supreme Lord, but because they are struggling with different menta
lities, they have been given different types of bodies (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mana\'f9 \'f1a\'f1\'f6h\'e4n\'e9ndriy\'e4\'ebi prak\'e5ti-sth\'e4ni kar\'f1ati}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). Thus they have become sons of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 prak\'e5ti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or material nature, which is impregnated by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Every living entity in this materi
al world is struggling for existence, and the only salvation or relief from the cycle of birth and death in the evolutionary process is full surrender. This is indicated by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 "I offer my respectful obeisances unto You."
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.14
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 14
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\v\f70\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SaveRiNd]YaGau<ad]\'ed\\e SavRPa[TYaYaheTave )\line ASaTaaC^aYaYaae\'a2
-aYa Sada>aaSaaYa Tae NaMa" )) 14 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 sarvendriya-gu\'eba-dra\'f1\'f6re
\par sarva-pratyaya-hetave
\par asat\'e4 cch\'e4yayokt\'e4ya
\par sad-\'e4bh\'e4s\'e4ya te nama\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s2997\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10300851 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sarva-indriya-gu\'eba-dra\'f1\'f6re}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the seer of all objectives pursued by the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sarva-pratyaya-hetave}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
who is the solution to all doubts (and without whose help one cannot solve all doubts and inabilities); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 asat\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash with the manifestation of unreality or illusion; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ch\'e4yay\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash because of the resemblance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ukt\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash called; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash of reality; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4bh\'e4s\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the reflection; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 
te}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my respectful obeisances.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
My Lord, You are the observer of all the objectives of the senses. Without Your mercy, there is no possibility of solving the problem of doubts. The
 material world is just like a shadow resembling You. Indeed, one accepts this material world as real because it gives a glimpse of Your existence.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
To paraphrase this verse: "The objectives of sensual activities are actually observed by You. Without Your direction, the living entity cannot take even a step forward. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (15.15), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarvasya c\'e4ha\'e0 h\'e5di sannivi\'f1\'f6o matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 You are situated in everyone's heart, and only from You come remembrance and forgetfulness. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Ch\'e4yeva yasya bhuvan\'e4ni bibharti durg\'e4.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 The living entity under the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 wants to enjoy this material world, but unless You give him directions and remind him, he cannot make progress in pursuing his shadowy objective in life. The cond
itioned soul wrongly progresses toward the wrong objective, life after life, and he is reminded of that objective by You. In one life the conditioned soul desires to progress toward a certain objective, but after his body changes, he forgets everything. N
onetheless, my Lord, because he wanted to enjoy something of this world, You remind him of this in his next birth. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 Because the conditioned soul wants to forget You, by Your grace You give him opportunities, life after life,
 by which he can almost perpetually forget You. Therefore You are eternally the director of the conditioned souls. It is because You are the original cause of everything that everything appears real. The ultimate reality is Your Lordship, the Supreme Pers
onality of Godhead. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva-pratyaya-hetave}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is explained by \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura, who says that a result gives one a glimpse of its cause. For example, since an earthen pot is the result of t
he actions of a potter, by seeing the earthen pot one can guess at the existence of the potter. Similarly, this material world resembles the spiritual world, and any intelligent person can guess how it is acting. As explained in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9 s\'fcyate sa-car\'e4caram.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 The activities of the material world suggest that behind them is the superintendence of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.15
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 15
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s2993\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\v\f70\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 NaMaae NaMaSTae_i%l/k-ar<aaYa\line  iNaZk-ar<aaYaad(>auTak-ar<aaYa )\line 
SavaRGaMaaManaYaMaha<aRvaYa\line  NaMaae_PavGaaRYa ParaYa<aaYa )) 15 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 namo namas te 'khila-k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4ya
\par ni\'f1k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4y\'e4dbhuta-k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4ya
\par sarv\'e4gam\'e4mn\'e4ya-mah\'e4r\'ebav\'e4ya
\par namo 'pavarg\'e4ya par\'e4ya\'eb\'e4ya
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash again I offer my respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 te}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash unto You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 akhila-k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the supreme cause of everything; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ni\'f1k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4ya}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto You who are causeless; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 adbhuta-k\'e4ra\'eb\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the wonderful cause of everything; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sarva}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4gama-\'e4mn\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the source of the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 parampar\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  system of all Vedic knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4-ar\'ebav\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the great ocean o
f knowledge, or the great ocean wherein all the rivers of knowledge merge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nama\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I offer my obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 apavarg\'e4ya}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto You who can give deliverance or liberation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 para-aya\'eb\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the shelter of all transcendentalists.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 My Lord, You are the cause o
f all causes, but You Yourself have no cause. Therefore You are the wonderful cause of everything. I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are the shelter of the Vedic knowledge contained in the \'e7\'e4stras like the Pa\'efcar\'e4tras and Ved\'e4
nta-s\'fctra, which are Your representations, and who are the source of the parampar\'e4 system. Because it is You who can give liberation, You are the only shelter for all transcendentalists. Let me offer my respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 The Supreme Personality of God
head is described herein as the wonderful cause. He is wonderful in the sense that although there may be unlimited emanations from the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ), He always remains complete (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 p\'fcr\'ebasya p\'fcr\'ebam \'e4d\'e4ya p\'fcr\'ebam ev\'e4va\'e7i\'f1yate}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
). In our experience in the material world, if we have a bank balance of one million dollars, as we withdraw money from the bank the balance gradually diminishes until it becomes nil. However, the Supreme Lord, the Personality of Godhead, is so complete t
hat although innumerable Personalities of Godhead expand from Him, He remains the same Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 P\'fcr\'ebasya p\'fcr\'ebam \'e4d\'e4ya p\'fcr\'ebam ev\'e4va\'e7i\'f1yate.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  Therefore He is the wonderful cause. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Govindam}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid16664248  \'e4di-puru\'f1a\'e0 tam aha\'e0 bhaj\'e4mi}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 .
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9\line sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9\line 
an\'e4dir \'e4dir govinda\'f9\line sarva-k\'e4ra\'eba-k\'e4ra\'ebam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, who is known as Govinda, is the supreme controller. He has an eternal, blissful, spiritual body. He is the origin of all. He has no other origin, for He is the prime cause of all causes." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1785001\charrsid1785001 Brahma-sa
\'e0hit\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  5.1)
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
Even in this material world, we can understand that the sun has existed for millions of years and has given off heat and light since its creation, yet the sun still retains its power and never changes. What then is to be said of the supreme cause, }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 para\'e0 brahma,}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  K\'e5\'f1\'eba? Everything emanates from Him perpetually, yet He maintains His original form (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). K\'e5\'f1\'eba personally says in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (10.8), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 matta\'f9 sarva\'e0 pravartate:}{\insrsid4605116 
 "Everything emanates from Me." Everything emanates from K\'e5\'f1\'eba eternally, yet He is the same K\'e5\'f1\'eba and does not change. Therefore He is the shelter of all transcendentalists who are eager to get free from material bondage.
\par Everyone must take shelter of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. It is therefore advised:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ak\'e4ma\'f9 sarva-k\'e4mo v\'e4\line mok\'f1a-k\'e4ma ud\'e4ra-dh\'e9\'f9\line t\'e9vre
\'eba bhakti-yogena\line yajeta puru\'f1a\'e0 param
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Whether one desires everything or nothing or desires to merge into the existence of the Lord, he is intelligent only if he worships Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, by rendering transcendental loving service." (}{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  2.3.10) }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Para\'e0 brahma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the Supreme Lord, and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 para\'e0 dh\'e4ma,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the supreme repose, is K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore anyone who desires anything\emdash whether he be a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 karm\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yog\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \emdash should try to perceive the Supreme Personality of Godhead very seriously, and all of his desires will be fulfilled. The Lord says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ye yath\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 prapadyante t\'e4\'e0s tathaiva bhaj\'e4my aham:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "As the living entities surrender unto Me, I reward them accordingly." Even the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 karm\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  who wants everything for his enjoyment can get it from K\'e5\'f1\'eba. For K\'e5\'f1\'eba, supplying what he wants is not at all difficult. Actually, however, one should worship K\'e5
\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, for the sake of getting liberation.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9.}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  By studying the Vedic literature, one should understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As confirmed here, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarv\'e4gam\'e4mn\'e4ya-mah\'e4r\'ebav\'e4ya.}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  He is the ocean, and all Vedic knowledge flows toward Him. Therefore, intelligent transcendentalists take shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva-dharm\'e4
n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). This is the ultimate goal.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.16
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 16
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
