\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"But what need is there, Arjuna, for all this detailed knowledge? With a single fragment of Myself I pervade and support this entire universe." Thus K\'e5\'f1\'eba says that the entire material world is maintained by His partial representation as Param
\'e4tm\'e4. The Lord enters every universe as Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu and then expands Himself as K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu to enter the hearts of all living entities and even enter the atoms. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 A\'eb\'f2\'e4ntara-stha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntara-stham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 Every universe is full of atoms, and the Lord is not only within the universe but also within the atoms. Thus within every atom the Supreme Lord exists in His Vi\'f1\'ebu feature as Param\'e4tm\'e4, but all the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vi\'f1
\'ebu-tattvas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  emanate from K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (10.2), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 aham \'e4dir hi dev\'e4n\'e4m:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4di,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or beginning, of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 devas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  of this material world\emdash Brahm\'e4, Vi
\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7vara. Therefore He is described here as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhagavate b\'e5hate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Everyone is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhagav\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
everyone possesses opulence\emdash but K\'e5\'f1\'eba is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 b\'e5h\'e4n bhagav\'e4n,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the possessor of unlimited opulence. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1
\'eba\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the origin of everyone. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhava\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Even Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7vara come from K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Matta\'f9 paratara\'e0 n\'e4nyat ki\'efcid asti dhana\'efjaya:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 there is no personality superior to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Therefore Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6
h\'e4kura says that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhagavate b\'e5hate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  means "unto \'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eba."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 In this material world, everyone is a }{
