\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "A human being who identifies the body made of three elements as the self, who con
siders the by-products of the body to be his kinsmen, who considers the land of his birth to be worshipable, and who goes to a place of pilgrimage simply to bathe rather than to meet men of transcendental knowledge there is to be considered like a cow or 
an ass." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  10.84.13) Practically everyone, therefore, is a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pa\'e7u,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 an animal, and everyone is attacked by the crocodile of material existence. Not only the King of the elephants but every one of us is being attacked by the crocodile and is suffering the consequences.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Only K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a can deliver us from this material existence. Indeed, He is always trying to deliver us. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati.}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  He is within our hearts and is not at all inattentive. His only aim is to deliver us from mate
rial life. It is not that He becomes attentive to us only when we offer prayers to Him. Even before we offer our prayers, He incessantly tries to deliver us. He is never lazy in regard to our deliverance. Therefore this verse says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bh\'fcri-karu\'eb\'e4ya namo 'lay\'e4ya.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 It is the causeless mercy of the Supreme Lord that He always tries to bring us back home, back to Godhead. God is liberated, and He tries to make us liberated, but although He is constantly trying, we refuse to accept His instructions (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). Nonetheless, He has not become angry. Therefore He is described here as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bh\'fcri-karu\'eb\'e4ya,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  unlimitedly merciful in delivering us from this miserable material condition of life and taking us back home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.3.18
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 18
