\cs3005\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 When the King of the elephants was describing the supreme authority, without mentioning any particular person, he did not invoke the demigods, headed by Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7
iva, Indra and Candra. Thus none of them approached him. However, because Lord Hari is the Supersoul, Puru\'f1ottama, the Personality of Godhead, He appeared before Gajendra.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
From the description of Gajendra, he apparently was aiming at the supreme authority although he did not know who the supreme authority is. He
 conjectured, "There is a supreme authority who is above everything." Under the circumstances, the Lord's various expansions, such as Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7
iva, Candra and Indra, all thought, "Gajendra is not asking our help. He is asking the help of the Supr
eme, who is above all of us." As Gajendra has described, the Supreme Lord has various parts and parcels, including the demigods, human beings and animals, all covered by separate forms. Although the demigods are in charge of maintaining different aspects 
of the universe, Gajendra thought that they were unable to rescue him. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Hari\'e0 vin\'e4 naiva m\'e5ti\'e0 taranti:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 no one can rescue anyone from the dangers of birth, death, old age and disease. It is only the Supreme Personality of Godhead who can rescue one from the 
dangers of material existence. Therefore an intelligent person, to get free from this dangerous existence, approaches the Supreme Personality of Godhead, not any demigod. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (7.20), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9 prapadyante 'nya-devat\'e4\'f9:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 those who are unintelligent approach the various demigods for temporary material benefits. Actually, however, these demigods cannot rescue the living entity from the dangers of material existence. Like other living entities, the demigods are merely
 external parts of the Supreme Personality of Godhead's transcendental body. As stated in the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras, sa \'e4tma-a\'ecg\'e4ny any\'e4 devat\'e4\'f9.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 Within the body is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4tm\'e4,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  the soul, whereas the various parts of the body like the hands and legs are external. Similarly, the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4tm\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  of the entire cosmic manifestation is N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and all the demigods, human beings and other living entities are parts of His body.

\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
It may also be concluded that since a tree lives on the strength of its root and when the root 
is nourished with water all the parts of the tree are nourished, one should worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the original root of everything. Although the Supreme Personality of Godhead is very difficult to approach, He is very near to u
s
 because He lives within our hearts. As soon as the Lord understands that one is seeking His favor by fully surrendering, naturally He immediately takes action. Therefore although the demigods did not come to the aid of Gajendra, the Supreme Personality o
f Godhead immediately appeared before him because of his fervent prayer. This does not mean that the demigods were angry with Gajendra, for actually when Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is worshiped, all the other demigods are also worshiped. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Yasmin tu\'f1\'f6e jagat tu\'f1\'f6am:}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  if the Supreme Personality of Godhead is satisfied, everyone is satisfied.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yath\'e4 taror m\'fcla-ni\'f1ecanena\line t\'e5pyanti tat-skandha-bhujopa\'e7\'e4kh\'e4
