\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4418615 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 This Fourth Chapter describes the pre
vious birth of Gajendra and the crocodile. It tells how the crocodile became a Gandharva and how Gajendra became an associate of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 There was a king on the Gandharva planet whose name was H\'fch\'fc. Once this King H\'fch\'fc was enjoy
ing with women in the water, and while enjoying he pulled the leg of Devala \'c5\'f1i, who was also taking a bath in the water. Upon this, the sage became very angry and immediately cursed him to become a crocodile. King H\'fch\'fc
 was very sorry when cursed in that way, and he begged pardon from the sage, who in compassion gave him the benediction that he would be freed when Gajendra was delivered by the Personality of Godhead. Thus the crocodile was delivered when killed by N\'e4
r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par When Gajendra, by the mercy of the Lord, became one of the Lord's associates in Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha, he got four hands. This achievement is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 s\'e4r\'fcpya-mukti,}{\insrsid4605116 
 or the liberation of receiving a spiritual body exactly like that of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Gajendra, in his previous birth, had been a great devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. His name was Indradyumna, and he was the King of the T\'e4
mila country. Following the Vedic principles, this King retired from family life and constructed a small cottage in the Malay\'e4cala Hills, where he always worshiped the Supreme Personality of Godhead in silence. Agastya \'c5\'f1
i, along with many disciples, once approached King Indradyumna's }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama,}{\insrsid4605116  but because the King was meditating on the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he could not receive Agastya \'c5\'f1
i properly. Thus the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e5\'f1i}{\insrsid4605116  became very angry
 and cursed the King to become a dull elephant. In accordance with this curse, the King was born as an elephant, and he forgot all about his previous activities in devotional service. Nonetheless, in his birth as an elephant, when he was dangerously attac
k
ed by the crocodile, he remembered his past life in devotional service and remembered a prayer he had learned in that life. Because of this prayer, he again received the mercy of the Lord. Thus he was immediately delivered, and he became one of the Lord's
 four-handed associates.
\par \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 ends this chapter by describing the good fortune of the elephant. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 says that by hearing the narration of Gajendra's deliverance, one can also get the opportunity to be delivered. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 vividly describes this, and thus the chapter ends.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.4.1
