\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3012\fs28\cf9\insrsid4605116\charrsid8146024 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: }{
\cs3005\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
My dear King, after Agastya Muni had thus cursed King Indradyumna, the Muni left that place along with his disciples. Since the King was a devotee, he accepted Agastya Muni's curse as welcome because it was the desire of the Suprem
e Personality of Godhead. Therefore, although in his next life he got the body of an elephant, because of devotional service he remembered how to worship and offer prayers to the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 This is the unique position of a devotee of the Supreme Persona
lity of Godhead. Although the King was cursed, he welcomed the curse because a devotee is always aware that nothing can happen without the desire of the Supreme Lord. Although the King was not at fault, Agastya Muni cursed him, and when this happened the 
King considered it to be due to his past misdeeds. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Tat te 'nukamp\'e4\'e0 susam\'e9k\'f1am\'e4\'eba\'f9}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  10.14.8). This is a practical example of how a devotee thinks. He regards any reverses in life as blessings of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, instead o
f being agitated by such reverses, he continues his activities of devotional service, and K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a takes care of him and enables him to be promoted to the spiritual world, back to Godhead. If a devotee has to suffer the reactions of his past misdeeds, the Sup
reme Lord arranges for him to be given only a token of these reactions, and very soon he is freed from all the reactions of material contamination. One should therefore adhere to devotional service, and the Lord Himself will very soon see to one's promoti
on to the spiritual world. A devotee should not be disturbed by unfortunate circumstances, but must continue his regular program, depending on the Lord for everything. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 upadh\'e4rayan,}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  "considering," is very significant in this verse. This word indicates that a devotee knows what is what; he understands what is happening in material, conditional life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.4.13
