\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 The brother of T\'e4
masa, the fourth Manu, who has previously been described, was the fifth Manu, Raivata. The sons of Raivata included Arjuna, Bali and Vindhya. During the reign of this Manu, Indra, the King of heaven, was known as Vibhu. Among the demigods were the Bh\'fc
tarayas, and among the seven }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e5\'f1is}{\insrsid4605116  were Hira\'ebyarom\'e4, Veda\'e7ir\'e4 and \'dcrdhvab\'e4hu. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e5\'f1i}{\insrsid4605116  known as \'c7ubhra, by his wife, Viku\'eb\'f6h\'e4
, gave birth to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha. This Supreme Personality of Godhead manifested a Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha planet at the request of Ram\'e4dev\'e9. His power and activities are mentioned in the Third Canto.
\par The sixth Manu was C\'e4k\'f1u\'f1a, the son of Cak\'f1u Manu. Among the sons of the sixth Manu were P\'fcru, P\'fcru\'f1a and Sudyumna. During the reign of this Manu, Mantradruma was Indra, the King of the heavenly planets. Among the demigods were the 
\'c4pyas, and among the seven }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e5\'f1is}{\insrsid4605116  were Havi\'f1m\'e4n and V\'e9raka. The wife of Vair\'e4ja, whose name was Devasambh\'fcti, gave birth to Ajita, an incarnation
 of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This Ajita, taking the shape of a tortoise and holding the mountain known as Mandara on His back, churned the ocean and produced nectar for the demigods.
\par Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it was very eager to hear about the churning of the ocean, and therefore \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 began to explain to him how the demigods, having been cursed by Durv\'e4s\'e4 Muni, were defeated in battle by the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 asuras.}{\insrsid4605116  When the demigods were deprived of their heavenly kingdom, they went to the assembly house of Lord Brahm\'e4 and informed Lord Brahm\'e4 of what had happened. Then Brahm\'e4
