\emdash \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 iti}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash thus; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4bh\'e4\'f1ya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
talking; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sur\'e4n}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the demigods; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vedh\'e4\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash Lord Brahm\'e4
, who is the head of this universe and who gives everyone good sense in Vedic knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 saha}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash with; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 devai\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the demigods; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 arim-dama}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, subduer of all kinds of enemies (such as the senses); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ajitasya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash of the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 padam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash to the place; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 s\'e4k\'f1\'e4t}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash directly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jag\'e4ma}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash went; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tamasa\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the world of darkness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 param}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash transcendental to, beyond.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it, subduer of all enemies, after Lord Brahm\'e4 finished speaking to the demigods, he took them with him to the abode of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, which is beyond this material world. The Lord's abode is on an island called \'c7vetadv\'e9
pa, which is situated in the ocean of milk.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it is addressed here as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 arindama,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 "subduer of all enemies." Not only do we have enemies outside of our bodies, but within our bodies there are many enemies, such as lusty desires, anger and greed. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it is specifically addressed as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 arindama}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 because in his political life he was able to subdue all kinds of enemies, and even though he was a young king, as soon as he heard that he was going to die within seven days, he immediately left his kingdom
. He did not follow the dictates of enemies within his body, such as lust, greed and anger. He was not at all angry with the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 muni's}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 son who had cursed him. Rather, he accepted the curse and prepared for his death in the association of \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9. Death is inevitable; no one can surpass the force of death. Therefore Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it, while fully alive, wanted to hear }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  He is consequently addressed here as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 arindama.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Another word, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sura-priya,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is also significant. Although K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is equal toward everyone, He is especially inclined toward His devotees (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
ye bhajanti tu m\'e4\'e0 bhakty\'e4 mayi te te\'f1u c\'e4py aham}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). The devotees are all demigods. There are two kinds of men within this world. One is called the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 deva,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  and the other is called the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asura.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  states:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 dvau bh\'fcta-sargau loke 'smin\line daiva \'e4sura eva ca\line vi\'f1\'ebu-bhakta\'f9
 sm\'e5to daiva\line \'e4suras tad-viparyaya\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Anyone who is a devotee of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba is called a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 deva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and others, even though they may be devotees of demigods, are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asuras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  R\'e4va\'eb
a, for example, was a great devotee of Lord \'c7iva, but he is described as an }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asura.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Similarly, Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu is described as a great devotee of Lord Brahm\'e4, yet he was also an }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asura.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Therefore, only the devotee of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sura,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  not }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asura.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is very much pleased with His devotees, even if they are not on the topmost stage of devotional service. Even on the lower stages of devotional service one is transcendental, and if one continues with devotional life, he continues to be a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 deva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sura.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  If one continues in this way, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a will always be pleased with him and will give him all instructions so that he may very easily return home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Concerning }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ajitasya padam,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  the abode of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the milk ocean of this material world, \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura says: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pada\'e0 k\'f1
\'e9rodadhi-stha-\'e7vetadv\'e9pa\'e0 tamasa\'f9 prak\'e5te\'f9 param.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The island known as \'c7vetadv\'e9pa, which is in the ocean of milk, is transcendental. It has nothin
g to do with this material world. A city government may have a rest house where the governor and important government officers stay. Such a rest house is not an ordinary house. Similarly, although \'c7vetadv\'e9
pa, which is in the ocean of milk, is in this material world, it is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 para\'e0 padam,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  transcendental.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.5.25
