\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 There [at \'c7vetadv\'e9pa], Lord Brahm\'e4
 offered prayers to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, even though he had never seen the Supreme Lord. Simply because Lord Brahm\'e4 had heard about the Supreme Personality of Godhead fro
m Vedic literature, with a fixed mind he offered the Lord prayers as written or approved by Vedic literature.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 It is said that when Brahm\'e4
 and the other demigods go to see the Supreme Personality of Godhead in \'c7vetadv\'e9pa, they cannot directly see Him, but their prayers are heard by the Lord, and the needful action is taken. This we have seen in many instances. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7ruta-p\'fcrv\'e4ya}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  is significant. We get experience by directly seeing or by hearing. If it is not possible to see someone directly, we c
an hear about him from authentic sources. Sometimes people ask whether we can show them God. This is ludicrous. It is not necessary for one to see God before he can accept God. Our sensory perception is always incomplete. Therefore, even if we see God, we
 may not be able to understand Him. When K\'e5\'f1\'eba was on earth, many, many people saw Him but could not understand that He is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4 m\'e4nu\'f1
\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4\'e7ritam.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  Even though the rascals and fools saw K\'e5\'f1\'eba personally
, they could not understand that He is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Even upon seeing God personally, one who is unfortunate cannot understand Him. Therefore we have to hear about God, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, from the authentic Vedic literature and from persons who understand the Vedic version properly. Even though Brahm\'e4 had not seen the Supreme Personality of Godhead before, he was confident that the Lord was there in \'c7vetadv\'e9
pa. Thus he took the opportunity to go there and offer prayers to the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 These prayers w
ere not ordinary concocted prayers. Prayers must be approved by Vedic literature, as indicated in this verse by the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 daiv\'e9bhir g\'e9rbhi\'f9.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  In our K\'e5\'f1
\'eba consciousness movement we do not allow any song that has not been approved or sung by bona fide devotees. We cannot allow cinema songs to be sung in the temple. We generally sing two songs. One is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7r\'e9-k\'e5
\'f1\'eba-caitanya prabhu nity\'e4nanda \'e7r\'e9-advaita gad\'e4dhara \'e7r\'e9v\'e4s\'e4di-gaura-bhakta-v\'e5nda.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  This is bona fide. It is always mentioned in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  and it is accepted by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4c\'e4ryas.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The other, of course, is the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4-mantra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 \emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4
ma, Hare Hare. We may also sing the songs of Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura, Bhaktivinoda \'d6h\'e4kura and Locana d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura, but these two songs\emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "\'e7r\'e9-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-caitanya}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 " and the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4-mantra}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 \emdash 
are sufficient to please the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although we cannot see Him. Seeing the Lord is not as important as appreciating Him from the authentic literature or the authentic statements of authorized persons.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.5.26
