\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e7r\'e9-brahm\'e4 uv\'e4ca}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash Lord Brahm\'e4 said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 avikriyam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto the Personality of Godhead, who never changes (as opposed to material existence); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 satyam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the eternal supreme truth; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 anantam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unlimited; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4dyam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the original cause of all causes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 guh\'e4-\'e7ayam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash present in everyone's heart; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ni\'f1
kalam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash without any decrease in potency; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 apratarkyam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash inconceivable, not within the jurisdiction of material arguments; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mana\'f9-agray\'e4nam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash more quick than the mind, inconceivable to mental speculation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vacas\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by jugglery of words; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 aniruktam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash indescribable; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nam\'e4mahe}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all of us demigods offer our respectful obeisances; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 deva-varam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
unto the Supreme Lord, who is not equaled or surpassed by anyone; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vare\'ebyam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the supreme worshipable, who is worshiped by the G\'e4yatr\'e9 }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mantra.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3012\fs28\cf9\insrsid4605116\charrsid8146024 Lord Brahm\'e4 said:}{
\cs3005\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  O Supreme Lord, O changeless, unlimited supreme truth. You are the origin of everything. Being all-pervading, You are in everyone's heart and also in the a
tom. You have no material qualities. Indeed, You are inconceivable. The mind cannot catch You by speculation, and words fail to describe You. You are the supreme master of everyone, and therefore You are worshipable for everyone. We offer our respectful o
beisances unto You.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid2624936 PURPORT}{\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead is not anything of material creation. Everything material must change from one form to another\emdash for example, from earth to earthen pot and from earthen pot to earth again. All our creations are t
emporary, impermanent. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, however, is eternal, and similarly the living entities, who are parts of Him, are also eternal (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4
tana\'f9}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ). The Supreme Personality of Godhead is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 san\'e4tana,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  eternal,
 and the individual living entities are also eternal. The difference is that K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or God, is the supreme eternal, whereas the individual souls are minute, fragmental eternals. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4
}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (13.3), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'f1etra-j\'efa\'e0 c\'e4pi m\'e4\'e0 viddhi sarva-k\'f1etre\'f1u bh\'e4rata.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 Although the Lord is a living being and the individual souls are living beings, the Supreme Lord, unlike the individual souls, is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vibhu,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  all-pervading, and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ananta,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  unlimited. The Lord is the cause of everything. The living entities are innumerable
, but the Lord is one. No one is greater than Him, and no one is equal to Him. Thus the Lord is the supreme worshipable object, as understood from the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 na tat-sama\'e7 c\'e4bhyadhika\'e7 ca d\'e5\'e7yate}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ). The Lord is supreme because no one can evaluate Him
 by mental speculation or jugglery of words. The Lord can travel more quickly than the mind. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7ruti-mantras}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7opani
\'f1ad}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  it is said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 anejad eka\'e0 manaso jav\'e9yo\line nainad dev\'e4 \'e4pnuvan p\'fcrvam ar\'f1at\line 
tad dh\'e4vato 'ny\'e4n atyeti ti\'f1\'f6hat\line tasminn apo m\'e4tari\'e7v\'e4 dadh\'e4ti
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Although fixed in His abode, the Personality of Godhead is swifter than the mind and can overcome all others running. The powerful demigods cannot approach Him. Although in one place, He controls those who supply the air and rain. He surpasses all i
n excellence." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  4) Thus the Supreme is never to be equaled by the subordinate living entities.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
Because the Lord is situated in everyone's heart and the individual living entity is not, never should the individual living entity be equated with the Supreme Lord. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (15.15) the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarvasya c\'e4ha\'e0 h\'e5di sannivi\'f1\'f6a\'f9:}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 "I am situated in everyone's heart." This does not mean, however, that everyone is equal to the Lord. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7ruti-mantras}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  it is also said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 h\'e5di hy ayam \'e4tm\'e4 prati\'f1\'f6hita\'f9.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  In the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 satya\'e0 para\'e0 dh\'e9mahi.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  say, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 satya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4nam anantam}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ni\'f1kala\'e0 ni\'f1kriya\'e0 \'e7\'e4nta
\'e0 niravadyam.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  God is supreme. Although naturally He does not do anything, He is doing everything. As the Lord says in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{
\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid16338951 
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarva\'e0\line jagad avyakta-m\'fcrtin\'e4\line mat-sth\'e4
ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"By Me, in My unmanifested form, this entire universe is pervaded. All beings are in Me, but I am not in them." (Bg. 9.4)
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9\line s\'fcyate sacar\'e4caram\line hetun\'e4
nena kaunteya\line jagad viparivartate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "This material nature, working under My direction, O son of Kunt\'e9
, is producing all moving and unmoving beings. By its rule this manifestation is created and annihilated again and again." (Bg. 9.10) Thus although the Lord is silent in His abode, He is doing everything through His different energies (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 par\'e4sya \'e7aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ).
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 All the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantras,}{
\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7ruti-mantras,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  are included in this verse spoken by Lord Brahm\'e4, for Brahm\'e4 and
 his followers, the Brahma-samprad\'e4ya, understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead through the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 parampar\'e4}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 system. We have to gain understanding through the words of our predecessors. There are twelve }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4janas,}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or authorities, of whom Brahm\'e4 is one.
\par }\pard\plain \s1434\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 svayambh\'fcr n\'e4rada\'f9 \'e7ambhu\'f9\line kum\'e4ra\'f9 kapilo manu\'f9\line prahl
\'e4do janako bh\'e9\'f1mo\line balir vaiy\'e4sakir vayam\line (}{\cs2542\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid9896351 6.3.20)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 We belong to the disciplic succession of Brahm\'e4
, and therefore we are known as the Brahma-samprad\'e4ya. As the demigods follow Lord Brahm\'e4 to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead, we also have to follow the authorities of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 parampar\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  system to understand the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.5.27
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 27
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
