\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 vipa\'e7cita\'e0 pr\'e4\'eba-mano-dhiy\'e4tman\'e4m
\par arthendriy\'e4bh\'e4sam anidram avra\'ebam
\par ch\'e4y\'e4tapau yatra na g\'e5dhra-pak\'f1au
\par tam ak\'f1ara\'e0 kha\'e0 tri-yuga\'e0 vraj\'e4mahe
\par }\pard\plain \s2996\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4283093 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vipa\'e7citam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
unto the omniscient; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 pr\'e4\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash how the living force is working; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mana\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
how the mind is working; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 dhiya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash how the intelligence is working; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4tman\'e4m}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
of all living entities; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 artha}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the objects of the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 indriya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the senses; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4bh\'e4sam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 anidram}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash always awake and free from ignorance; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 avra\'ebam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash without a material body subject to pains and pleasures; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ch\'e4y\'e4-\'e4tapau}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
\emdash the shelter for all who are suffering from ignorance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yatra}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash wherein; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash not; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 g\'e5dhra-pak\'f1au}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash partiality toward any living being; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto Him; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ak\'f1aram}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash infallible; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 kham}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all-pervading like the sky; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tri-yugam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash appearing with six opulences in three }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yugas}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (Satya, Tret\'e4 and Dv\'e4para); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vraj\'e4mahe}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash I take shelter.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead directly and indirectly knows how everything, including the living force, mind and intelligence, is working under His con
trol. He is the illuminator of everything and has no ignorance. He does not have a material body subject to the reactions of previous activities, and He is free from the ignorance of partiality and materialistic education. I therefore take shelter of the 
lotus feet of the Supreme Lord, who is eternal, all-pervading and as great as the sky and who appears with six opulences in three yugas [Satya, Tret\'e4 and Dv\'e4para].
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 In the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9
mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  the Supreme Personality of Godhead is described in this way: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 janm\'e4dy asya yato'nvay\'e4d itarata\'e7 c\'e4rthe\'f1v abhij\'efa\'f9.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  The Lord is the origin of all emanations, and He directly and indirectly knows everything about all the activities within His creation. Therefore the Lord is addressed here as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vipa\'e7citam,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  one who is full of all knowledge or who knows everything. The Lord is the Supreme Soul, and He knows everything about the living entities and their senses.

\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 anidram,}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  meaning "always awake and free from ignorance," is very important in this verse. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (15.15), }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca:}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 it is the Lord who gives intelligence to everyone and who causes everyone to forget. There are millions and millions of living entities, and the Lord gives them directions. Therefore He ha
s no time to sleep, and He is never in ignorance of our activities. The Lord is the witness of everything; He sees what we are doing at every moment. The Lord is not covered by a body resulting from }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 karma.}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Our bodies are formed as a result of our past deeds (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 karma\'eb\'e4 daiva-netre\'eba}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
), but the Supreme Personality of Godhead does not have a material body, and therefore He has no }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 avidy\'e4,}{\insrsid4605116  ignorance. He does not sleep, but is always alert and awake.
\par The Supreme Lord is described as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 tri-yuga}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  because although He appeared variously in Satya-yuga, Tret\'e4-yuga and Dv\'e4
para-yuga, when He appeared in Kali-yuga He never declared Himself the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-var\'eba\'e0 tvi\'f1\'e4k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'e0\line s\'e4\'ecgop\'e4\'ecg\'e4
stra-p\'e4r\'f1adam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 The Lord appears in Kali-yuga as a devotee. Thus although He is K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, He chants the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  like a devotee. Still, }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (11.5.32) recommends:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yaj\'efai\'f9 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-pr\'e4yair\line yajanti hi sumedhasa\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, whose complexion is not black like that of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a but is golden (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tvi\'f1\'e4k\'e5\'f1\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ), is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He is accompanied by associates like Nity\'e4nanda, Advaita, Gad\'e4dhara and \'c7r\'e9v\'e4
sa. Those who are sufficiently intelligent worship this Supreme Personality of Godhead by performing }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-yaj\'efa.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  In this incarna
tion, the Supreme Lord declares Himself not to be the Supreme Lord, and therefore He is known as Tri-yuga.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.5.28
\par }\pard\plain \s2994\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4605116 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT 28
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 TEXT
