aNaai>a iv}{\f0\insrsid4605116 \'db}{\f35\insrsid4605116 u\'c0l/Ma\'edNaeiMa\line  Yad+aMaahuSTaMa*Ta& Pa[Pa}{\f0\insrsid4605116 \'db}{\f35\insrsid4605116 e )) 28 ))}{\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 ajasya cakra\'e0 tv ajayeryam\'e4\'eba\'e0
\par manomaya\'e0 pa\'efcada\'e7\'e4ram \'e4\'e7u
\par tri-n\'e4bhi vidyuc-calam a\'f1\'f6a-nemi
\par yad-ak\'f1am \'e4hus tam \'e5ta\'e0 prapadye
\par }\pard\plain \s2996\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4283093 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\insrsid4283093 SYNONYMS}{\v\insrsid4605116 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ajasya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
of the living being; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 cakram}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the wheel (the cycle of birth and death in this material world); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tu}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash but; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ajay\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash by the external energy of the Supreme Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e9ryam\'e4\'ebam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash going around with great force; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 mana\'f9-mayam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash which is nothing but a mental creation depending chiefly on the mind; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 pa\'efcada\'e7a}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash fifteen; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 aram}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash possessing spokes; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4
\'e7u}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash very quick; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tri-n\'e4bhi}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash having three naves (the three modes of material nature); }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vidyut}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash like electricity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 calam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash moving; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 a\'f1\'f6a-nemi}
{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash made of eight fellies (the eight external energies of the Lord}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid10910032\charrsid6049549 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bh\'fcmir \'e4po 'nalo v\'e4yu\'f9,}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  etc.); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yat}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash who; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ak\'f1am}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the hub; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4hu\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash they say; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash unto Him; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e5tam}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash the fact; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 prapadye}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash let us offer our respectful obeisances.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
In the cycle of material activities, the material body resembles the wheel of a mental chariot. The ten senses [five for working and five for gathering knowledge] and the five life airs within the body form the fift
een spokes of the chariot's wheel. The three modes of nature [goodness, passion and ignorance] are its center of activities, and the eight ingredients of nature [earth, water, fire, air, sky, mind, intelligence and false ego] comprise the rim of the wheel
.
 The external, material energy moves this wheel like electrical energy. Thus the wheel revolves very quickly around its hub or central support, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the Supersoul and the ultimate truth. We offer our respectful obeisa
nces unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
The cycle of repeated birth and death is figuratively described herein. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (7.5):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 apareyam itas tv any\'e4\'e0\line prak\'e5ti\'e0 viddhi me par\'e4m\line j\'e9va-bh\'fct
