\emdash persons who are sober, undisturbed by material agitation.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 The Supreme Personality of Godhead is situated in pure goodness [\'e7
uddha-sattva], and therefore He is eka-var\'eba\emdash the o\'e0k\'e4ra [pra\'ebava]. Because the Lord is beyond the cosmic manifestation, which is considered to be darkness, He is not 
visible to material eyes. Nonetheless, He is not separated from us by time or space, but is present everywhere. Seated on His carrier, Garu\'f2
a, He is worshiped by means of mystical yogic power by those who have achieved freedom from agitation. Let us all offer our respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Sattva\'e0 vi\'e7uddha\'e0 vasudeva-\'e7abditam}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  4.3.23). In this material world, the three modes of material nature\emdash 
goodness, passion and ignorance\emdash prevail. Among these three, goodness is the platform of knowledge
, and passion brings about a mixture of knowledge and ignorance, but the mode of ignorance is full of darkness. Therefore the Supreme Personality of Godhead is beyond darkness and passion. He is on the platform where goodness or knowledge is not disturbed
 by passion and ignorance. This is called the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vasudeva}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  platform. It is on this platform of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vasudeva}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  that V\'e4sudeva, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba, can appear. Thus K\'e5\'f1\'eba appeared on this planet as the son of Vasudeva. Because the Lord is situated beyond the three modes of materi
al nature, He is unseen by those who are dominated by these three modes. One must therefore become }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 dh\'e9ra,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 or undisturbed by the modes of material nature. The process of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yoga}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  may be practiced by one who is free from the agitation of these modes. Therefore }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yoga}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  is defined in this way: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yoga indriya-sa\'e0yama\'f9.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 As previously explained, we are disturbed by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 indriyas,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 or senses. Moreover, we are agitated by the three modes of material nature, which are imposed upon us by the external energy. In conditional life,
 the living entity moves turbulently in the whirlpool of birth and death, but when one is situated on the transcendental platform of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vi\'e7uddha-sattva,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 pure goodness, he can see the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who sits on the back of Garu\'f2a. Lord Brahm\'e4 offers his respectful obeisances unto that Supreme Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.5.30
