\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 As one can derive fire from wood, milk from the milk bag 
of the cow, food grains and water from the land, and prosperity in one's livelihood from industrial enterprises, so, by the practice of bhakti-yoga, even within this material world, one can achieve Your favor or intelligently approach You. Those who are p
ious all affirm this.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 Although the Supreme Personality of Godhead is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 nirgu\'eba,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  not to be found within this material world, the entire material world is pervaded by Him, as stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}
{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarvam}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ). The material world is nothin
g but an expansion of the Lord's material energy, and the entire cosmic manifestation rests upon Him (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mat-sth\'e4ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
). Nonetheless, the Supreme Lord cannot be found here (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 ). A devotee, however, can see the Supreme Personal
ity of Godhead through the practice of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  One ordinarily does not begin to practice }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  unless he has practiced it in previous births. Moreover, one can begin }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 only by the mercy of the spiritual master and K\'e5\'f1\'eba. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Guru-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pras\'e4de p\'e4ya bhakti-lat\'e4-b\'e9ja.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 The seed of devotional service is obtainable by the mercy of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  the spiritual master, and K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s3015\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7616644 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 Only by the practice of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 
bhakti-yoga}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  can one achieve the favor of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and see Him face to face (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 prem\'e4\'efjana-cchurita-bhakti-vilocanena santa\'f9 sadaiva h\'e5daye\'f1
u vilokayanti}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). One cannot see the Lord by other methods, such as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 karma, j\'ef\'e4na}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 yoga.}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  Under the direction of the spiritual master, one must cultivate }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'eb
o\'f9 smara\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). Then, even within this material world, although the Lord is not visible, a devotee can see Him. This is confirmed in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti y\'e4v\'e4n ya\'e7 c\'e4smi tattvata\'f9}{\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ) and in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3017\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakty\'e4ham ekay\'e4 gr\'e4hya\'f9}{\insrsid4605116 
). Thus by devotional service one can achieve the favor of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although He is not visible or understandable to materialistic persons.
\par In this verse, the cultivation of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  is compared to m
any material activities. By friction one can get fire from wood, by digging the earth one can get food grains and water, and by agitating the milk bag of the cow one can get nectarean milk. Milk is compared to nectar, which one can drink to become immorta
l
. Of course, simply drinking milk will not make one immortal, but it can increase the duration of one's life. In modern civilization, men do not think milk to be important, and therefore they do not live very long. Although in this age men can live up to 
o
ne hundred years, their duration of life is reduced because they do not drink large quantities of milk. This is a sign of Kali-yuga. In Kali-yuga, instead of drinking milk, people prefer to slaughter an animal and eat its flesh. The Supreme Personality of
 Godhead, in His instructions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  advises }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 go-rak\'f1ya,}{\insrsid4605116 
 which means cow protection. The cow should be protected, milk should be drawn from the cows, and this milk should be prepared in various ways. One should take ample milk, and thus one can pr
olong one's life, develop his brain, execute devotional service, and ultimately attain the favor of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As it is essential to get food grains and water by digging the earth, it is also essential to give protection to the co
ws and take nectarean milk from their milk bags.
\par The people of this age are inclined toward industrial enterprises for comfortable living, but they refuse to endeavor to execute devotional service, by which they can achieve the ultimate goal of life by retu
rning home, back to Godhead. Unfortunately, as it is said, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 na te vidu\'f9 sv\'e4rtha-gati\'e0 hi vi\'f1\'ebu\'e0 dur\'e4\'e7ay\'e4 ye bahir-artha-m\'e4nina\'f9.}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 
 People without spiritual education do not know that the ultimate goal of life is to go back home, back to Godhead. Forgetting this aim of life, they are working very hard in disappointment and frustration (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid11874098 mogh\'e4\'e7\'e4
 mogha-karm\'e4\'ebo mogha-}{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4n\'e4 vicetasa\'f9}{\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 ). The so-called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 vai\'e7yas}{\insrsid4605116 \emdash the industrialists or businessmen\emdash 
are involved in big, big industrial enterprises, but they are not interested
 in food grains and milk. However, as indicated here, by digging for water, even in the desert, we can produce food grains; when we produce food grains and vegetables, we can give protection to the cows; while giving protection to the cows, we can draw fr
om them abundant quantities of milk; and by getting enough milk and combining it with food grains and vegetables, we can prepare hundreds of nectarean foods. We can happily eat this food and thus avoid industrial enterprises and joblessness.
\par Agriculture and cow protection are the way to become sinless and thus be attracted to devotional service. Those who are sinful cannot be attracted by devotional service. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  (7.28):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ye\'f1\'e4\'e0 tv anta-gata\'e0 p\'e4pa\'e0\line jan\'e4n\'e4\'e0 pu\'ebya-karma\'eb\'e4
m\line te dvandva-moha-nirmukt\'e4\line bhajante m\'e4\'e0 d\'e5\'f2ha-vrat\'e4\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Persons who have acted piously in previous lives and in this life, whose sinful actions are completely eradicated and who are freed from the duality of delusion, engage themselves in My service with determination." The ma
jority of people in this age of Kali are sinful, short-living, unfortunate and disturbed (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mand\'e4\'f9 sumanda-matayo manda-bh\'e4gy\'e4 hy upadrut\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). For them, Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu has advised:
