\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash O Lord, whose navel resembles a lotus flower, or from whose navel grows a lotus flower; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ati-cira}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
for an extremely long time; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e9psita}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash desiring; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 artham}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash 
for the ultimate goal of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 d\'e5\'f1\'f6v\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash seeing; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gat\'e4\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash in our vision; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nirv\'e5tam}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash transcendental happiness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 adya}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash today; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 
sarve}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash all of us; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gaj\'e4\'f9}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash elephants; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 dava-art\'e4\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash being afflicted in a forest fire; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 iva}{\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 g\'e4\'ecgam ambha\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 \emdash with water from the Ganges.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3003\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid6049549 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
Elephants afflicted by a forest fire become very happy when they get water from the Ganges. Similarly, O my Lord, from whose navel grows a lotus flower, since You have now appeared before us, we have become transcendentally happy. By seeing Your
 Lordship, whom we have desired to see for a very long time, we have achieved our ultimate goal in life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
The devotees of the Lord are always very eager to see the Supreme Lord face to face, but they do not demand that the Lord come before them, for a pure devotee considers such a demand to be contrary to devotional service. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu teaches this lesson in His }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7ik\'f1\'e4\'f1\'f6aka.}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Adar\'e7an\'e4n marma-hat\'e4\'e0 karotu v\'e4.}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  The devotee is always eager to see the Lord face to face, but if he is brokenheart
ed because he cannot see the Lord, even life after life, he will never command the Lord to appear. This is a sign of pure devotion. Therefore in this verse we find the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ati-cira-\'e9psita-artham,}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  meaning that the devotee aspires for a long, long time to see the Lord. If the Lord, by His own pleasure, appears before the devotee, the devotee feels extremely happy, as Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja felt when he personally saw the Supreme Personality of Godhead. When Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw the Lord, he had no desire to ask the Lord for any benediction. Indeed, simply by seeing the Lord, Dhruva Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja felt so satisfied that he did not want to ask the Lord for any benediction (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sv\'e4min k\'e5t\'e4rtho 'smi vara\'e0 na y\'e4ce}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
). A pure devotee, whether able or unable to see the Lord, always engages in the Lord's devotional service, always hoping that at some time the Lord may be pleased to appear before him so that he can see the Lord face to face.
