 the source of butter. Butter, when clarified by melting, produces ghee, or clarified butter, which is inevitably necessary for performing great ritualistic sacrifices. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 (}{
\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 18.5}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ), yaj\'efa-d\'e4na-tapa\'f9-karma na ty\'e4jya\'e0 k\'e4ryam eva tat:}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549 
 sacrifice, charity and austerity are essential to keep human society perfect in peace and prosperity. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Yaj\'efa,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  the performance of sacrifice, is essential; to perform }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yaj\'efa,}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  clarified butter is absolutely necessary; and to get clarified butter, milk is necessary. Milk is produced when there are sufficient cows. Therefore in }{
