 kvacit tatra na bh\'fcta-sauh\'e5dam}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  is very important in this verse. We actually see 
that there are many Hindus, Muslims, Christians, Buddhists and religionists of other cults who adhere to their religious principles very nicely but are not equal to all living entities. Indeed, although they profess to be very religious, they kill poor an
imals. Such religion has no meaning. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3008\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid6049549  (1.2.8) says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 dharma\'f9 svanu\'f1\'f6hita\'f9 pu\'e0s\'e4\'e0\line vi\'f1vaksena-kath\'e4su ya\'f9
\line notp\'e4dayed yadi rati\'e0\line \'e7rama eva hi kevalam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
One may be very expert in following the religious principles of his own sect, but if he has no tendency to love the Supreme Personality of Godhead, his observance of religious principles is simply a waste of time. One must develop a sense of loving V\'e4
sudeva (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 v\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). The sign of a devotee is that he is a friend to everyone (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 suh\'e5da\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct
\'e4n\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). A devotee will never allow a poor animal to be killed in the name of religion. This is the difference between a superficially religious person and a devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644 We find that there hav
e been many great heroes in history, but they could not escape from the cruel hands of death. Even the greatest hero cannot escape from the ruling power of the Supreme Personality of Godhead when K\'e5\'f1\'eba comes as death. That is described by K\'e5
\'f1\'eba Himself: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e5tyu\'f9 sarva-hara\'e7 c\'e4ham.}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  The Lord, appearing as death, takes away a hero's so-called power. Even Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu could not be saved when }{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid12929836 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\cs3017\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116\charrsid7616644  appeared before him as death. One's material strength is nothing before the strength of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.8.22
