\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
In human society there are various activities performed for the protection of one's wealth and life by one's words, one's mind and one's actions, but they are all performed for o
ne's personal or extended sense gratification with reference to the body. All these activities are baffled because of being separate from devotional service. But when the same activities are performed for the satisfaction of the Lord, the beneficial resul
ts are distributed to everyone, just as water poured on the root of a tree is distributed throughout the entire tree.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 This is the distinction between materialistic activities and activities performed in K\'e5
\'f1\'eba consciousness. The entire world is active, and this includes the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 karm\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhaktas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  However, all activities except those of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhaktas,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the devotees, end in bafflement and a waste of time and energy. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Mogh\'e4\'e7\'e4 mogha-karm\'e4\'ebo mogha j\'ef\'e4n\'e4 vicetasa\'f9:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 if one is not a devote
e, his hopes, his activities and his knowledge are all baffled. A nondevotee works for his personal sense gratification or for the sense gratification of his family, society, community or nation, but because all such activities are separate from the Supre
me Personality of Godhead, they are considered }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asat.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  means bad or temporary, and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  means permanent and good. Activities performed for the satisfaction of K\'e5\'f1\'eba are permanent and good, but }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 activity, although sometimes celebrated as philanthropy, altruism, nationalism, this "ism" or that "ism," will never produce any permanent result and is therefore all bad. Even a little work done in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness is a permanent asset and is all-good because it is done for K\'e5\'f1\'eba, the all-good Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is everyone's friend (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 suh\'e5da\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the only enjoyer and proprietor of everything (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0 sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
). Therefore any activity performed for the Supreme Lord is permanent. As a result of such activities, the performer is immediately recognized. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Na ca tasm\'e4n manu\'f1ye\'f1u ka\'e7cin me priya-k\'e5ttama\'f9.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Such a devotee, because of full knowledge of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is immediately transcendental,
 although he may superficially appear to be engaged in materialistic activities. The only distinction between materialistic activity and spiritual activity is that material activity is performed only to satisfy one's own senses whereas spiritual activity 
is meant to satisfy the transcendental senses of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. By spiritual activity everyone factually benefits, whereas by materialistic activity no one benefits and instead one becomes entangled in the laws of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 karma.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Thus ends the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Eighth Canto, Ninth Chapter, of the }{
\cs2344\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  entitled "The Lord Incarnates as Mohin\'e9-m\'fcrti."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf18\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.10: The Battle Between the Demigods and the Demons
