\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.10 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4418615 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 
The summary of Chapter Ten is as follows. Because of envy, the fight between the demons and the demigods continued. When the demigods were almost defeated by demoniac maneuvers and became morose, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu appeared among them.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 Both the demigods and
 the demons are expert in activities involving the material energy, but the demigods are devotees of the Lord, whereas the demons are just the opposite. The demigods and demons churned the ocean of milk to get nectar from it, but the demons, not being dev
otees of the Lord, could derive no profit. After feeding nectar to the demigods, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu returned to His abode on the back of Garu\'f2a, but the demons, being most aggrieved, again declared war against the demigods. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, the son of Virocana, became the commander in chief of the demons. In the beginning of the battle, the demigods prepared to defeat the demons. Indra, King of heaven, fought with Bali, and other demigods, like V\'e4yu, Agni and Varu\'eb
a, fought against other leaders of the demons. In this
 fight the demons were defeated, and to save themselves from death they began to manifest many illusions through material maneuvers, killing many soldiers on the side of the demigods. The demigods, finding no other recourse, surrendered again to the Supre
me Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'ebu, who then appeared and counteracted all the illusions presented by the jugglery of the demons. Heroes among the demons such as K\'e4lanemi, M\'e4l\'e9, Sum\'e4l\'e9 and M\'e4lyav\'e4
n fought the Supreme Personality of Godhead and were all killed by the Lord. The demigods were thus freed from all dangers.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.10.1
