\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 
Having been graced by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the demigods began fighting the demons again, with renewed energy. King Indra released his thunderbolt against Bali, and when Bali fell, his friend Jambh\'e4
sura attacked Indra, who then cut off Jambh\'e4sura's head with his thunderbolt. When N\'e4rada Muni learned that Jambh\'e4sura had been killed, he informed Jambh\'e4sura's relatives Namuci, Bala and P\'e4
ka, who then went to the battlefield and attacked the demigods. Indra, King of heaven, severed the heads of Bala and P\'e4ka and released the weapon known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 kuli\'e7a,}{\insrsid4605116 
 the thunderbolt, against Namuci's shoulder. The thunderbolt, however, returned unsuccessful, and thus Indra became morose. At that time, an unseen voice came 
from the sky. The voice declared, "A dry or wet weapon cannot kill Namuci." Hearing this voice, Indra began to think of how Namuci could be killed. He then thought of foam, which is neither moist nor dry. Using a weapon of foam, he was able to kill Namuci
. Thus Indra and the other demigods killed many demons. Then, at the request of Lord Brahm\'e4, N\'e4rada went to the demigods and forbade them to kill the demons any longer. All the demigods then returned to their abodes. Following the instructions of N
\'e4rada, whatever demons remained alive on the battlefield took Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja to Asta Mountain. There, by the touch of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya's hand, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja regained his senses and consciousness, and those demons whose heads and bodies had not been completely lost were brought back to life by the mystic power of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya.
