\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
Pure devotees or great saintly persons who desire to achieve the highest goal in life and who are completely free from all material desires for sense gratification engage constantly in the transcendental service of Your lotus feet.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
One is in the material world when he thinks, "I am this body, and everything with reference to my body is mine." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Ato g\'e5ha-k\'f1etra-sut\'e4pta-vittair janasya moho 'yam aha\'e0 mameti.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 This is the symptom of material life. In the materialistic conception of life, one thinks, "This is my house, this is my land, this is my family, this is my state," and so on. But those who are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 munaya\'f9,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  saintly persons following in the footsteps of N\'e4rada Muni, simply engage in the transcendental loving service of the Lord without any personal desire for sense gratification. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Any\'e4bhil\'e4
\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0 j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Either in this life or in the next, the only concern of such saintly devotees is to serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Thus they are also absolute
 because they have no other desires. Being freed from the dualities of material desire, they are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7reyas-k\'e4m\'e4\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  In other words, they are not concerned with }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (religiosity), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 artha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (economic development), or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'e4ma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 (sense gratification). The only concern of such devotees is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mok\'f1a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  liberation. This }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mok\'f1a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 does not refer to becoming one with the Supreme like the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers. Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu explained that real }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mok\'f1a}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 means taking shelter of the lotus feet of the Personality of Godhead. The Lord clearly explained this fact while instructing S\'e4rvabhauma Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya. S\'e4rvabhauma Bha\'f6\'f6\'e4c\'e4rya wanted to correct the word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mukti-pade}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  but Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu informed him that there is no need to correct any word in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  He explained that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mukti-pade}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  refers to the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u, who offers }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mukti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and is therefore called Mukunda. A pure devotee is not concerned with material things. He is not concerned with religiosity, economic 
development or sense gratification. He is interested only in serving the lotus feet of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.12.7
