{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 asat}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash which is nonexistent, as the cause; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 dvayam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash both of them; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 advayam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
without duality; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 ca}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash and; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 svar\'ebam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash gold; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 k\'e5ta}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
manufactured into different forms; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4k\'e5tam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the original source of gold (the gold mine); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 iva}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash like; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 iha}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash in this world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vastu-bheda\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
difference in the substance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 aj\'ef\'e4nata\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash only because of ignorance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tvayi}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash unto You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 janai
\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash by the general mass of people; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vihita\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash it should be done; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 vikalpa\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash differentiation; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yasm\'e4t}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash because of; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gu\'eba-vyatikara\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash free from the differences created by the material modes of nature; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nirup\'e4dhikasya}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash without any material designation.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
My dear Lord, Your Lordship alone is the cause and the effect. Therefore, although You appear to be two, You are the absolute o
ne. As there is no difference between the gold of a golden ornament and the gold in a mine, there is no difference between cause and effect; both of them are the same. Only because of ignorance do people concoct differences and dualities. You are free fro
m material contamination, and since the entire cosmos is caused by You and cannot exist without You, it is an effect of Your transcendental qualities. Thus the conception that Brahman is true and the world false cannot be maintained.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura says that the living entities are representations of the Supreme Personality of Godhead's marginal potency whereas the various bodies accepted by the living entities are products of the material energy. Thus the body is considered mate
rial, and the soul is considered spiritual. The origin of them both, however, is the same Supreme Personality of Godhead. As the Lord explains in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (7.4-5):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bh\'fcmir \'e4po 'nalo v\'e4yu\'f9\line kha\'e0 mano buddhir eva ca\line aha\'eck\'e4
ra it\'e9ya\'e0 me\line bhinn\'e4 prak\'e5tir a\'f1\'f6adh\'e4
\par apareyam itas tv any\'e4\'e0\line prak\'e5ti\'e0 viddhi me par\'e4m\line j\'e9va-bh\'fct\'e4\'e0 mah\'e4-b\'e4ho\line yayeda\'e0 dh\'e4ryate jagat
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and false ego\emdash 
all together these eight comprise My separated material energies. But besides this inferior n
ature, O mighty-armed Arjuna, there is a superior energy of Mine, which consists of all living entities who are struggling with material nature and are sustaining the universe." Thus both matter and the living entities are manifestations of energy of the 
S
upreme Lord. Since the energy and the energetic are not different and since the material and marginal energies are both energies of the supreme energetic, the Supreme Lord, ultimately the Supreme Personality of Godhead is everything. In this regard, the e
xample may be given of gold that has not been molded and gold that has been molded into various ornaments. A gold earring and the gold in a mine are different only as cause and effect; otherwise they are the same. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  describes that Brahman is the cause of everything. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Janm\'e4dy asya yata\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 Everything is born of the Supreme Brahman, from which everything emanates as different energies. None of these energies, therefore, should be considered false. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s' differentiation between Brahman and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e4y\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is only due to ignorance.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad V\'e9rar\'e4ghava \'c4c\'e4rya, in his }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bh
\'e4gavata-candra-candrik\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  describes the Vai\'f1\'ebava philosophy as follows. The cosmic manifestation is described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 asat,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 cit}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 acit.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Matter is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 acit,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and the living force is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 cit,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  
but their origin is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, in whom there is no difference between matter and spirit. According to this conception, the cosmic manifestation, consisting of both matter and spirit, is not different from the Supreme Personality o
f Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Ida\'e0 hi vi\'e7va\'e0 bhagav\'e4n ivetara\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  "This cosmic manifestation is also the Supreme Personality of Godhead, although it appears different from Him." In }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (9.4) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarva\'e0\line jagad avyakta-m\'fcrtin\'e4\line mat-sth\'e4
ni sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line na c\'e4ha\'e0 te\'f1v avasthita\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"By Me, in My unmanifested form, this entire universe is pervaded. All beings are in Me, but I am not in them." Thus although someone may say that the Supreme Person is different from the cosmic manifestation, actually He is not. The Lord says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarvam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 "In My impersonal feature I am spread throughout the world." Therefore, this world is not different from Him. The difference is a difference in names. For example, whether we speak of gold earrings, gold bangle
s or gold necklaces, ultimately they are all gold. In a similar way, all the different manifestations of matter and spirit are ultimately one in the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid12259764 E}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
kam ev\'e4dvit\'e9ya\'e0 brahma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  This is the Vedic version (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Ch\'e4ndogya Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  6.2.
1). There is oneness because everything emanates from the Supreme Brahman. The example already given is that there is no difference between a golden earring and the gold mine as it is. The Vai\'e7e\'f1ika philosophers, however, because of their M\'e4y\'e4
v\'e4da conception, create differences. They say, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 brahma satya\'e0 jagan mithy\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  "The Absolute Truth is real, and the cosmic manifestation is false." But why should the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  be considered }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mithy\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ? The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 is an emanation from Brahman. Therefore the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is also truth.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vai\'f1\'ebavas, therefore, do not consider the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagat}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  to be }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mithy\'e4;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  rather, they regard everything as reality in connection with the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 an\'e4saktasya vi\'f1ay\'e4n\line yath\'e4rham upayu\'efjata\'f9\line nirbandha\'f9 k
\'e5\'f1\'eba-sambandhe\line yukta\'e0 vair\'e4gyam ucyate
\par pr\'e4pa\'efcikatay\'e4 buddhy\'e4\line hari-sambandhi-vastuna\'f9\line mumuk\'f1ubhi\'f9 parity\'e4go\line vair\'e4gya\'e0 phalgu kathyate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Things should be accepted for the Lord's service and not for one's personal sense gratification. If one accepts something without attachment and accepts it because it is related to K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one's renunciation is called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yukta\'e0 vair\'e4gyam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Whatever is favorable for the rendering of service to the Lord should be accepted and should not be rejected as a material thing." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  1.2.255-256) The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagat}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  should not be rejected as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mithy\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 It is truth, and the truth is realized when everything is engaged in the service of the Lord. A flower accepted for one's sense gratification is material, but when the same flower is offered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead by 
a devotee, it is spiritual. Food taken and cooked for oneself is material, but food cooked for the Supreme Lord is spiritual }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pras\'e4da.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 This is a question of realization. Actually, everything is given by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore ever
ything is spiritual, but those who are not advanced in proper knowledge make distinctions because of the interactions of the three modes of material nature. In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 says that although the sun is the only light, the sunshine, whic
h is exhibited in seven colors, and darkness, which is the absence of sunshine, are not different from the sun, for without the existence of the sun such differentiations cannot exist. There may be varied nomenclature because of different conditions, but 
they are all the sun. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4486105 P}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ur\'e4\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  therefore say:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 eka-de\'e7a-sthitasy\'e4gner\line jyotsn\'e4 vist\'e4ri\'eb\'e9 yath\'e4\line 
parasya brahma\'eba\'f9 \'e7aktis\line tathedam akhila\'e0 jagat
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Just as the illumination of a fire, which is situated in one place, is spread all over, the energies of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid352899 Parabrahman}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 , are spread all over this universe." (}{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vi\'f1\'ebu Pur\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  1.22.53) Materially, we can directly perceive the sunshine spreading itself according to different names and activities, but ultimately the sun is one. Similarly, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 everything is an expansion of the Supreme Brahman. Therefore, the Supreme Lord is everything, and He is one without differentiation. There is no existence separate from the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.12.9
