As described in this chapter, because Aditi, the mother of the demigods, was very afflicted, her husband, Ka\'e7yapa Muni, told her how to observe vows in austerities for the benefit of her sons.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 
Since the demigods were not visible in the heavenly kingdom, their mother, Aditi, because of separation from them, was very much aggrieved. One day after many, many years, the great sage Ka\'e7yapa emerged from a trance of meditation and returned to his }
{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama.}{\insrsid4605116  He saw that the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama}{\insrsid4605116  was no longer beautiful and that his wife was very morose. Everywhere in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama,}{
\insrsid4605116  he saw signs of lamentation. The great sage therefore inquired from his wife about the well-being of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama}{\insrsid4605116  and asked her why she looked so morose. After Aditi informed Ka\'e7
yapa Muni about the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4\'e7rama's}{\insrsid4605116  well-being, she told him that she was lamenting for the absence of her sons. She then requested him to tell her how her sons could return and reoccupy their positions. Sh
e wanted all good fortune for her sons. Moved by Aditi's request, Ka\'e7
yapa Muni instructed her in the philosophy of self-realization, the difference between matter and spirit, and how to be unaffected by material loss. But when he saw that Aditi was not sat
isfied even after he had given these instructions, he advised her to worship V\'e4sudeva, Jan\'e4rdana. He assured her that only Lord V\'e4sudeva could satisfy her and fulfill all her desires. When Aditi then expressed her desire to worship Lord V\'e4
sudeva, Praj\'e4pati Ka\'e7yapa told her about a process of worship known as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 payo-vrata,}{\insrsid4605116  which is executed in twelve days. Lord Brahm\'e4 had instructed him how to satisfy Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a by this process, and thus he advised his wife to observe this vow and its regulative principles.
