\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 puru\'f1am}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the Supreme Person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bhagavantam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jan\'e4rdanam}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash who can kill all the enemies; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sarva-bh\'fcta-guh\'e4-v\'e4sam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash living within the core of the heart of everyone; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 v\'e4sudevam}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, who is all-pervading and is the son of Vasudeva; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jagat-gurum}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the spiritual master and teacher of the whole world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
My dear Aditi, engage in devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the master of everything, who can subdue everyone's enemies, and who sits within everyone's heart. Only that Supreme Person\emdash K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or V\'e4sudeva
\emdash can bestow all auspicious benedictions upon everyone, for He is the spiritual master of the universe.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 With these words, Ka\'e7yapa Muni tried to pacif
y his wife. Aditi made her appeal to her material husband. Of course, that is nice, but actually a material relative cannot do anything good for anyone. If anything good can be done, it is done by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4
sudeva. Therefore, Ka\'e7yapa Muni advised his wife, Aditi, to begin worshiping Lord V\'e4sudeva, who is situated in everyone's heart. He is the friend of everyone and is known as Jan\'e4
rdana because He can kill all enemies. There are three modes of material nature\emdash goodness, passion and ignorance\emdash and above material nature, transcendental to material nature, is another existence, which is called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e7uddha-sattva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  In the material world, the mode of goodness is considered the best, but because of material contamination, even the mode of good
ness is sometimes overpowered by the modes of passion and ignorance. But when one transcends the competition between these modes and engages himself in devotional service, he rises above the three modes of material nature. In that transcendental position,
 one is situated in pure consciousness. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Sattva\'e0 vi\'e7uddha\'e0 vasudeva-\'e7abditam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 4.3.23). Above material nature is the position called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vasudeva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or freedom from material contamination. Only in that position can one perceive the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4
sudeva. Thus the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vasudeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  condition fulfills a spiritual necessity. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 V\'e4sudeva\'f9 sarvam iti sa mah\'e4tm\'e4 sudurlabha\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 When one realizes V\'e4sudeva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he becomes most exalted.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Param\'e4tm\'e4 (V\'e4sudeva) is situated in everyone's heart, as confirmed in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  The Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 satata-yukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam\line 
dad\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 ta\'e0\line yena m\'e4m upay\'e4nti te
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"To those who are constantly devoted and who worship Me with love, I give the understanding by which they can come to Me." (Bg. 10.10)
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati

\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "The Supreme Lord is situated in everyone's heart, O Arjuna." (Bg. 18.61)
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhokt\'e4ra\'e0 yaj\'efa-tapas\'e4\'e0\line sarva-loka-mahe\'e7varam\line suh\'e5da\'e0
 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4tv\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 \'e7\'e4ntim \'e5cchati
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "The sages, know
ing Me as the ultimate purpose of all sacrifices and austerities, the Supreme Lord of all planets and demigods and the benefactor and well-wisher of all living entities, attains peace from the pangs of material miseries." (Bg. 5.29)
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Whenever one is perplexed, let him take shelter of the lotus feet of V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1
\'eba, who will give the devotee intelligence to help him surpass all difficulties and return home, back to Godhead. Ka\'e7yapa Muni advised his wife to seek shelter at the lotus feet of V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba,
 so that all her problems would be very easily solved. Thus Ka\'e7yapa Muni was an ideal spiritual master. He was not so foolish that he would present himself as an exalted personality, as good as God. He was actually a bona fide }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  because he advised his wife to seek shelter at the lotus feet of V\'e4sudeva. One who trains his subordinate or disciple to worship V\'e4
sudeva is the truly bona fide spiritual master. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagad-gurum}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is very important in this regard. Ka\'e7yapa Muni did not falsely declare himself to be }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagad-guru,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  although he actually was }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 jagad-guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  because he advocated the cause of V\'e4sudeva. Actually, V\'e4sudeva is }{
