entities from the path of self-realization. Anyone who is in this material world is extremely anxious to get more and more things for sense gratification. Actually, however, the purpose of life is not sense gratification but self-realization. Therefore, t
hose who are too addicted to sense gratification are advised to practice the mystic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  system, or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 a\'f1\'f6\'e4\'ecga-yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 system, consisting of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yama, niyama, \'e4sana, pr\'e4\'eb\'e4y\'e4ma, praty\'e4h\'e4ra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and so on. In this way, one can control the senses. The purpose of controlling 
the senses is to stop one's implication in the cycle of birth and death. As stated by \'c5\'f1abhadeva:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 n\'fcna\'e0 pramatta\'f9 kurute vikarma\line yad indriya-pr\'e9taya \'e4p\'e5\'eboti
\line na s\'e4dhu manye yata \'e4tmano 'yam\line asann api kle\'e7ada \'e4sa deha\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "When a person considers sense gratific
ation the aim of life, he certainly becomes mad after materialistic living and engages in all kinds of sinful activity. He does not know that due to his past misdeeds he has already received a body which, although temporary, is the cause of his misery. Ac
t
ually the living entity should not have taken on a material body, but he has been awarded the material body for sense gratification. Therefore I think it not befitting an intelligent man to involve himself again in the activities of sense gratification, b
y which he perpetually gets material bodies one after another." (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  5.5.4)}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid2650715  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Thus according to \'c5\'f1
abhadeva the human beings in this material world are just like madmen engaged in activities which they should not perform but which they do perform only for se
nse gratification. Such activities are not good because in this way one creates another body for his next life, as punishment for his nefarious activities. And as soon as he gets another material body, he is put into repeated suffering in material existen
ce. Therefore the Vedic culture or brahminical culture teaches one how to be satisfied with possessing the minimum necessities in life.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 To teach this highest culture, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 var\'eb\'e4\'e7
rama-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is recommended. The aim of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  divisions\emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya, \'e7\'fc
dra, brahmacarya, g\'e5hastha, v\'e4naprastha}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sanny\'e4sa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \emdash is to train one to control the senses and be content with the bare necessities. Here Lord V\'e4
manadeva, as an ideal }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  refuses Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's offer to give Him anything He might want. H
e says that without contentment one could not be happy even if he possessed the property of the entire world or the entire universe. In human society, therefore, the brahminical culture, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'f1atriya}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  culture and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vai\'e7ya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  culture must be maintained, and people mu
st be taught how to be satisfied with only what they need. In modern civilization there is no such education; everyone tries to possess more and more, and everyone is dissatisfied and unhappy. The K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is therefore establishing various farms, especially in America, to show how to be happy and content with minimum necessities of life and to save time for self-realization, which one can very easily achieve by chanting the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mah\'e4-mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare.
