\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 The utterance of the word o\'e0 signi
fies separation from one's monetary assets. In other words, by uttering this word one becomes free from attachment to money because his money is taken away from him. To be without money is not very satisfactory, for in that position one cannot fulfill one
's desires. In other words, by using the word }{\fs28\insrsid16080458 "}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 o\'e0}{\fs28\insrsid16080458 "}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 
 one becomes poverty-stricken. Especially when one gives charity to a poor man or beggar, one remains unfulfilled in self-realization and in sense gratification.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali wanted to give everything to V\'e4
manadeva, who had appeared as a beggar, but \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, being Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali's familial spiritual master in the line of seminal succession, could not appreciate Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Bali's promise. \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4
rya gave Vedic evidence that one should not give everyth
ing to a poor man. Rather, when a poor man comes for charity one should untruthfully say, "Whatever I have I have given you. I have no more." It is not that one should give everything to him. Actually the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is meant for }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 o\'e0 tat sat,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the Absolute Truth. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 O\'e0k\'e4ra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 is meant for freedom from all attachment to money because money should be spent for the purpose of the Supreme. The tendency of modern civilization is to give money in charity to the poor. Such charity has no spiritual value because we actually se
e that although there are so many hospitals and other foundations and institutions for the poor, according to the three modes of material nature a class of poor men is always destined to continue. Even though there are so many charitable institutions, pov
erty has not been driven from human society. Therefore it is recommended here, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhik\'f1ave sarvam o\'e0 kurvan n\'e4la\'e0 k\'e4mena c\'e4tmane.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 One should not give everything to the beggars among the poor.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 The best solution is that of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement. This 
movement is always kind to the poor, not only because it feeds them but also because it gives them enlightenment by teaching them how to become K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious. We are therefore opening hundreds and thousands of centers for those who are poor, both in money and in knowledge, to enlighten them in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness and reform their character by teaching them how to avoid illicit sex, intoxication, meat-eating and gambling, which are the most sinful activities and which cause people to suffer, life after lif
e. The best way to use money is to open such a center, where all may come live and reform their character. They may live very comfortably, without denial of any of the body's necessities, but they live under spiritual control, and thus they live happily a
nd save time for advancement in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. If one has money, it should not be squandered away on nothing. It should be used to push forward the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement so that all of human society will become happy, prosperous and hopeful of being promoted back home, back to Godhead. The Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  in this regard reads as follows:

