\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7604001 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 The summary of this Twentieth Chapter is as follows. Despite his knowledge that Lord V\'e4
manadeva was cheating him, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja gave everything to the Lord in charity, and thus the Lord extended His body and assumed a gigantic form as Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 After hearing the instructive advice of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja became c
ontemplative. Because it is the duty of a householder to maintain the principles of religion, economic development and sense gratification, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja thought it improper to withdraw his promise to the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 brahmac\'e4r\'e9.
}{\insrsid4605116  To lie or fail to honor a promise given to a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\insrsid4605116 
 is never proper, for lying is the most sinful activity. Everyone should be afraid of the sinful reactions to lying, for mother earth cannot even bear the weight of a sinful liar. The spreading of a kingdom or empire is temporary; if there 
is no benefit for the general public, such expansion has no value. Previously, all the great kings and emperors expanded their kingdoms with a regard for the welfare of the people in general. Indeed, while engaged in such activities for the benefit of the
 
general public, eminent men sometimes even sacrificed their lives. It is said that one who is glorious in his activities is always living and never dies. Therefore, fame should be the aim of life, and even if one becomes poverty-stricken for the sake of a
 good reputation, that is not a loss. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja thought that even if this }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{\insrsid4605116  V\'e4manadeva, were Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, if the Lord accepted his charity and then again arrested him, Bali Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja would not envy Him. Considering all these points, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja finally gave in charity everything he possessed.
\par Lord V\'e4manadeva then immediately extended Himself into a universal body. By the mercy of Lord V\'e4manadeva, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja could see that the Lord is all-pervading and that everything rests in His body. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja could see Lord V\'e4
manadeva as the supreme Vi\'f1\'ebu, wearing a helmet, yellow garments, the mark of \'c7r\'e9vatsa, the Kaustubha jewel, a flower garland, and ornaments decorating His entire body. The Lord gradually covered the entire surface of the world, a
nd by extending His body He covered the entire sky. With His hands He covered all directions, and with His second footstep He covered the entire upper planetary system. Therefore there was no vacant place where He could take His third footstep.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.20.1
