rya stressed that one's material means of livelihood and one's material reputation, sense gratification and e
conomic development must continue properly. To see to this is the first duty of a man who is a householder, especially one who is interested in material affairs. If a religious principle does not affect one's material condition, it is to be accepted. At t
he present time, in this age of Kali, this idea is extremely prominent. No one is prepared to accept any religious principle if it hampers material prosperity. \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4
rya, being a person of this material world, did not know the principles of a devotee. A de
votee is determined to serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead to His full satisfaction. Anything that hampers such determination should certainly be rejected. This is the principle of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 bhakti.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c4nuk\'fclyasya sa\'eckalpa\'f9 pr\'e4tik\'fclyasya varjanam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (}{\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Cc. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Madhya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 22.100). To perform devotional service, one must accept only that which is favorable and reject that which is unfavorable. Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja had the opportunity to contribute everything he possessed to the lotus feet of Lord V\'e4manadeva, but \'c7ukr
\'e4c\'e4rya was putting forward a material argument to hamper this process of devotional service. Under the circumstances, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja decided that such hindrances should certainly be avoided. In other words, he decided immediately to reject the advice of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya and go on with his duty. Thus he gave all his possessions to Lord V\'e4manadeva.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.20.3
