 Actually, however, their philosophy is not correct. Here, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was the seer of the Personality of Godhead's universal body, and that body was that which was seen. Thus there is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 dvaita-v\'e4da;}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  there are always two entities\emdash 
the seer and the seen. The seer is a part of the whole, but he is not equal to the whole. The part of the whole, the seer, is also one with the whole, but since he is but a part, he cannot be the complete whole at any time. This }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 acintya-bhed\'e4bheda}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \emdash simultaneous oneness and difference\emdash is the perfect philosophy propounded by Lord \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu.
