\'f1ar\'e4ja, J\'e4mbav\'e4n, played his bugle to vibrate the glories of the Lord. When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was deprived of all his possessions, the demons were very angry. Although Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja warned them not to do so, they took up weapons against Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. All of them were defeated, however, by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's eternal associates, and, in accordance with Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's order, they all entered the lower planets of the universe. Understanding Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's purpose, Garu\'f2a, the carrier of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, immediately arrested Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja with the ropes of Varu\'eba. When Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja was thus reduced to a helpless position, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu asked him for the third step of land. Because Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu appreciated Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's determination and integrity, when Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was unable to fulfill his promise, Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu ascertained that the place for him would be the planet Sutala, which is better than the planets of heaven.
