ja also considered how great personalities give up their family relationships and material possessions to satisfy the Supreme Personality of G
odhead. Indeed, they sometimes even sacrifice their lives for the satisfaction of the Lord, just to become His personal servants. Accordingly, by following in the footsteps of previous }{\cs1998\i\insrsid4605116 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\insrsid4605116 
 and devotees, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja perceived himself successful.
\par While Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, having been arrested by the ropes of Varu\'eba, was offering prayers to the Lord, his grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja appeared there and described how the Supreme Personality of Godhead had delivered Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja by taking his possessions in a tricky way. While Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was present, Lord Brahm\'e4 and Bali's wife, Vindhy\'e4vali, described the supremacy of the Supreme Lord. Since Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja had given everything to the Lord, they prayed for his release. The Lord then described how a nondevotee's possession of wealth is a danger whereas a devotee's opulence is a benediction from the Lord. Then, being pleased with Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, the Supreme Lord offered His disc to protect Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and promised to remain with him.
