at during his lifetime his family, society, country, body and relatives are everything. Why should one give up any one of them and take shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead? But from the behavior of great personalities like Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja we understand that surrendering to the Lord is the right action for an intelligent person. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja took shelter of Vi\'f1\'ebu against the will of his father. Similarly, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja took shelter of V\'e4manadeva against the will of his spiritual master, \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, and all the leading demons. People may be surprised that devotees like Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja could seek shelter of the side of the enemy, giving up the natural affinity for family, hearth and home. In this connection, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja explains that the body, which is the center of all material activities, is also a foreign element. Even though we want to keep the body fit and helpful to our activities, the body cannot continue eternally. Although I am the soul, which is 
eternal, after using the body for some time I have to accept another body (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tath\'e4 deh\'e4ntara-pr\'e4pti\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
), according to the laws of nature, unless I render some service with the body for advancement in devotional service. One should not use the body for any othe
r purpose. One must know that if he uses the body for any other purpose he is simply wasting time, for as soon as the time is ripe, the soul will automatically leave the body.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 We are very interested in society, friendship and love, but what are they? Those
 in the garb of friends and relatives merely plunder the hard-earned money of the bewildered soul. Everyone is affectionate toward his wife and is attached to her, but what is this wife? The wife is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 str\'e9,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  which means, "one who expands the material condition." If a person lives without a wife, his material conditions are less extensive. As soon as one marries and is connected with a wife, his material necessities increase.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 pu\'e0sa\'f9 striy\'e4 mithun\'e9-bh\'e4vam eta\'e0\line tayor mitho h\'e5daya-granthim 
\'e4hu\'f9\line ato g\'e5ha-k\'f1etra-sut\'e4pta-vittair\line janasya moho 'yam aha\'e0 mameti
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"The attraction between male and female is the basic principle of material existence. On the basis of this misconception, which ties together the hearts of the male and female, one becomes attracted to his 
body, home, property, children, relatives and wealth. In this way one increases life's illusions and thinks in terms of 'I and mine.' " (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1837309\charrsid1837309 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 5.5.8) Human life is meant for self-realization, not for increasing unwanted things. Actually, a wife increases u
nwanted things. One's lifetime, one's home and everything one has, if not properly used in the service of the Lord, are all sources of material conditions of perpetual suffering under the threefold miseries (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 adhy\'e4
tmika, adhibhautika}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 adhidaivika}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). Unfor
tunately, there is no institution in human society for education on this subject. People are kept in darkness about the goal of life, and thus there is a continuous struggle for existence. We speak of "survival of the fittest," but no one survives, for no
 one is free under material conditions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.22.10
