 arrest of her husband and accused him of having no intelligence because he had claimed proprietorship of the property of the Lord. Such a claim is a sign of demoniac life. Although the demigods, who are officials appointed by the Lord for management, are
 
attached to materialistic enjoyment, they never claim to be proprietors of the universe, for they know that the actual proprietor of everything is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is the qualification of the demigods. But the demons, instead of ac
c
epting the exclusive proprietorship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, claim the property of the universe for themselves through demarcations of nationalism. "This part is mine, and that part is yours," they say. "This part I can give in charity, and 
this part I can keep for my enjoyment." These are all demoniac conceptions. This is described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (16.13): }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 idam adya may\'e4 labdham ima
\'e0 pr\'e4psye manoratham.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  "Thus far I have acquired so much money and land. Now I have to add more and more. In thi
s way I shall be the greatest proprietor of everything. Who can compete with me?" These are all demoniac conceptions.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's wife accused Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
