\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7604001 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 This chapter describes how Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, along with his grandfather Prahl\'e4da Mah
\'e4r\'e4ja, entered the planet Sutala and how the Supreme Personality of Godhead allowed Indra to reenter the heavenly planet.
\par }\pard \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid4605116 The great soul Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja experienced that the highest gain in life is to attain devotional service under the shelter of the Lord's lotus feet in full surrender.
 Being fixed in this conclusion, his heart full of ecstatic devotion and his eyes full of tears, he offered obeisances to the Personality of Godhead and then, with his associates, entered the planet known as Sutala. Thus the Supreme Personality of Godhead
 satisfied the desire of Aditi and reinstalled Lord Indra. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, being aware of Bali's release from arrest, then described the transcendental pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in this material world. Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r
\'e4ja praised the Supreme Lord for creating the material world, for being equal to everyone and for being extremely liberal to the devotees, just like a desire tree. Indeed, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja said that the Lord is kind not only to His devotees but also to the demons. In this
 way he described the unlimited causeless mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Then, with folded hands, he offered his respectful obeisances unto the Lord, and after circumambulating the Lord he also entered the planet Sutala in accordance with th
e Lord's order. The Lord then ordered \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya to describe Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja's faults and discrepancies in executing the sacrificial ceremony. \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4
rya became free from fruitive actions by chanting the holy name of the Lord, and he explained how chanting can diminish all the faults of the conditioned soul. He then completed Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja's sacrificial ceremony. All the great saintly persons accepted Lord V\'e4manadeva as the benefactor of Lord Indra because He had returned Indra to his heavenly planet. They acc
epted the Supreme Personality of Godhead as the maintainer of all the affairs of the universe. Being very happy, Indra, along with his associates, placed V\'e4
manadeva before him and reentered the heavenly planet in their airplane. Having seen the wonderful activities of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu in the sacrificial arena of Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, all the demigods, saintly persons, Pit\'e4s, Bh\'fc
tas and Siddhas glorified the Lord again and again. The chapter concludes by saying that the most auspicious function of the conditioned soul is to chant and hear about the glorious activities of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.23.1
