es made of material energy. Thus the demigods living in the upper planetary systems and the living entities living in the lower planetary system are of the same nature. Nonetheless, those living as human beings on this planet are sometimes attracted to wo
rshiping the demigods in the higher planetary systems. Such worship is temporary. As the human beings on this planet have to change their bodies (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tath\'e4 deh\'e4ntara-pr\'e4pti\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
), the living entities known as Indra, Candra, Varu\'eba and so on will also have to change their bodies in due course of time. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 antavat tu phala\'e0 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "Men of small intelligence worship the demigods, and their fruits are limited and temporary." }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 K\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9 prapadyante 'nya-devat\'e4\'f9: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
those who do not know the position of the demigods are inclined to worship the demigods for some material purpose, but the results of such worship are never permanent. Consequently, here it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 yathetare\'f1\'e4
\'e0 p\'e5thag-\'e4tman\'e4\'e0 sat\'e4m, padopasarpa\'eba\'e0 m\'e5\'f1\'e4 bhavet.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 In other words, if one is to worship someone else, he must worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Then his worship will never be fruitless. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Svalpam apy asya dharmasya tr\'e4yate mahato bhay\'e4t:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  even a slight attempt to worship the Supreme Personality of Godhead is a permanent asset. Therefore, as recommended in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, tyaktv\'e4 sva-dharma\'e0 cara\'eb\'e4mbuja
\'e0 hare\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  One should take to the worship of the lotus feet of Hari, even if this means giving up the so-called occupational duty assig
ned because of the particular body one has accepted. Because worship in terms of the body is temporary, it does not bear any permanent fruit. But worship of the Supreme Personality of Godhead gives immense benefit.
