\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
Neither all the demigods, nor the so-called gurus nor all other people, either independently or together, can offer mercy that equals even one ten-thousandth of Yours. Therefore I wish to take shelter of Your lotus feet.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 It is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 k\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4
\'f9 prapadyante 'nya-devat\'e4\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  people in general, being motivated by material desires, worship the demigods to get fruitive results very quickly. People generally do not become devotees of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, since Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu never becomes the order-supplier of His devotee. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu does not give a devotee benedictions that will create a further demand for benedictions. By worshiping the demigods one may get results, but, as described in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 antavat tu phala\'e0 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 whatever great benedictions one may achieve from the demigods are all temporary
. Because the demigods themselves are temporary, their benedictions are also temporary and have no permanent value. Those who aspire for such benedictions have a poor fund of knowledge (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). The benedictions of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu are different. By the mercy of the Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, one can be completely freed from material contamination and go back home, back to Godhead. Therefore the benedictions offered by the demigods cannot compare to even one ten-thousandth of the Lord's benedictions. One shou
ld not, therefore, try to obtain benedictions from the demigods or false }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 gurus.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  One should aspire only for the benediction offered by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As the Lord says in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (18.66):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya\line m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja\line aha\'e0 tv
\'e4\'e0 sarva-p\'e4pebhyo\line mok\'f1ayi\'f1y\'e4mi m\'e4 \'e7uca\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
"Abandon all varieties of religion and just surrender unto Me. I shall deliver you from all sinful reaction. Do not fear." This is the greatest benediction.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.24.50
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 TEXT 50
