\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb120\sa60\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 acak\'f1u\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
one who does not have his power of sight; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 andhasya}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash for such a blind person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 agra\'eb
\'e9\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the leader, who goes first; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 k\'e5ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash accepted; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash similarly; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 janasya}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash such a person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 avidu\'f1a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash who has no knowledge of the goal of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 abudha\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash a foolish rascal; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 guru\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the spiritual master; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tvam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash Your Lordship; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 
arka-d\'e5k}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash appear like the sun; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sarva-d\'e5\'e7\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash of all sources of knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sam\'e9k\'f1a\'eba\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 
\emdash the complete seer; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 v\'e5ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash accepted; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 guru\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the spiritual master; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 na\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash our; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 sva-gatim}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash one who knows his real self-interest; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 bubhutsat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash such an enlightened person.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 
As a blind man, being unable to see, accepts another blind man as his leader, people who do not know the goal of life accept someone as a guru who is a rascal and a fool. But
 we are interested in self-realization. Therefore we accept You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as our spiritual master, for You are able to see in all directions and are omniscient like the sun.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 The conditioned soul, being wrapped in ignoranc
e and therefore not knowing the goal of life, accepts a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  who can juggle words and make some display of magic that is wonderful to a fool. Sometimes a foolish person accepts someone as a }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  because he can manufacture a small quantity of gold by mystic
 yogic power. Because such a disciple has a poor fund of knowledge, he cannot judge whether the manufacture of gold is the criterion for a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 Why should one not accept the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, from whom unlimited numbers of gold mines come into being? }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhavo matta\'f9 sarva\'e0 pravartate.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  All the gold mines are created by the energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, why should one accept a magician who can manufacture only a small portion of gold? Such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 gurus}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  are accepted by those who are blind, not knowing the goal of life. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Satyavrata, however, knew the goal of life. He knew the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore he accepted the Lord as his }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Either the Supreme Lord or His representative can become }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  The Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e4
m eva ye prapadyante m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 "One can get relief from the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e4y\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 as soon as he surrenders unto Me." Therefore it is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru's}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  business to instruct his disciple to surrender 
to the Supreme Personality of Godhead if he wants relief from the material clutches. This is the symptom of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  This same principle was instructed by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu: }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 y\'e4re dekha, t\'e4re kaha 'k\'e5\'f1\'eba'-upade\'e7a.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  In other words, one is advised not to accept a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 who does not follow the path of instruction given by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.24.51
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 TEXT 51
