\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\insrsid4605116  (an ordinary person); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 janasya}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash of an ordinary person who does not know the goal of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 \'e4di\'e7ate}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash instructs; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 asat\'e9m}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash impermanent, material; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 gatim}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash the goal of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 
yay\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash by such knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 prapadyeta}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash he surrenders; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 duratyayam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash insurmountable; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash to ignorance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tvam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash Your Lordship; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 tu}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash but; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 avyayam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash indestructible; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 j\'ef\'e4nam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 amogham}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
without material contamination; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 a\'efjas\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash very soon; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 prapadyate}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash achieves; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 yena}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash by such knowledge; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 jana\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash a person; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 nijam}{\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash his own; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid4605116 padam}{
\fs28\insrsid4605116 \emdash original position.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 A materialistic so-called guru instructs his materialistic dis
ciples about economic development and sense gratification, and because of such instructions the foolish disciples continue in the materialistic existence of ignorance. But Your Lordship gives knowledge that is eternal, and the intelligent person receiving
 such knowledge is quickly situated in his original constitutional position.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid4605116 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi340\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 So-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 gurus}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 instruct their disciples for the sake of material profit. Some }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  advises that one meditate in such a way that his intelligence will increase in regard to
 keeping his body fit for sense gratification. Another }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 advises that sex is the ultimate goal of life and that one should therefore engage in sex to the best of his ability. These are the instructions of foolish }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 gurus.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 In other words, because of the instructions of a foolish }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 one remains perpetually in material existence and suffers its tribulations. But if one is intelligent enough to take instructions from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as enunciated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or the S\'e4\'eckhya philosophy of Kapiladeva, one can very soon attain liberation and be situated in his original position of spiritual life. The words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 nija\'e0 padam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  are significant. The living entity, being part and parcel of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, has the birthright to a position in Vaiku\'eb\'f6
haloka, or the spiritual world, where there is no anxiety. Therefore, one should follow the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Then, as stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
after giving up one's body, one will return home, back to Godhead. The Lord lives in the spiritual world in His original personality, and a devotee who follows the instructions of the Lord approaches Him (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 m\'e4m eti}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). As a spiritual person, such a devotee returns to the Personality of Godhead and plays and dances with Him. That is the ultimate goal of life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 SB 8.24.52
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid4605116 TEXT 52
