Sometimes it is argued that people do not know who is a spiritual master and that finding a spiritual master from whom to get enlightenment in regard to the destination of life is very difficult. To answer all these questions, King Satyavrata sh
ows us the way to accept the Supreme Personality of Godhead as the real spiritual master. The Supreme Lord has given full directions in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 about how to deal with everything in this material world and how to return home, back to Godhead. Therefore, one should not be misled by so-called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 gurus}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 who are rascals and fools. Rather, one should directly see the Supreme Personality of Godhead as the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  or instructor. It is difficult, however, to understand }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  without the help of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Therefore the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 appears in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 parampar\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  system. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (4.34) the Supreme Personality of Godhead recommends:
