 brahma para\'e0 dh\'e4ma pavitra\'e0 parama\'e0 bhav\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ). Similarly, following in the footsteps of \'c7r\'e9 Arjuna, who is a personal devotee of the Lord, one should accept the supremacy of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, as supported by Vy\'e4sa, Devala, Asita, N\'e4rada and later by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'e4c\'e4ryas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  R\'e4m\'e4nuj\'e4c\'e4rya, M}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid15668177 adhv\'e4c\'e4rya, Nimb\'e4rka and Vi\'f1\'ebus}{
