u. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's purpose was to take back all the Vedic literatures from the demon Hayagr\'e9va and restore them to Lord Brahm\'e4. Incidentally, by His causeless mercy, the Lord spoke with Satyavrata. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
satyavrat\'e4n\'e4m}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  is significant because it indicates that those on the level of Satyavrata can take knowledge from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 delivered by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Whatever is spoken by the Supreme Lord is accepted as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Veda.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 ved\'e4nta-k\'e5d veda-vit:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the compiler of all Vedic knowledge, and He knows the purport of the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  Therefore, anyone who takes knowledge from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 as it is, knows the purpose of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
). One cannot understand Vedic knowledge from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 veda-v\'e4da-rat\'e4s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  who read the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 
 and misconstrue their subject matter. One has to know the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  from the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Eighth Canto, Twenty-fourth Chapter, of the }{
\cs2344\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid4605116  entitled "Matsya, the Lord's Fish Incarnation."
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid4605116 \emdash 
